2026-08-28 00:01:03 | INFO     | p2p_knowledge_hub.chunking.recursive_chunker:chunk:54 | Following chunks were produced. [DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('000191c2-a362-49df-b7ab-192a6232c6fe'), chunk_index=1, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418012, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='---\nid: 10_Final_Notes\naliases: []\ntags: []\n---', page_no=None, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('50745502-d3c6-4e75-931b-6a0c0a9d39ec'), chunk_index=2, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418036, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='<!-- toc -->\n\n- [Transformer Full Architecture](#transformer-full-architecture)\n    * [Encoder](#encoder)\n        + [***Input Layer***](#input-layer)\n        + [***Multi-Head Attention***](#multi-head-attention)\n        + [***FIRST ADD & NORM (after attention)***](#first-add--norm-after-attention)\n        + [***FEED‑FORWARD NETWORK (FFN)***](#feed%E2%80%91forward-network-ffn)\n        + [***Then SECOND ADD & NORM — but you asked up to FFN output)***](#then-second-add--norm--but-you-asked-up-to-ffn-output)\n- [What Problems Can You Solve?](#what-problems-can-you-solve)\n\n<!-- tocstop -->', page_no=None, section=None, title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fba4e713-26a0-4dd0-8d71-e4f590777e10'), chunk_index=3, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418350, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='### Encoder\n\n#### ***Input Layer***\n\n**Token Embedding**\n  - *Notation :-* X (shape: [seq_len, d_model])\n  - *What :-* Converts each token in to a dense vector(non-zero. all carries a specific piece of information.) \n  - *Why :-* Neural networks need continuous vectors, not discrete IDs.\n  - *How :-* Learnable lookup table (vocab_size × d_model) *nn.embedding*.\n  - ***How Learnable Lookup or nn.Embedding***', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0f77be44-265b-479c-ae91-1c9c351df5bd'), chunk_index=4, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418356, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='**Positional Encoding**\n- *Notation :-* PE (same shape as X)\n- *What :-* Adds information about position (order) of tokens.\n- *Why :-* Self‑attention is permutation‑invariant; without position info, “hello world” = “world hello”. *Bi-Directional*', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('63a1ee3c-6ef1-4521-b690-910c699b6284'), chunk_index=5, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418361, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="- *How :-* Sinusodial functions or learnable embeddings, added elementwise x' = x + PE. Using sin and cos in every alternate dimension. Sine is applied to even-indexed dimensions, cosine to odd-indexed dimensions of the PE vector.\n\n**Embedding + Positional Encoding: Without positional encoding, “I love you” = “you love I” to the model.**", page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c1a5ea18-f6ac-4a93-bce0-89999059b805'), chunk_index=6, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418365, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="`#### ***Multi-Head Attention***\n- **Linear Projections to QKV**\n- *Notation :-* Q = X'·W_Q,  K = X'·W_K,  V = X'·W_V\n- *Shape :-* W_Q, W_K, W_V are [d_model, d_k]; d_k = d_model / num_heads.\n- *What :-* Create three different representations from the same input\n- *Why :-* Query (what to look for), Key (what can be attended), Value (what to extract)", page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8c382b96-760b-4230-ae04-4bc0062b6786'), chunk_index=7, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418369, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='- *Note :-* Each head has its own W_Q, W_K, W_V.', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('97cd10cf-bde6-49e8-96b6-da5575990aee'), chunk_index=8, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418373, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='- **Split into heads**\n- *Notation :-* Q → [num_heads, seq_len, d_k] (and same for K, V)\n- *What :-* Reshape and transpose to process heads in parallel.\n- *Why :-* Different heads can attend to different relationships (e.g., syntax, coreference).\n- **Scaled Dot‑Product Attention per head**\n- **Scores :- ** S = (Q·Kᵀ) / √d_k\n- *What :-*  Dot product between every query and every key.', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('941cdafc-52e5-44f1-a1ab-1fa938337cbb'), chunk_index=9, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418378, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='- *Why :-* Measures similarity (attention weight).\n- *√d_k:-* Scales down to prevent large dot products pushing softmax into saturated region. If we have [10, 1] than it represents [0.99, 0.01] after softmax. After scaling the same will be [0.73, 0.27].', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('817eb904-0af1-48c3-a6eb-a4939131f34c'), chunk_index=10, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418382, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='- *Padding Mask:-* Sentences are padded with 0 to match sequence length. Before softmax, PAD positions in the attention score matrix are set to −∞ so they become ~0 after softmax and contribute nothing to the output.\n- **Weights :- ** A = softmax(S)   (applied row‑wise)\n- *What :-* Normalised attention probabilities over keys for each query.', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('909e5657-7448-4816-8e11-88fa8bfe9530'), chunk_index=11, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418389, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='- *Why :-* To convert raw dot‑product scores (which can be any real number) into a probability distribution\n- **Output :- ** head_out = A · V\n- *What :-* Weighted sum of values.\n- *Why :-* Attend to relevant positions and aggregate their information.\n- **Concatenate heads**\n- *Notation :-* concat = [head₁_out, head₂_out, ..., head_h_out]\n- *Shape :-*  [seq_len, d_model] (since h * d_k = d_model)', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e3b947d7-aefe-4c51-83bf-5fbf4111b3c3'), chunk_index=12, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418393, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='- **Output projection**\n- *Notation :-* attn_out = concat · W_O\n- *Shape :-*  W_O is [d_model, d_model]\n- *What :-* Linear transformation after concatenation.\n- *Why :-* Mix information from different heads and project back to d_model.\n\n**Multi‑head attention: Single‑head attention is a special case; multiple heads capture different linguistic patterns.**\n**Scaling by √d_k: Prevents dot products from becoming too large, which would push softmax into extremely small gradients.**', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cf897969-35de-4b3c-9dbc-6f77fd84df9b'), chunk_index=13, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418397, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="#### ***FIRST ADD & NORM (after attention)***\n- **Residual connection**\n- Tiny gradient = tiny slope = optimizer takes microscopic steps = no convergence\nResidual = guarantees a minimum gradient of 1 = slope stays meaningful = learning continues\n- *Notation :-* attn_res = X' + attn_out\n- *What :-* Add the original input (from step 1) to the attention output.", page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1f99f118-4c5b-4788-88be-d364f867633c'), chunk_index=14, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418401, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='- *Why :-* Helps gradients flow through many layers (differnet encoders. We have 6 in original paper); mitigates vanishing gradient. So during backprop, the gradient has to travel backward through: FFN → Add&Norm → MHA → Add&Norm → FFN → Add&Norm → MHA → ... repeated N times', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a4634e0c-61b4-481b-ae9e-f6c4deee7427'), chunk_index=15, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418405, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Each operation multiplies the gradient by some value less than 1, and after 6 blocks that's a lot of sequential multiplication — the signal degrades.", page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d18081d0-9f4a-49f9-9c3e-bd1876aafbc5'), chunk_index=16, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418409, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='- **Layer Normalization**\n      - *Notation :-* norm1 = LayerNorm(attn_res)\n      - *What :-* Normalises across feature dimension (d_model) to mean 0, variance 1, then scales/shifts. This comes all data points around mean where mean is 0 after normalization. It helps smooth gradients and faster convergence\n      - *Why :-* Stabilises training, allows higher learning rates.\n\n**Residual connections: Essential for training deep networks (>10 layers). Without them, training collapses.**', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ec1ed05c-e9c9-4b24-af3a-199bca0332dd'), chunk_index=17, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418413, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='**Layer Normalization: Faster convergence than batch norm for sequences; works per sample, not per batch.**\n\n#### ***FEED‑FORWARD NETWORK (FFN)***', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ebdc803e-3897-4141-b125-16fc1cd73e73'), chunk_index=18, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418417, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="This framing slightly undersells attention. Both attention and FFN learn representations — they just do different things. A more accurate framing: attention decides which information to mix across tokens; FFN applies nonlinear transformation to each token's mixed representation independently. Geva et al. (2021) — which is in your references — showed FFN layers act as key-value memory, where the first layer detects patterns and the second retrieves associated content", page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1785630c-0ed4-42f2-b341-2553810b13a6'), chunk_index=19, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418423, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="That's interview-level depth.\n\n- **First Linear Layer (expansion)**\n- *Notation :-* hidden = ReLU(norm1·W₁ + b₁)\n- *Shape :-*  W₁: [d_model, d_ff] (d_ff usually 4×d_model), b₁: [d_ff]\n- *What :-* Project to higher dimension. Adding non-Linearity.", page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3cd8831f-cda0-4f04-98c5-af5ecb861650'), chunk_index=20, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418427, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='- *Why :-* without the FFN, the model has no position-wise nonlinearity — attention can only do weighted averaging of V, which limits representational power. Gives capacity to learn non‑linear features per position by adding activation ReLU / GeLU. Without expansion, FFN would be too weak.\n- *Activation :-* ReLU (or GELU) adds non‑linearity.\n- **Second Linear Layer (projection back)**\n- *Notation :- * ffn_out = hidden·W₂ + b₂', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0ace897e-e28d-4ccd-95c5-ddf84b86525c'), chunk_index=21, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418431, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='- *Shape :- *  W₂: [d_ff, d_model], b₂: [d_model]\n- *What :- * Project back to d_model.\n- *Why :- * Return to the model’s internal dimension for the next block or output.\n\n**FFN expansion (d_ff >> d_model): Gives the model “thinking capacity” after mixing information via attention. Without it, the model is just a series of linear+softmax operations.**', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6be384bc-4556-4e40-9f3e-a81d0a107f0b'), chunk_index=22, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418434, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="#### ***Then SECOND ADD & NORM — but you asked up to FFN output)***\n  - *Notation :-*  ffn_res = norm1 + ffn_out   ← norm1 here is the FFN's input, which is correct\nencoder_out = LayerNorm(ffn_res)\n  - *Note :-* Same residual + layer norm pattern repeats after FFN.\nTwo reasons:", page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('056d8218-2a28-43bf-b971-c680386d71dd'), chunk_index=23, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418438, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Second residual path – gives gradients an alternative route around the FFN, preventing the FFN from becoming a bottleneck. Without it, deep models would struggle to train.\n\nStabilise the next block’s input – after FFN, the distribution may have shifted. LayerNorm re‑centres and re‑scales so that the next encoder block (or decoder) receives well‑behaved inputs.', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('aed74bf6-9e1e-4932-99e5-b82b06a05568'), chunk_index=24, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418442, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Pattern: Every sub‑layer (attention, FFN) is wrapped with Add → LayerNorm. This is the hallmark of the Transformer architecture and is critical for training stability at scale.', page_no=None, section='Transformer Full Architecture', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b8e0a80d-abd2-4265-8893-3028e4572033'), chunk_index=25, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418503, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='***With a from-scratch Transformer***\n\n|Problem|Example|\n| --------------- | --------------- | \n|Sequence-to-sequence|Simple machine translation (e.g. English → French on a small dataset)|\n|Text summarization (toy)| Abstractive summary on short paragraphs|\n|Simple chatbot| Response generation on a small dialogue dataset|', page_no=None, section='What Problems Can You Solve?', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('59630fd1-930f-461d-ae6a-68f7a38dd648'), chunk_index=26, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418508, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Project 1 (Path A — 1 week): Build a minimal Transformer in PyTorch for English→French translation on the Multi30k dataset. Don't aim for good BLEU scores. Aim for a clean, readable implementation where you can point to every component and explain it. This becomes a strong interview talking point.", page_no=None, section='What Problems Can You Solve?', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c148b3fd-0d7e-4fe6-a396-e31d45c01f27'), chunk_index=27, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418512, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='| Problem Type               | Models                          | Example Task                                                      |\n|----------------------------|---------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Text Classification        | BERT, DistilBERT                | Sentiment, spam detection, topic labeling                         |\n| Named Entity Recognition   | BERT                            | Extract names, dates, org names from text                         |\n| Question Answering         | BERT, RoBERTa                   | "Given this paragraph, answer this question"                      |\n| Summarization              | T5, BART                        | Summarize news articles or documents                              |', page_no=None, section='What Problems Can You Solve?', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f14027fc-d2c8-425d-a7ef-719d8b72ac46'), chunk_index=28, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418515, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='| Text Generation            | GPT-2, GPT-Neo                  | Complete prompts, generate structured text                        |\n| Translation                | MarianMT, T5                    | Language pairs                                                    |\n| Semantic Search            | Sentence-BERT                   | Find similar documents, semantic similarity                       |', page_no=None, section='What Problems Can You Solve?', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('80cde32f-a079-40d8-a9d8-9fbf44960657'), chunk_index=29, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418519, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Project 2 (Path B — 2–3 weeks): Fine-tune DistilBERT for a classification task. The reason to start with DistilBERT over full BERT is purely practical — it's faster to train on Colab's free tier. Pick a task that connects to your P2P background if possible. For example: classifying financial news sentiment, or detecting clause types in loan agreement text. A generic IMDb sentiment classifier is fine too but less memorable.", page_no=None, section='What Problems Can You Solve?', title='Final Notes'), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('752daf09-5b85-472f-ac09-82b73ebed60b'), chunk_index=30, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('ca1dd95a-f496-4110-945b-4afee8ecb0df'), document_group_id=UUID('2425b352-f816-4f5b-bf85-9e5692e5e279'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 31, 3, 418523, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Project 2 is what you'd actually show in a portfolio or talk about in an interview for an Applied NLP role.", page_no=None, section='What Problems Can You Solve?', title='Final Notes')]
