2026-08-28 00:03:10 | INFO     | p2p_knowledge_hub.chunking.recursive_chunker:chunk:54 | Following chunks were produced. [DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c315509e-89b5-4bf9-a56b-099dda7ff964'), chunk_index=1, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364148, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='1\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\nGuide to the \nVendor Onboarding \nProcess', page_no=1, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6641ca24-0571-45cd-b933-3ca86effdf8f'), chunk_index=2, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364233, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='2\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\nGuide to the Vendor\nOnboarding Process\nThe first stage in a third-party risk management (TPRM) program is\nonboarding a new vendor. There’s often a sense of urgency to onboard\nthe vendor quickly, but it’s essential to proceed through the process with\ncareful planning, consideration, and collaboration between both parties.\nThis will ensure the relationship between your organization and the', page_no=2, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('01c9b038-569a-4d2c-ac8a-81ba22dbd033'), chunk_index=3, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364240, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='vendor starts off on the right path.\nThis guide provides an overview of the onboarding process, with best\npractices and considerations for each phase. The activities presented here\nare designed to be repeatable and scalable for organizations of all sizes,\nalthough keep in mind that this isn’t an all-inclusive list. Your organization\nmay have additional vendor onboarding needs that aren’t addressed in this', page_no=2, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('13a3a0bd-0508-47d2-b5a6-fce2de740427'), chunk_index=4, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364244, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='guide, so consider how the following activities can be integrated into your\nexisting processes.', page_no=2, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('00462076-b2e5-4ea8-8f3b-e82b55ef36b7'), chunk_index=5, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364271, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\nThe onboarding process will be most effective when you begin by\nplanning for the vendor engagement and assessing the vendor’s\ninherent risk and criticality. The information gathered during these\ninitial steps will help streamline the subsequent onboarding activities,\nsuch as the scope of due diligence required, and help you determine\nhow to manage the vendor relationship throughout its lifetime.\nPhase 1\nPlanning &', page_no=3, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c5f076ee-57e6-40fa-bdde-ce17b727e4fb'), chunk_index=6, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364276, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Risk Assessment', page_no=3, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('07652ddc-3a37-42c1-92a3-14b82e079da1'), chunk_index=7, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364347, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='4\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\n5 Best Practices in Planning\n1.\t Confirm the business need\nIt may seem redundant, but your organization should formally confirm the need for a\nnew vendor. You might discover that an existing vendor in your inventory can provide\nthe new product or service, in which case the onboarding process may be less extensive', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7d6e5c87-1c05-4cbc-aa58-57c7d99a9771'), chunk_index=8, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364352, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='because of the information you have already collected from the vendor.\n2.\t Identify the key players\nAssigning duties and responsibilities will help avoid unnecessary confusion and delays\nthroughout the onboarding process.', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c6b577b3-0a1b-404e-88d9-82b72527ee8d'), chunk_index=9, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364356, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='In general, the onboarding process will require the following roles:\n•\t Process owners – These are the individuals that drive and manage the onboarding\nprocess to ensure the activities are completed correctly and on time. Process owners\nwill typically be a combination of vendor or product owners and the dedicated vendor\nrisk management team.\n•\t Reviewers – Many onboarding activities will need to be reviewed for accuracy and', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('24d36b01-f7f9-4ac9-a1cd-3fa2cbfaa917'), chunk_index=10, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364360, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='compliance, which generally falls to various subject matter experts (SMEs) across\ndifferent departments. Information security, project management, procurement,\nlegal, and compliance are just some of the teams that may be responsible for\nreviewing the onboarding tasks and deliverables.\n•\t Approvers – Consider the different levels of approval needed for each onboarding\nactivity. TPRM regulations state that senior management and the board should be', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d6a0955b-be60-41ba-a420-de26f7af9593'), chunk_index=11, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364364, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='involved in critical and high-risk vendor activities, but your organization should\ndetermine the specifics of what this entails.', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6bce2375-75f9-4760-b152-e61de65a97c0'), chunk_index=12, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364428, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3.\t Establish a vendor selection process\nConsider how your organization will facilitate the vendor selection process.\nThese are just some of the details you may want to consider and document\nduring the planning phase:\n•\t Will you begin by comparing two or more requests for proposals (RFPs)?\n•\t How will you make the final decision between two vendors that are\nequally desirable?', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('80b05f07-4a11-4b28-b37b-8fc4c26985f5'), chunk_index=13, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364433, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\t If there’s a need for an alternate vendor, will you keep one or more\nchoices as backups?\n•\t Who makes the final decision or approval?\n4.\t Choose an exit strategy\nIt’s essential to consider a plan of action that your organization will take\nwhen the vendor relationship ends. An exit strategy will usually come down\nto the following options:\n•\t Replacing the vendor with an alternative', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a99ff5a5-7fef-49e3-86ea-657f0edd05b3'), chunk_index=14, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364437, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\t Bringing the outsourced activity in-house\n•\t Discontinuing the outsourced activity altogether\n•\t Combining two or more of these options\n5.\t Set expectations about timing\nOnboarding cycle times will depend on many factors, such as the vendor’s\nresponsiveness to document requests and contract negotiations. While\nsome of these details might be out of your control, it can still be helpful to', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d2f5c5df-1c10-44e7-9432-17d9bb11ac35'), chunk_index=15, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364442, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='set realistic expectations or goals about timing with the vendor and internal\nstakeholders. These expectations can help keep both parties on track, while\nalso identifying potential roadblocks that need to be addressed.\n5\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ddf82708-0f89-4003-8bd6-b58bdd23276d'), chunk_index=16, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364521, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='6\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\nVendor Risk Assessments\nAfter the onboarding process has been planned, you can move on to the risk assessment\nactivities. This is essentially the phase where you evaluate the potential vendor relationship\nby identifying the inherent risk and classifying the criticality. These activities provide the first\nimpression of the vendor relationship and help identify any hidden risks that can negatively', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e6371cf0-4455-4c4e-b470-270b5f281c32'), chunk_index=17, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364525, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='impact your organization or customers.\nVendor risks that are left unmanaged can lead to significant consequences for your organization,\nsuch as data breaches, reputational damage, and operational failures.\nInherent risk is naturally present in the vendor’s product or service. Every vendor\nengagement will involve inherent risk, so it’s essential to identify and quantify that risk\nthrough an assessment. These assessments are always done internally and are usually', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bcdf76b3-8669-49c4-ab2d-0ae550f69e48'), chunk_index=18, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364529, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='completed by your vendor owner.\nBased off the inherent risk assessment, your\norganization will assign a risk rating to the\nvendor. These risk levels are often rated on\na scale of low, moderate, or high.\n•\t Strategic – The vendor’s actions or\ndecisions don’t align with your strategic\nobjectives\n•\t Operational – The vendor doesn’t have\neffective internal processes, people,\ncontrols, or systems\n•\t Compliance – The vendor doesn’t', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3a8008e8-6b14-483f-b74c-225da6f0bf2a'), chunk_index=19, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364533, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='comply with laws, regulations, or your\norganization’s internal policies\nInherent risk assessment\nCommon risk types may include:\nHere’s a closer look at each activity:\n•\t Cyber and information security – The\nvendor has security vulnerabilities from\nmissing or ineffective controls\n•\t Financial – The vendor’s financial health\nis poor\n•\t Reputational – The vendor’s actions,\nlawsuits, poor service, outages, fraud, or\ndata breaches reflect negatively on your\norganization', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4a06cbbe-3546-4bb2-834d-b0857ab91cde'), chunk_index=20, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364563, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='7\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\nAll vendors should be classified as critical or non-critical to your\noperations. Criticality is not a risk rating, but rather identifies the\nrelationships most essential to your operations and/or customers.\n•\t The sudden loss of the vendor would create a significant disruption to your organization\n•\t The sudden loss of the vendor would disrupt your customers', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('755fa0ee-bbf7-484f-af4a-5169c692f061'), chunk_index=21, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364568, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\t If the vendor’s operations were down for more than 24 hours, this would create a\nmaterial negative impact on your organization\nCriticality classification\nA critical vendor will typically fall under one or more of the following criteria:', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('165c40b6-18a0-43df-b4e4-6188dfe2f28f'), chunk_index=22, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364621, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='8\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\n1.\t Keep a detailed inventory\nVendor risk assessments include a lot of information and documentation from both the\nSME and the vendor. The information and provided documentation should be kept in an\norganized inventory.\n2.\t Verify the vendor’s business standing and reputation\nIt’s important to validate that the vendor is a legitimate business. You should', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ff6a41e1-a9af-4a0e-96e1-d6bac1809263'), chunk_index=23, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364625, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='understand the vendor’s ownership structure, check if they’ve previously done business\nunder a different name and confirm the vendor’s location. You should also check the\nvendor’s reputation through news searches, reviews, and the Better Business Bureau.\n3.\t Ask the right questions\nUltimately, the vendor risks uncovered in the vendor risk assessment will guide the due\ndiligence process. It’s important to determine the right questions to ask the vendor to', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6a94aea9-834c-4fa8-ab8e-48ea0b4050a7'), chunk_index=24, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364629, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='better understand the vendor’s risk and how to mitigate it.\n3 Best Practices in Vendor\nRisk Assessments\nEXAMPLE:\nIf your inherent risk assessment uncovers\ncybersecurity risk because the vendor’s product\nwould be integrated with your network, you\nshould ask the vendor questions about their\nhuman resources, employee vetting and training\npractices, and information security and privacy\npolicies and practices.', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('00061cee-8a8a-4d73-b19e-70f01e401678'), chunk_index=25, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364637, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='9\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\nThe vendor’s inherent risk and criticality classification will drive your \ndue diligence efforts, meaning that critical and high-risk vendors should \nundergo the highest scrutiny. Due diligence reviews involve collecting \nand validating various types of information from the vendor, such as \nthe tax ID, credit report, financial statements, cybersecurity plans, SOC \nreports, insurance certificates, and more.  \nPhase 2 \nDue Diligence', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f55218cb-baa7-487a-9dec-2735aef33711'), chunk_index=26, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364685, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='10\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\nPre-contract due diligence is one of the most important onboarding activities, as it gives\nbetter insight into the vendor’s controls and risk management processes. Due diligence is also\nperformed periodically throughout the relationship, but this first occurrence allows you to\naddress any concerns before signing the vendor contract.\n*This is not an exhaustive due diligence list', page_no=10, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cad67223-57d1-4d94-bdbb-576908ad1033'), chunk_index=27, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364689, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Here are some examples of what to consider\ncollecting for each risk type:\nLow-risk vendors\nCollect baseline\ndocuments, like business\nlicense, tax ID, credit\nreport, Dun & Bradstreet\nreport, OFAC checks, and\nnegative news search\nfindings.\nModerate-risk vendors\nCollect all baseline\ndocuments, plus\nadditional information\nsuch as SOC reports,\ninformation security\npolicies, insurance\ncertificates, and three\nyears of audited financial\nstatements.\nHigh-risk vendors\nIn addition to all the', page_no=10, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('33f6cb0d-50c7-42e5-9a85-75eceada9713'), chunk_index=28, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364693, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='items you’d collect for\nlow and moderate-risk\nvendors, you should also\nreview documents like\npolicies and procedures,\nbusiness continuity and\ndisaster recovery plans,\nand penetration and\nvulnerability testing\nresults.', page_no=10, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('32e56521-b12d-48e8-819a-68ebd75e2270'), chunk_index=29, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364742, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='11\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\n1.\t Standardize your document requests\nLow, moderate, and high-risk vendors should have their own due diligence\nrequirements, which will ensure your organization isn’t spending additional time\non requesting non-relevant documents. Another way to create more efficiency is\nto establish a list of standardized documents for each risk domain and product or\nservice type. Taking a standardized approach to document requests will help identify', page_no=11, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1e08e57a-0b69-486b-ac18-515328f0bfe5'), chunk_index=30, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364746, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='exactly which documents the vendor will need to provide based on the inherent risks\nof the vendor’s product or service.\n2.\t Consider acceptable alternative documents\nIn some cases, vendors may be unwilling or unable to provide certain due diligence\ndocuments. Maybe a private vendor won’t disclose its financials, or another vendor\nhasn’t yet completed a SOC report. One of the easiest ways to save time and effort is', page_no=11, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1a464f11-f692-4643-ac3c-4b0dd65ef376'), chunk_index=31, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364750, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='to provide the vendor with a list of alternative documents they can submit.\nPRO TIP:\nYou can also suggest an\nalternative method of reviewing\nthe documents, such as hosting a\nvirtual session, so they don’t need\nto submit a physical file.\n4 Best Practices in Due Diligence', page_no=11, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cb94c97c-b23c-4e44-84e1-313d42af0f58'), chunk_index=32, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364789, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='12\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\n3.\t Use SMEs to review documentation\nOnce due diligence documents are gathered, it’s important to provide them to \nqualified SMEs who can accurately assess and interpret the data. SMEs are often \nlicensed or certified in their specific risk areas.', page_no=12, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9894e764-6e74-435e-a407-1ff9957e3064'), chunk_index=33, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364794, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='EXAMPLE:\nA certified public accountant (CPA) would be qualified to review a vendor’s\nfinancial statements. They should provide a written report that details the scope\nof the review, the documents and information considered, and any identified\ngaps, material weaknesses, or other issues.\n4.\t Create a remediation strategy\nIf the SME discovers any inadequacies or issues during the due diligence review, it’s\nimportant to develop and document a remediation strategy.\nEXAMPLE:', page_no=12, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1575e8db-9590-4c9b-be3b-fb2985180c49'), chunk_index=34, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364798, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A critical vendor’s untested business continuity plan would be an issue that\nneeds to be addressed. Your organization should determine whether the issue\nmust be remediated before the contract is signed. If remediation can occur after\ncontract execution, make sure to document specific timeline requirements.', page_no=12, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8bfaece9-ba62-4b52-85d4-6042cb42b26b'), chunk_index=35, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364805, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='13\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\nOnce the vendor assessment and due diligence is complete, your \norganization is prepared to make it official by selecting the vendor and \nproceeding with the contract negotiation and execution. \nPhase 3 \nContracting', page_no=13, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cdb13cf1-1d25-4992-a927-0cacbeb45334'), chunk_index=36, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364845, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='14\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\nThis phase involves two key activities:\n1\nObtaining internal approvals\nRefer back to your vendor selection\nprocess and solicit approval from\nthe appropriate team or individual\nwithin your organization. The approval\nshould be formally documented and\nstored according to your governance\ndocuments.\n2\nNegotiating and signing the contract\nThis can be another lengthy process, depending\non the contract provisions you want to include.', page_no=14, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('470cbc0a-5a61-4fa0-9f3b-a9085ee024d5'), chunk_index=37, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364849, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Some vendors will introduce standard contracts,\nso it’s important to work closely with your legal\nteam to ensure your vendor contract is revised\nas needed to include the appropriate terms and\nconditions that will protect your organization\nthroughout the engagement. Critical and high-\nrisk vendor contracts require additional scrutiny\nand should include some key provisions such as\nservice level agreements (SLAs), a right to audit\nclause, cybersecurity protections, and more.', page_no=14, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('de1b8c37-b781-4229-9cb9-a6e312a07ed5'), chunk_index=38, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364990, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='15\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\n5 Key Provisions of\nVendor Contracts:\n5 Best Practices for\nContract Negotiation\nNegotiating a vendor contract can be a\nchallenging process, depending on what\nyou’re trying to achieve and how the\nvendor responds to your requests.\nKeep these helpful tips in mind as you\nbegin the process:\n•\t Prioritize your needs – What\nare you looking to get from this', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b3878a94-3467-4b00-9330-1cd248eac80a'), chunk_index=39, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364994, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='vendor? What is important to\nyou? It’s important to focus first\non your expectations and how the\nvendor will provide value to your\norganization.\n•\t Establish clear objectives –\nEstablish what you want to have\nin the contract and what you are\nwilling to negotiate or let go of.\nWhat’s a deal-breaker for you?\n•\t Set or know your deadline – This\nwill help you move the process', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d110ce72-61a3-40ae-8191-ffaa8422c627'), chunk_index=40, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 364997, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='along. Are you in a hurry and willing\nto concede to some of their terms?\nIf the vendor is in a hurry to meet\nquota, this can give you leverage.\n•\t Negotiate gradually – This will help\nbreak the process down and allow\neach party to not be overwhelmed\nwith changes.\n•\t Move on – Be willing to move\non and walk away from the\nnegotiations, as this may push', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('90daac47-cb91-45c4-9721-a9f480de8106'), chunk_index=41, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365001, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='things in your favor. Perhaps you\ncan move to another vendor that\nsuits your needs better. If the\ncontract negotiation is this difficult,\nhow will the relationship be\nthroughout the lifecycle?\n•\t Right to audit – Throughout the vendor\nengagement, you’ll periodically perform\nscheduled due diligence reviews and re-assess\nrisks. There may also be occasions where you\nneed to review documents outside of those', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4bf4bc5c-ccda-42db-a8fe-b4de7db60bef'), chunk_index=42, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365005, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='periodic due diligence reviews. A right to audit\nclause ensures your organization will be able to\ncollect documents from the vendor upon request.\n•\t Service level agreements (SLAs) – These can vary\ndepending on the vendor’s product or service but\nshould be clearly defined and measurable. SLAs\nshould include details on rights and remedies if\nthe vendor fails to meet your standards, such as\ntermination of the contract.', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fb0934da-c562-47e9-9f81-1ae3bbf7719f'), chunk_index=43, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365009, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\t Data breach notifications – Regulators have\nset expectations for organizations to notify\ntheir customers of certain data breaches – even\nif the cybersecurity incident was caused by a\nthird-party vendor. A contractual clause for data\nbreach notifications should include details like a\ntimeline for when the vendor should notify your\norganization of an incident, how the vendor will\ninvestigate the incident, and how the vendor will', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a869f00c-9256-4a45-93ea-c5e06d327767'), chunk_index=44, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365013, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='handle the compromised information.\n•\t Use of subcontractors – Your vendors’\nsubcontractors, or your fourth parties, should be\nidentified in critical vendor contracts. Although\nyour organization doesn’t have a contractual\nrelationship with these subcontractors, you can\nrequire your vendor to monitor and perform\noversight on its subcontractors.\n•\t Business continuity and disaster recovery\n(BC/DR) – Reviewing BC/DR plans should be done\nduring due diligence, but you may want to add', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f4e19d48-5861-49ab-a461-1711946224ee'), chunk_index=45, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365016, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='these details in your critical vendor contracts, too.\nContractual provisions around BC/DR plans may\ninclude independent testing requirements, the\nfrequency and availability of these test results,\nand your organization’s right to transfer your\naccount to another vendor without penalty in the\nevent of business failure or interruption.', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a61c5b97-64e1-41ac-90aa-fa58a6d51800'), chunk_index=46, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365066, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='16\nGuide to Your Vendor Onboarding Process\nThe onboarding process will generally end with any final\nadministrative tasks that are completed internally. These will be\nunique to your organization, but here are a couple to consider:\n•\t Add vendor to internal systems – Make sure the new vendor is\nproperly recorded and categorized in the appropriate systems,\nwhich might include your accounts payable program, an', page_no=16, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e3b354de-12af-4800-aa6e-12bfb7c872dc'), chunk_index=47, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365070, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='information security system, and a TPRM platform. Also, be sure\nto document the official onboarding date for your records.\n•\t Notify the stakeholders – The vendor onboarding process\ncan be weeks or months long, so it’s a good idea to notify your\nstakeholders once everything is complete. This can help avoid\nany unintentional delays for projects that are dependent on the\nnew vendor.\nFinal Administrative Tasks', page_no=16, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e6ec9af7-f2b8-4c61-8695-e5a7505b386d'), chunk_index=48, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365073, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Bringing a new vendor into\nyour organization can present\nmany exciting opportunities,\nbut it’s important to be\nthorough and deliberate\nthroughout the onboarding\nprocess. When your vendor\nrelationship begins on a\nstrong foundation of planning\nand due diligence, your\norganization will be better\nprepared to reap the benefits\nof this partnership.', page_no=16, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('34f7a64b-49e1-46e6-9787-17bdc2153425'), chunk_index=49, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365122, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Download Now\nDownload free samples of Venminder’s\nvendor Control Assessments and see\nhow they empower third-party risk\nprofessionals in mitigating risks.\nAbout Venminder\nVenminder is an industry recognized leader of third-party risk management solutions. Dedicated to third-party risk, the\ncompany is the go-to partner for software, high-quality assessments on vendor controls, certified subject-matter expertise,\nand education.', page_no=17, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('456e74fe-4af8-4679-aeec-b3401607b64f'), chunk_index=50, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365126, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Venminder’s platform provides a centralized location to execute a third-party risk management program. It enables users\nto store documentation, onboard a vendor, track contracts, manage SLAs, send and manage questionnaires, manage due\ndiligence and oversight, complete risk assessments, create workflows, run reporting, and more.\nAssessments performed by Venminder’s qualified experts, including CISSPs, CPAs, financial risk analysts, paralegals and more,', page_no=17, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5475020d-92ad-4909-bfd8-3daa67619476'), chunk_index=51, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('5a80750d-d5d0-4868-9b16-1db130010354'), document_group_id=UUID('a797cf67-40d3-43fd-b452-5bc23e906b32'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 33, 10, 365130, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='are readily available in an online exchange library. The assessments enable customers to identify possible risks and understand\nareas of strength on their vendors’ information security and privacy standards, SOC reports, financial viability, business\ncontinuity/disaster recovery preparedness, contractual standards, regulatory compliance, and more.\n© 2024 Venminder, Inc.\nManage Vendors. Mitigate Risk. Reduce Workload.\n+1 (888) 836-6463  |  venminder.com', page_no=17, section=None, title=None)]
