ice . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .129', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fc76ff86-4f76-4e01-9ca2-05d02f1cebb3'), chunk_index=89, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 361637, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Enable goods receipt-based invoice verification . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 131', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5f67d167-0d5c-47d9-930b-891f2c71e949'), chunk_index=90, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 361641, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Match receipts to invoices without ship notices . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 131', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('467afe85-84af-4a60-84aa-33bc6c727d1e'), chunk_index=91, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 361644, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Allow edits to matched quantity in receipt matching . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 132', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c3aaba32-84de-44ff-b343-d572070b7ecd'), chunk_index=92, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363472, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Days to delay creating an IR document . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 133', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('de3dc44e-6493-40df-bde9-90866171dfd0'), chunk_index=93, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363480, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Third-party tax calculation for buying and invoicing . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 134', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4d4df7f9-c3d4-4605-9d19-cc70eff472b8'), chunk_index=94, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363485, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Enhanced third-party tax calculation for invoicing . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 134', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2b32f7f6-d039-4108-8e72-3fe4847512ee'), chunk_index=95, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363489, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Enhanced warnings for force actions on invoices and payments. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .135', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('568b3c14-550f-4481-a418-27e770be67f8'), chunk_index=96, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363493, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Use receipt unit price to validate invoice unit price. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 135', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0a6a40fc-7aea-460e-88a6-7a94156629b8'), chunk_index=97, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363497, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Managing Payment Documents. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . 137\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Managing Payment Documents. . . . . . . . . . . . . .140\n4\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nContent', page_no=4, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c5c1d1f1-6d3d-4c90-b117-fcb3e935fe47'), chunk_index=98, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363520, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Process tax accrual payments . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .140', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('387bdfc4-c8f4-48fe-ba74-3e5b930f5832'), chunk_index=99, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363524, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='ERP errors that trigger auto-resend of documents . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .140\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nContent\nPUBLIC\n5', page_no=5, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('97bfc06f-87c1-4a2b-b9bd-cc35689ca298'), chunk_index=100, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363563, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nThis guide is for SAP Ariba buyer users and administrators seeking a general understanding of workflows and\nprocesses for invoices and payments.\nBuyers process invoices from suppliers in order to pay for goods and services.\nThis guide applies to:\n•\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing\n•\nSAP Ariba Invoice Management\n•\nSAP Ariba Contract Invoicing\nRelated Guides\nCreating and Managing Invoices\nReconciling Invoices', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7702892f-c452-424d-8703-ebf8003a1617'), chunk_index=101, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363567, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Managing Payment Documents\nInvoicing Data Import and Administration Guide\nTax and Charge Configuration\nManaging Contract Compliance\n6\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide', page_no=6, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d7c575a9-785d-4940-9394-4d4d85364ad9'), chunk_index=102, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363709, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Invoicing and Payment Workflow in SAP Ariba\nSolutions\nAlthough your company's specific invoice workflow depends on your site's configuration and your company's\nbusiness processes, SAP Ariba invoicing solutions SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement support a common general process.\n1.\nDepending on your site enablement options and the invoice process flow configured for your site, an invoice is\ncreated:\n•", page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9b63a27a-cccf-4358-82be-12670cec42ec'), chunk_index=103, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363714, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='In your external ERP system and loaded into your SAP Ariba solution through SAP Business Network. This\noption is only available if your solution includes SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\n•\nBy the supplier on SAP Business Network and transmitted to your SAP Ariba solution.\n•\nManually by a user in your site using a paper invoice sent by a supplier.\n•', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('54966a42-ad56-4c1e-aa43-0878bf23cad2'), chunk_index=104, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363718, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Manually by a supplier punching into your site from their SAP Business Network account to create a\ncontract-based invoice.\n•\nBy an invoice conversion service (ICS) provider that converts paper invoices to electronic format and\nsends them through SAP Business Network to your site.\n•\nAutomatically by SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing for procurement transactions from supplier locations\nthat are enabled for Evaluated Receipt Settlement (ERS) and automatic invoicing.', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('223db3e1-7cfd-4dee-bb6b-a457a6ea553d'), chunk_index=105, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363721, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When an invoice is submitted in any of these ways, your SAP Ariba invoicing solution creates an approvable\ninvoice document.\n2. When the invoice is approved, two associated approvable documents are automatically created:\n•\nAn invoice reconciliation (IR) document, which invoice exception handlers use to resolve any discrepancies\nbetween the invoice, associated orders or contracts, and receipts, to validate accounting and other\ninformation.\n•', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('84e8180c-fce1-44a3-a6db-d8a1aa4b35d5'), chunk_index=106, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363725, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A payment request document, which is used to generate a payment once the invoice is reconciled.\n3. If any advance payments have been made for the purchase orders corresponding to the invoice, a payment\nmanager is added to the approval flow of the invoice reconciliation document. The payment manager adjusts\nthese advance payments against the invoice.', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('df0b515c-9b10-4543-8e17-a79aaee9b612'), chunk_index=107, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363729, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="4. The automatic reconciliation processor tries to match the IR to existing purchase orders, contracts, and\nreceipts, and then validates them according to your site's configuration. At this point, one of the following two\nprocesses occurs:\n•\nIf there are no discrepancies in the IR, or if the discrepancies are within your company's pre-configured", page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('632e08a1-0f1e-4eb6-86f0-79c82dfe6589'), chunk_index=108, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363732, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='tolerances, the IR is sent directly to the responsible group or person for approval to pay the supplier.\n•\nIf there are unacceptable discrepancies in the IR, they are displayed as exceptions on the IR document and\nmust be manually reconciled. One or more exception handlers resolve exceptions, and the IR is sent to the\nresponsible group or person for approval to pay the supplier.', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0dfdd114-46c3-43ed-80ef-c9910aec1eac'), chunk_index=109, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363736, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If your site is configured to handle final approval of the IR, the invoice moves to Reconciled status at this point.\nIf your site is configured to send the IR for final reconciliation and approval in your ERP system, the invoice\nmoves to Reconciling status until that final approval is received.\n5. After the invoice is reconciled, the payment is scheduled through the payment request.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('34942316-b372-472e-a724-80f1b67c9f09'), chunk_index=110, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363740, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Workflow in SAP Ariba Solutions\nPUBLIC\n7', page_no=7, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('45dd3366-17f3-4688-abcb-3af7cf7151c0'), chunk_index=111, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363746, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Related Information\nInvoice and Invoice Reconciliation Status Flow [page 95]\nPayment Document Status Flow [page 92]\nAdvance Payment Status Flow [page 99]\n8\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoicing and Payment Workflow in SAP Ariba Solutions', page_no=8, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b24dd653-2046-407e-b3c5-8c331911f34e'), chunk_index=112, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363867, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Advance Payment Workflow\nThe following steps explain the workflow for advance payments. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing can be configured\nto support header-level and line-level advance payments.\n1.\nA user creates a requisition for material items. A purchase order is generated after the requisition is fully\napproved.\n2. A payment agent or payment manager creates and submits an advance payment document for the purchase', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1f181419-764c-4c41-942f-21bdd00536fd'), chunk_index=113, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363872, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='order. The status of the advance payment document changes from Composing to Submitted.\n3. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing generates an approval flow for the advance payment document if the approval\nprocess for advance payments is enabled.\n4. Approvers approve the advance payment document. The status of the advance payment document changes to\nApproved.', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8e26fc7e-b051-4e05-80e3-ab520973b51e'), chunk_index=114, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363876, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5. The approved advance payment document is exported to the external systems in one of the following ways:\n•\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing exports the advance payment documents to external systems using the\nweb services channel.\n•\nA customer administrator exports the advance payment documents to a CSV file, which is used to import\nthe advance payment documents into the external systems.', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3e3d166b-ff0d-460d-8f3d-0d79b5a5df76'), chunk_index=115, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363879, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='6. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing receives the ERP payment request ID for the exported advance payment\ndocuments, in one of the following ways:\n•\nThe external system sends the payment request IDs to SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing using the web\nservices channel.\n•\nThe customer administrator imports advance payment IDs generated by the external system, using CSV\nfiles.\nThe status of the advance payment documents changes to Paying.', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5fe10e95-d612-45d0-9446-ba9161e099bf'), chunk_index=116, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363883, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='7.\nThe external system processes the payment and sends the remittance information to SAP Ariba Buying and\nInvoicing.\n8. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing changes the status of the advance payment document to Paid when the entire\npayment is made for it. (For line-level advance payments, the status changes to Paid when the payment is\nprocessed for all line items on the advance payment document.)', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('65ccdf07-4592-4313-80b6-730ff9b9adbb'), chunk_index=117, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363887, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Alternatively, if the site is not integrated with an external system, the payment manager manually marks an\nadvance payment in Approved or Paying state as Paid by clicking the Force Pay button on the advance\npayment page.\n9. The supplier sends an invoice to the buyer.\n10. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing generates an invoice reconciliation document for the invoice.', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bdc48c67-bdd0-4a64-ad06-d1e0dfe08b0f'), chunk_index=118, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363890, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='11. The payment manager adjusts the advance payment amount against the invoice amount in the invoice\nreconciliation document.\n12. The invoice manager reconciles the invoice.\n13. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing generates a payment request for the reconciled invoice. This payment request\nfile has information about the advance payments adjusted against the invoice.', page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ed3da04b-2ee2-4878-a794-6bbd323092d9'), chunk_index=119, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363894, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="The amount of the payment request is the total approved invoice amount, not the total invoice amount minus\nthe advance payment. The ERP system handles the deduction when processing the payment. Also, payment\nrequests on the invoice Reference tab don't indicate the use of advance payments.\n14. The system exports the payment request to the external system for payment processing.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nAdvance Payment Workflow\nPUBLIC\n9", page_no=9, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('29ddf62d-4593-433f-a0c3-f0b3f60cb759'), chunk_index=120, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363916, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Line-item credit memos and advance payments\nIf the supplier sends a line-item credit memo against an invoice that was adjusted for an advance payment, SAP\nAriba Buying and Invoicing doesn't reverse the adjustment. There are no accumulator adjustments for advance\npayments. Accumulators on invoices, credit memos, and IR documents have nothing to do with advance payments.\nRelated Information\nAdvance Payment Status Flow [page 99]\n10\nPUBLIC", page_no=10, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5b72cecd-e1ef-4785-8e89-834694d845e2'), chunk_index=121, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 363920, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nAdvance Payment Workflow', page_no=10, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('378d9628-fad3-4f59-9bc9-f69ed28f7c34'), chunk_index=122, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364020, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Contract-Based Invoicing\nIn contract-based invoicing, suppliers punch into your SAP Ariba invoicing solution to create invoices based on the\ncontracts you have with them.\nIn contract-based invoicing, suppliers create invoices from no release item-level, commodity-level, customer\ncatalog-level, or supplier-level contract by punching into your site from SAP Business Network. Your site must\nbe configured to allow contract-based invoicing. If it is, suppliers use the contract-based invoicing workflow to', page_no=11, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c7497e0f-a304-444b-804d-ebf4e341fbd0'), chunk_index=123, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364024, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='create an invoice for all contracts except for blanket purchase orders that do not allow contract invoicing.\nWhen suppliers create contract-based invoices, they can enter an optional email address in the Sold To Email\nAddress field. This address is used to set the Requester (On Behalf Of) on the invoice and invoice reconciliation', page_no=11, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2a3c8366-dcb1-4923-809a-9ac4879f6621'), chunk_index=124, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364028, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="documents. This field is validated, and suppliers cannot submit an invoice with an invalid Sold To Email Address\nvalue.\nThere are two different ways suppliers can create contract-based invoices, and the method they use depends on\nyour site's configuration:\n•\nIn collaborative invoicing, suppliers punch into your site from SAP Business Network to create the invoice.\n•", page_no=11, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9694cb13-b5ff-450e-999a-5cf1b1f7b03b'), chunk_index=125, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364032, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='In SAP Business Network-validated contract invoicing, suppliers create the invoice in their SAP Business\nNetwork accounts and punch into your site only to retrieve the contract and add contract lines.\nContract-Based Invoicing from Blanket Purchase Orders\nSuppliers can create contract-based invoices against blanket purchase order contracts in some cases.\nWith blanket purchase order contracts (BPOs), contract agents must specify the Allow invoicing against the', page_no=11, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bead78f3-5c89-4348-accc-098a81a79c77'), chunk_index=126, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364036, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='contract option in order to allow contract-based invoicing. If this option is not specified, suppliers can create\ninvoices using PO-Flip (purchase order-to-invoice flip) on SAP Business Network for no-release order item-level\nBPOs. For no-release order supplier-, commodity-, or customer catalog-level BPOs, they must create a non-PO\ninvoice on SAP Business Network and provide the contract ID as a reference.\nSAP Business Network-Validated Contract Invoicing Workflow [page 11]', page_no=11, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c0cb5683-4fca-4c1d-8dd9-418b454c4b82'), chunk_index=127, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364040, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Business Network-Validated Contract Invoicing\nWorkflow\nIn SAP Business Network-validated contract invoicing, suppliers create invoices on SAP Business Network but\npunch into the SAP Ariba invoicing solution to retrieve the contract and add items.\nThe following general steps describe the supplier workflow for SAP Business Network-validated contract invoicing,\nwhich must be enabled in your site.\n•\nSuppliers initiate the contract-based invoice creation from SAP Business Network by selecting the customer', page_no=11, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a5466a09-836b-4f00-8fc2-d69b0ac19b21'), chunk_index=128, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364044, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='for which they are creating the invoice.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nContract-Based Invoicing\nPUBLIC\n11', page_no=11, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2ce6b5eb-dce7-4e2b-b9c1-ca9276fa2f2d'), chunk_index=129, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364147, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\nSAP Business Network automatically transfers the supplier to your invoicing site, where the supplier selects\nthe contract and enters the invoice number, invoice date, and the Sold To Email Address (email of the person\nwho requested the goods or services). Depending on the contract specifications, the Sold To Email Address\nmight be defaulted from the contact person on the contract.\n•', page_no=12, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('90d3177f-eaaf-4b1b-95ba-6745a61f252a'), chunk_index=130, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364152, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The supplier user is then returned to their familiar Create Invoice page to enter additional invoice header\ninformation.\n•\nTo add items to the invoice, the supplier is again transferred to your site to select the items from the customer\ncatalog. If allowed, they can also add non-catalog items.\n•\nDepending on the contract configuration, the supplier might enter accounting information.\n•', page_no=12, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('350398a5-0050-42d3-8acf-1b6993472800'), chunk_index=131, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364156, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="The invoice line items are validated against the contract line items, and the contract's pricing terms are\napplied. If any discrepancies are found, the supplier receives an error message prompting them to correct the\ninformation.\n•\nThe supplier is returned to SAP Business Network.\n•\nIf the supplier needs to make changes to any of the line items on the invoice, they are transferred back to your\nsite.\n•", page_no=12, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8d2c8fb0-c7ab-4b35-be3e-420e1fa3c55d'), chunk_index=132, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364160, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If allowed by your SAP Business Network business rules, the supplier can change the unit price on the invoice.\nThis effectively overrides the pricing terms defined in the contract for the items. For example, if a customer\ncatalog-level contract is defined with a 10% discount for all items, and the supplier changes the unit price of an', page_no=12, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3c5d9c81-4e47-4cb7-9a32-b646bc5ac3a6'), chunk_index=133, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364164, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='item on the invoice, that price will be the final price used on the invoice. Depending on your invoice exceptions\nconfiguration and tolerance settings, this situation might lead to an invoice exception that will require an\nexception handler to resolve the discrepancy before the invoice can be approved for payment.\n•\nOn SAP Business Network, the supplier completes the invoice by adding other header fields and adds any', page_no=12, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('500bdb91-a78d-4c80-9727-a5ebe665970b'), chunk_index=134, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364167, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='comments, attachments, tax, shipping documents, or special handling line items either at the invoice header\nor at the line item level.\n•\nBefore the supplier submits the invoice, they can always return to your site to retrieve additional items, change\na contract header field such as the Sold To Email Address, or edit or delete existing line items on the invoice.\n•', page_no=12, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('96e93190-d334-4881-93f3-d2be1f15a134'), chunk_index=135, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364171, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When the supplier submits the invoice, SAP Business Network validates it against the invoicing business rules\nset in your SAP Business Network account, adds a digital signature if required, and sends it to your site for\nreconciliation.\nParent topic: Contract-Based Invoicing [page 11]\n12\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nContract-Based Invoicing', page_no=12, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('92ff41b1-6aeb-47dd-a98d-32823c5ccf05'), chunk_index=136, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364292, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Services Invoicing\nServices invoicing is a set of features and a workflow that allow your company to track, manage, and approve how\nsuppliers fulfill and invoice orders for services.\nServices Invoicing Workflow in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 13]\nComparison of Services Invoicing Features in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 14]\nService Orders [page 17]\nService Sheets and Service Sheet Validation [page 19]\nService Invoices [page 20]', page_no=13, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a8342a0f-8285-4a24-b577-66a93aacd84c'), chunk_index=137, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364296, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Services Invoicing Workflow in SAP Ariba Solutions\nThe services invoicing workflow involves the following general steps between the buyer and supplier.\n1.\nDepending on the SAP Ariba solution, one of the following buyer actions apply:\n•\n(SAP Ariba Invoice Management) The buyer sends an approved purchase order with at least one service\nline (a line that requires a service sheet) from an integrated ERP system to SAP Business Network.', page_no=13, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('94e9b109-de1c-4153-bcf1-e5a95d65f6d7'), chunk_index=138, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364300, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Business Network receives the order, sends it to the supplier, and sends a copy order to SAP Ariba\nInvoice Management. The copy order triggers updates to accumulators on any associated contracts.\n•\n(SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing) The buyer creates a service requisition for a service item (an item that\nrequires a service sheet). After the requisition is fully approved, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing sends an', page_no=13, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bf76537e-ef12-4383-b47f-5b70e73beba3'), chunk_index=139, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364304, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='approved purchase order to the supplier.\n2. On the SAP Business Network, the supplier optionally confirms the purchase order and then creates a service\nsheet for it. The supplier can add items to the service sheet in the following circumstances:\n•\nIf your site is configured for supplier punchin, the supplier can punch in to add contract/catalog items. If', page_no=13, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b7705294-3f9e-485c-b33e-514a2bd98698'), chunk_index=140, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364308, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='your site allows it, the supplier can also add non-catalog items in the service sheet shopping cart during\npunchin. Your site might also allow suppliers to edit accounting information for those items.\n•\nIf your site is not configured for supplier punchin, but your SAP Business Network buyer account business\nrule settings allow it, the supplier can add ad hoc items to the service sheet on the SAP Business Network.', page_no=13, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('006d7479-cd33-4332-9bcc-36fcb57394a6'), chunk_index=141, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364312, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3. On the SAP Business Network, the supplier submits the service sheet and, if it passes validation, it enters the\napproval flow.\n4. If necessary, the approvers in the approval flow edit accounting information for service sheet lines and approve\nthe service sheet.\n5. (If approval in an external ERP system is not required) Approvers approve the service sheet and the status', page_no=13, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1636b757-432f-49e3-b5ae-398325e5255d'), chunk_index=142, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364316, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='of the service sheet changes to Processed. The SAP Ariba solution sends a status update to SAP Business\nNetwork.\n6. (If approval in an external ERP system is required) One of the following actions is applicable:\n•\n(For SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing) After approval, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing sends the approved', page_no=13, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('090c8f0e-b00f-48e4-b05e-d7a9ea1fa7a5'), chunk_index=143, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364320, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='service sheet to the ERP system for external approval and the status of the service sheet changes to\nAwaiting External Approval. After approval in the ERP system, the status of the service sheet changes to\nProcessed and SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing sends a status update to SAP Business Network.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nServices Invoicing\nPUBLIC\n13', page_no=13, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('876dc490-2905-4284-922c-c37fae478f19'), chunk_index=144, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364404, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\n(For SAP Ariba Invoice Management) After approval, SAP Ariba Invoice Managementsends the service\nsheet to the external ERP system for external approval and the status of the service sheet changes to\nAwaiting External Approval. The ERP system sends a status update to SAP Business Network, which\nsends the status update back to Ariba Invoice Professional. The service sheet status is then Processed.\n7.', page_no=14, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ddc0e716-3283-459d-8d66-2456fd5f7105'), chunk_index=145, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364409, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='On SAP Business Network, the supplier invoices one or more approved service sheets. SAP Business Network\nsends the invoice to the SAP Ariba invoicing solution, where the invoice follows the regular invoicing and\npayment process [page 7].\nIf a service sheet is rejected at any point before it is fully approved, either during validation or by an approver in the', page_no=14, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0f460cda-519c-45b3-a824-30daae405399'), chunk_index=146, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364412, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Ariba solution or the external ERP system, the supplier can edit and resubmit the rejected service sheet on the\nSAP Business Network using a different service sheet number. At that point, the SAP Business Network sends the\nservice sheet back to the SAP Ariba solution and it enters the validation and approval process again.\nParent topic: Services Invoicing [page 13]\nRelated Information', page_no=14, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0c7ed6da-8333-4221-944f-9e0a09da4ee9'), chunk_index=147, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364416, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Comparison of Services Invoicing Features in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 14]\nService Orders [page 17]\nService Sheets and Service Sheet Validation [page 19]\nService Invoices [page 20]\nInvoice and Invoice Reconciliation Status Flow [page 95]\nComparison of Services Invoicing Features in SAP\nAriba Solutions\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice Management support supplier punchin and full service sheet', page_no=14, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('61d2eef4-6584-47ea-8298-844f03958db3'), chunk_index=148, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364420, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='validation and approval, while SAP Ariba Contract Invoicing supports supplier punchin and more limited validation\nfor service sheet creation.\nServices invoicing includes item matching between orders, customer catalogs and contracts; order accumulation\nagainst contracts; and service sheet accumulation against orders. These features keep orders and invoices within\ncontract limits, within budget, and using contract pricing.', page_no=14, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('04368dd6-f49d-44f2-bdc1-3d2290ea024d'), chunk_index=149, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364424, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The following table briefly describes the different services invoicing features provided by each SAP Ariba solution:\nFeature\nSAP Ariba Contract Invoicing\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoic-\ning and SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement\nNotes\nService orders\n14\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nServices Invoicing', page_no=14, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a962a3b2-8367-4b56-9ee5-3fa3bd4e63a9'), chunk_index=150, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364485, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Feature\nSAP Ariba Contract Invoicing\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoic-\ning and SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement\nNotes\nSupport for service orders\nwith planned or unplanned\nservice lines\nX\nX\nFor SAP Ariba Invoice Man-\nagement, service orders are\nalways created in integrated\nERP systems\nService Sheets\nSupport for service sheets\nX\nX\nService sheet tolerances and\nrules are set in the SAP Busi-\nness Network buyer account', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('603ec4bf-bc12-4112-a306-9fa353a7a2f1'), chunk_index=151, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364489, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Suppliers can add non-catalog\n(unplanned) items to service\nsheets via punchin from SAP\nBusiness Network\nX\nX\nSet using configuration pa-\nrameters in the SAP Ariba in-\nvoicing solution\nSuppliers can add file attach-\nments to service sheets\nX\nX\nService sheet rules are set\nin the SAP Business Network\nbuyer account and a site con-\nfiguration parameter is ena-\nbled for the SAP Ariba solu-\ntion.', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2d9a147c-dfe8-403d-9d43-0d27df910430'), chunk_index=152, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364493, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Service sheet price validation\nagainst matching contracts\nand customer catalogs\nX\nX\nService sheet quantity and\namount tolerances for plan-\nned items\nX\nX\nSet using transaction rules\nin the SAP Business Network\nbuyer account\nService sheet price tolerances\nfor planned items on service\npurchase orders\nX\nX\nSet using transaction rules\nin the SAP Business Network\nbuyer account\nService sheet price tolerances\nfor unplanned items added', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('17af2723-4175-4f9f-8695-36d73ed81a86'), chunk_index=153, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364497, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='from contracts or customer\ncatalogs\nX\nX\nSet using configuration pa-\nrameters in the SAP Ariba sol-\nution\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nServices Invoicing\nPUBLIC\n15', page_no=15, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5253a6bf-5f06-4fbe-ab67-9856bbb69629'), chunk_index=154, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364553, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Feature\nSAP Ariba Contract Invoicing\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoic-\ning and SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement\nNotes\nWorkflow routing (including\nemail notifications) for:\n•\nService sheet approvals\nto accounts payable or\nbusiness users\n•\nExpired contracts\n•\nInvalid commodity codes\nor units of measure on\nservice sheets\nX\nInvoices\nSuppliers can submit contract\ninvoices (including contract\nvalidation for automated sup-\npliers)\nX\nX\nValidation for automated sup-', page_no=16, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('af13c428-829d-41ab-85eb-9b875825ea57'), chunk_index=155, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364558, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='pliers in SAP Ariba Contract\nInvoicing is through contract\nexceptions set to auto-reject\nSuppliers can submit contract\ninvoices based on blanket pur-\nchase orders (including con-\ntract validation for automated\nsuppliers)\nX\nX\nValidation for automated sup-\npliers in SAP Ariba Contract\nInvoicing is through contract\nexceptions set to auto-reject\nSuppliers can submit service\ninvoices created from service\nsheets\nX\nX\nBuyers can submit contract-\nbased invoices\nX', page_no=16, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1a261aaa-ac71-4f50-8d35-402082bdda1d'), chunk_index=156, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364561, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Workflow routing (including\nemail notifications) for:\n•\nInvoice exception types\nagainst purchase orders\n•\nInvoice exceptions to ac-\ncounts payable and busi-\nness users\n•\nInvoice approvals to ac-\ncounts payable or busi-\nness users\nX\nOther\n16\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nServices Invoicing', page_no=16, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('08d5fbb0-4803-4ce7-a52a-840fbd521acd'), chunk_index=157, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364605, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Feature\nSAP Ariba Contract Invoicing\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoic-\ning and SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement\nNotes\nAnalytical reporting, including\nprepackaged and custom re-\nports\nX\nField Engineer, Field Service\nAdministrator, Service Sheet\nEditor, and Reporting\nManager global user groups\nX\nData import task for importing\ncontracts as CSV files\nX\nX\nAccounting master data and\ndefault accounting\nX\nSupport for multi-ERP config-\nurations\nX\nX\nRequires additional SAP Ariba', page_no=17, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a0ef3f96-cd88-4455-8f47-eabef01f2ced'), chunk_index=158, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364609, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='services\nParent topic: Services Invoicing [page 13]\nRelated Information\nServices Invoicing Workflow in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 13]\nService Orders [page 17]\nService Sheets and Service Sheet Validation [page 19]\nService Invoices [page 20]\nContract-Based Invoicing [page 11]\nNon-PO Invoicing [page 34]\nService Orders\nService orders are purchase orders that include at least one line that requires a service sheet.', page_no=17, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('28ab32a3-a836-4b64-906f-6dcef0cc1465'), chunk_index=159, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364613, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Service orders have special characteristics such as maximum amounts, contract matching, and planned or\nunplanned service lines.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nServices Invoicing\nPUBLIC\n17', page_no=17, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ac45cbd8-2368-4b02-889e-da1c49be750b'), chunk_index=160, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364712, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Maximum Amounts for Service Order Lines\nService orders can include a maximum amount at the line level. Maximum amounts are budgeting tools that allow\nsuppliers to exceed the regular line amount by a specific amount (if the maximum amount is higher than the line\namount), or can enforce the line amount (if the maximum amount is the same as the line amount). Maximum', page_no=18, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('95a1e229-6363-4563-a701-e5d1c32c7367'), chunk_index=161, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364716, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="amounts are always hidden from suppliers on SAP Business Network but are visible to members of the Field\nEngineer group in your SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing solution. Suppliers are not able to submit service sheets\nthat exceed a line's maximum amount.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\n(If your site is not enabled for external approvals for service sheets) For service orders that do not include a", page_no=18, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1f400647-1a09-4cc7-8655-abdae01bfac8'), chunk_index=162, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364720, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='maximum amount for a line item, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing considers the order line-item amount as the\nmaximum amount to determine whether suppliers can submit service sheets.\nContract Matching for Service Orders\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing matches service orders only to associated contracts, determine whether or not\norder line items match existing customer catalogs for the contract, and identify them as customer catalog or\nnon-catalog items.', page_no=18, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a80ee30b-a5e7-4549-a79e-da5059ff940c'), chunk_index=163, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364724, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Planned and Unplanned Service Order Lines\nService lines can be planned, meaning that they describe specific pieces of work and have set quantities and\namounts. For service orders associated with a release contracts, all planned lines that match the contract\naccumulate against that contract at the header and line level.\nService lines can also be unplanned, meaning that they have a mandatory minimum amount but are otherwise', page_no=18, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b84d5e9c-bd44-4a19-9357-109a8ad28732'), chunk_index=164, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364728, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='open-ended. For unplanned lines, all accumulation against purchase order limits are calculated based on subtotals;\nthere is no checking on unit price or quantities.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nYou can enable the Validate service sheet maximum amount limit against unplanned items\nonly (Application.ServiceSheet.SupportServiceOrdersMaxAmountForUnplannedItemsOnly)\nparameter to validate the service sheet maximum amount limit against unplanned service items only. For\nmore information, see Validate service sheet maximum amount limit against unplanned items only.', page_no=18, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b325e127-d2bd-411a-8dd2-34d9d68ab7c8'), chunk_index=165, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364732, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Parent topic: Services Invoicing [page 13]\nRelated Information\nServices Invoicing Workflow in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 13]\n18\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nServices Invoicing', page_no=18, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('21408c37-8fac-4ae5-ba3c-926ce38805e1'), chunk_index=166, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364817, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Comparison of Services Invoicing Features in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 14]\nService Sheets and Service Sheet Validation [page 19]\nService Invoices [page 20]\nService Sheets and Service Sheet Validation\nA service sheet is a document that suppliers performing a service create in order to describe that service. After a\nsupplier submits a service sheet, it is validated and must be approved in the SAP Ariba solution or an integrated', page_no=19, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d646bfe6-66b5-4556-8eaa-f34dd8d038b8'), chunk_index=167, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364822, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='ERP system.\nSuppliers can only invoice service orders based on approved service sheets.\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice Management solutions support full validation and approval\nof service sheets. SAP Ariba Contract Invoicing only validates service sheets for contract and customer catalog\npricing. SAP Ariba invoicing solutions automatically reject service sheets during validation for the following\nreasons:\n•', page_no=19, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5df0a420-689a-4056-ad5a-5ac095c34b98'), chunk_index=168, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364825, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The associated order does not exist, or does exist but is in a state other than Ordered or Ordered with Errors.\n•\nThe service sheet includes an item from a contract but the price exceeds configured tolerances for the contract\nor customer catalog price.\n•\nThe service sheet references a different contract than the associated order.\n•', page_no=19, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a04a5f6c-8520-48e5-899d-80e38f2a30c9'), chunk_index=169, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364829, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The release contract associated with the order has expired after the order was made but before the service\nsheet was submitted, or the release contract associated with the service sheet has expired after the item was\nadded to the service sheet but before it was submitted. In SAP Ariba Procurement solutions, you can configure\ncontract exceptions to route the service sheet to exception managers for handling rather than automatically', page_no=19, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c4375cb7-98b3-43fc-b33c-4ce974e71d7d'), chunk_index=170, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364833, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='rejecting it.\n•\nThe service sheet contains non-catalog items and your site is not configured to allow suppliers to add non-\ncatalog items to service sheets.\n•\nThe service sheet is not associated with a contract but contains a customer catalog item, and the price is\nhigher than tolerances configured for the catalog price.\nParent topic: Services Invoicing [page 13]\nRelated Information', page_no=19, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bd1cf6c2-29b4-4058-b769-08b77baaa947'), chunk_index=171, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364837, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Services Invoicing Workflow in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 13]\nComparison of Services Invoicing Features in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 14]\nService Orders [page 17]\nService Invoices [page 20]\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nServices Invoicing\nPUBLIC\n19', page_no=19, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2fbeae69-cb5d-4802-98b0-ea240b446666'), chunk_index=172, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364872, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Service Invoices\nService invoices are based on approved service sheets for service orders and there must be at least one approved\nservice sheet.\nTypically, suppliers create service invoices in their SAP Business Network accounts and submit those invoices\nthrough SAP Business Network, but users can also create service invoices directly in the SAP Ariba invoicing\nsolution.', page_no=20, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('db213113-4deb-4b3b-b997-5d434f6985ff'), chunk_index=173, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364876, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='After a service invoice is approved, the SAP Ariba invoicing solution creates an invoice reconciliation document for\nthe invoice and the invoice reconciliation document moves through the reconciliation process defined for invoices\nin your site.\nParent topic: Services Invoicing [page 13]\nRelated Information\nServices Invoicing Workflow in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 13]\nComparison of Services Invoicing Features in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 14]\nService Orders [page 17]', page_no=20, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('eb733ac8-230e-41f7-b093-e4710a514cad'), chunk_index=174, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364880, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Service Sheets and Service Sheet Validation [page 19]\n20\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nServices Invoicing', page_no=20, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d34e9b58-f308-48a5-9dab-6698b3dbd77c'), chunk_index=175, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364988, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing Process for Brazil\nThe invoicing process for Brazil enables buyers in Brazil to view invoices in their standard SEFAZ-approved formats\nand to export invoice attachments to the external systems. It also enables buyers to view correction information\nreceived for invoices.\nBrazilian tax authority Secretaria da Fazenda (SEFAZ) mandates legal compliance on all commercial transactions', page_no=21, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('08e6dfb6-43a5-464f-9e2e-f205bac51458'), chunk_index=176, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364992, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="between suppliers and buyers. SEFAZ also mandates the use of defined standard electronic invoices to standardize\nthe transaction documents used between the tax authority and the tax payers (suppliers and buyers).\nTo enable buyers to adhere to SEFAZ's requirements, SAP Ariba provides the following invoicing capabilities to\nbuyers in Brazil:\n•\nView the following types of electronic invoices:\n•\nNota Fiscal Eletrônica (NFe): Goods invoice\n•", page_no=21, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d396fe95-0c4d-4207-ad40-8339a77f2ab4'), chunk_index=177, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 364996, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Conhecimento de Transporte (CTe): Shipping, handling, and transportation invoice\n•\nNota Fiscal de Serviço Eletrônica (NFSe): Services invoice\n•\nView the following invoice attachments:\n•\nXML: The SEFAZ-approved electronic invoice in XML format is attached to the invoice and invoice\nreconciliation document.\n•\nPDF: This is a human-readable, simplified representation of a Brazilian electronic invoice and contains', page_no=21, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('93ecd5a7-b8cc-476d-8d81-6b7567348a40'), chunk_index=178, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365000, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='essential transaction details such as sender, recipient and numeric barcode. The PDF format of an\nNFe is called Documento Auxiliar do Nota Fiscal Eletrônica (DANFe), that for a CTe is\ncalled Documento Auxiliar do Conhecimento de Transporte (DACTe), while that for an NFSe\nis called Documento Auxiliar do Nota Fiscal de Serviço Eletrônica (DANFSe). This format is', page_no=21, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('67b2e840-991a-4aa2-be5f-8ce23087dbf5'), chunk_index=179, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365004, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='displayed as an attachment as well as a thumbnail in the invoice and invoice reconciliation document.\n•\nReceive an email notification when an electronic invoice addendum, known as Carta de Correção\nEletrônica (CCe), is received for the invoice. The correction letter describes some auxiliary changes\n(changes that do not alter the tax, quantity or total amount) required to the submitted invoice. This email', page_no=21, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b774cf6e-d811-415e-9bcd-999e377e8ba7'), chunk_index=180, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365008, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="notification is sent to the requester of the invoice. If the requester's information is not available, the notification\nis sent to the Invoice Administrator and Invoice Manager groups.\n•\nView the change description extracted from the CCe in the Invoice Addendum section in invoice and invoice\nreconciliation documents.\n•\nView the XML file for the CCe and other attachments sent for the CCe in the Invoice Addendum section in", page_no=21, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ee139af0-9f7f-4eda-826c-73ee8369b83b'), chunk_index=181, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365012, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoice and invoice reconciliation documents.\n•\nExport the invoice attachments to the external system, as part of the payment requests generated for the\nreconciled invoice. This is supported only for the Web Services channel.\nRelated Information\nWorkflow for the Invoicing Process for Brazil [page 22]\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoicing Process for Brazil\nPUBLIC\n21', page_no=21, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2ec5de3e-42a2-48fa-afea-de1ab1fa08d4'), chunk_index=182, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365112, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Workflow for the Invoicing Process for Brazil\nThe workflow for the electronic invoicing process of Brazil is very similar to the general invoicing workflow. Some\nadditional steps are required to adhere to SEFAZ's invoicing requirements and to handle correction letters received\nfor invoices.\nWorkflow for Invoice Attachments\nThe following steps describe the workflow for viewing electronic invoices and their attachments:\n1.", page_no=22, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6af1c61a-2c5f-4f6a-ae69-63864b4324e8'), chunk_index=183, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365116, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="SAP Business Network sends an invoice along with its SEFAZ-approved XML and PDF formats attached to it to\nthe buyer's external ERP system.\n2. Users can review the attachments in the Attachments section. The PDF format is also displayed as a\nthumbnail in the header section of the invoice.\n3. After the invoice is approved, the invoice reconciliation document for the invoice is generated and the invoice", page_no=22, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4d4a8176-6baf-4818-9301-b0a2f2e17f7d'), chunk_index=184, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365120, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='attachments is copied to the invoice reconciliation document.\n4. Users who have the required permissions resolve the invoice exceptions, if any, and reconcile the invoice.\n5. The SAP Ariba invoicing solution generates a payment request for the reconciled invoice.\n6. The payment request along with the invoice attachments is exported to the external system for payment.\nWorkflow for Correction Letters', page_no=22, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a3497209-3e24-4bb2-bf74-68c46658e753'), chunk_index=185, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365123, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The following steps describe the workflow for correction letters received for invoices:\n1.\nSuppliers submit a correction letter (CCe) for an invoice to SAP Business Network. The CCe can contain two\nattachments – the original CCe in its XML format and the CCe in its PDF format. Though the CCe contains', page_no=22, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e0cae9fb-c266-485a-bd89-e7d2215af3b5'), chunk_index=186, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365127, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='a description of the changes required to the invoice, the invoice itself does not get modified when a CCe is\nreceived.\n2. SAP Business Network extracts the change description from the CCe and creates a notification request\ndocument in cXML format. This notification request contains the original XML format of the CCe as an\nattachment and any other attachments that are part of the CCe.', page_no=22, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('58cf0707-8042-4048-b6a6-e5054ade414d'), chunk_index=187, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365131, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="3. SAP Business Network sends this notification request to the SAP Ariba invoicing solution.\n4. The SAP Ariba invoicing solution extracts the change description and attachments from the notification\nrequest and displays them in the Invoice Addendum section of the invoice.\n5. The SAP Ariba invoicing solution sends an email notification to the requester of the invoice. If the requester's", page_no=22, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2d4e320c-2ddb-488c-a9e0-5d63b801ddee'), chunk_index=188, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365135, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='contact information is not available, an email is sent to the Invoice Administrator and Invoice Manager\ngroups.\n6. The SAP Ariba invoicing solution generates an invoice reconciliation document for the invoice. The invoice\naddendum is copied to the invoice reconciliation document.\n7.\nUsers who have the required permissions resolve the invoice exceptions, if any, and reconcile the invoice.', page_no=22, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6574a3e4-1631-4152-9127-26a8111d3b15'), chunk_index=189, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365138, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='8. The SAP Ariba invoicing solution generates a payment request for the reconciled invoice.\n22\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nWorkflow for the Invoicing Process for Brazil', page_no=22, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0e9d3d25-9732-4a4f-8536-398f84f8ae7c'), chunk_index=190, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365158, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='9. The payment request along with all the invoice attachments is exported to the external system for payment.\nThe invoice attachments exported to the external system include the attachments of the CCe.\nFor information on viewing invoice attachments and addendums, see Finding Invoices.\nRelated Information\nInvoicing and Payment Workflow in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 7]\nInvoicing Process for Brazil [page 21]\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide', page_no=23, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f11e5ce2-575e-4033-8208-4956f0991432'), chunk_index=191, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365162, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Workflow for the Invoicing Process for Brazil\nPUBLIC\n23', page_no=23, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('664c6d8e-f4d7-4f72-add3-13cb1b13d3c3'), chunk_index=192, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365274, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing Process for Japan\nThe tax authority in Japan will follow a new invoicing method called as TEKIKAKU SEIKYUSHO TOU HOZON\nHOUSHIKI, and it is effective October 1, 2023. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing now provides an enhanced method\nfor tax calculation to support the new invoicing method in Japan. Thus, invoices created in both these systems', page_no=24, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c4703fb1-580b-4bb4-9ad8-5728c40256d0'), chunk_index=193, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365279, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='will have the tax summarization calculated at the header level during invoice creation. The tax rounding (round up,\nround half-up, round down) occurs only once per tax rate in a single invoice.\nSupplier organizations need to register with the tax authority in Japan. The tax authority issues a unique ID for\neach supplier called as Tax Registration Number. This Tax Registration Number enables the buyers and suppliers', page_no=24, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('992268c7-97b4-4f00-90e2-72117fb06cc6'), chunk_index=194, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365282, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='using the SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing systems to continue business transactions and identify the business\ntransactions with qualified invoices to claim VAT returns.\nDuring invoice creation, the tax summarization of the taxes captured at the line level are displayed at the header\nlevel. Individual items in the invoice are grouped based on the tax type.', page_no=24, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ad5a25c3-aecf-44ae-8461-c82c64ca138e'), chunk_index=195, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365286, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='For example, in an invoice, the tax rate for the first two line items is SalesTax_8% and the tax rate for the next two\nline items is SalesTax_10. The tax summarization displays two header level tax lines for the four line items. Each line\nindicates the calculation based on each tax type.\nSuppliers who are registered with the Japanese tax authority will have a Tax Registration Number. The SAP Ariba', page_no=24, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('11b664d7-5c6b-4faa-9aa8-37bb9ead2657'), chunk_index=196, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365290, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Buying and Invoicing system qualifies a supplier as a qualified supplier if the Tax Registration Number is displayed\non the invoice. Ensure that you as a buyer update the supplier master data into the system.\nPrerequisite\n•\nBuyer Prerequisite\n•\nThe parameter EnableJapanConsumptionTax\n( Application.Procure.EnableJapanConsumptionTax ) must be set to Yes. This parameter is self-\nservice.\n•', page_no=24, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('aff0726a-2543-4d38-8fe7-801a09a43f2b'), chunk_index=197, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365293, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If you are using SAP ERP, then the tax codes used in the ERP system and SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing\nsystem must be the same. For more information, see SAP Note 3067001\n. If you are using additional\ntax codes in your ERP system based on the purchase to differentiate your purchases between a Qualified', page_no=24, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('92f7834b-eeef-4dbc-a782-e5aaf61889f7'), chunk_index=198, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365297, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Supplier and a nonqualified supplier, then you need to create a custom field named Qualified Supplier\nin SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing to switch tax code automatically based on the record existence/\nnon-existence in Supplier Tax Registration Number master and then you need to update the following\nconfiguration files into the system for transactions.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nContact your SAP Ariba administrator to import the configuration files.\n•', page_no=24, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('31a1b937-7542-4f8d-9ffb-4b72e4388589'), chunk_index=199, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365301, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='CurrencyInfo.csv, click here [page 27] to view a sample file.\n•\nTaxType.csv, click here [page 27] to view a sample file.\n•\nTaxTypeMap.csv, click here [page 28] to view a sample file.\n24\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoicing Process for Japan', page_no=24, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('eab12c00-a30b-4704-bda7-62b9889d4455'), chunk_index=200, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365396, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\nTaxCodeLookup.csv, click here [page 28] to view a sample file. You need to have one additional\ncustomization column in the TaxCodeLookUp file to identify the qualified supplier.\n•\nTaxCodeLookupFieldMapping.csv, click here [page 29] to view a sample file.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nIf you do not want to differentiate your transaction with a Qualified Supplier and a nonqualified supplier,\nyou do not need to update the configuration files.\n•', page_no=25, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3889b0a3-cafb-4b18-be9a-85524d80aab8'), chunk_index=201, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365400, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The tax type has unique tax rates. Ensure that the tax type and tax rates are preconfigured in the SAP Ariba\nBuying and Invoicing system.\n•\nYou must have a custom field created in the system to identify a qualified and a non-qualified supplier. For\nmore information, contact your SAP Customer Success Partner\nor you can create the custom field as\nmentioned below.\n\ue05c\xa0Note', page_no=25, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('691c1c14-83db-435d-af87-d4fa20f0ea0c'), chunk_index=202, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365404, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Incase of a non-qualified supplier, you do not need to create the custom field.\nFor documentation purpose, the custom field is named as Qualified Supplier. You can customize the name\nof the field as required.\n•\nSupplier GST ID - In a PO-FLIP scenario, the value of this field is copied from the invoice document\nsent from the supplier.', page_no=25, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9696ba5f-7bfc-44f3-9490-f198220a086f'), chunk_index=203, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365408, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="In ERS and paper invoice scenario, the value of this field is copied from the Supplier Tax Registration\nmaster data in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing. In this case, you can populate the supplier's Tax\nRegistration Number by selecting the supplier contact details. You can edit the value in this field only\nwhen using the paper invoice scenario.\nThe Supplier GST ID field is available under the\nHeader Information", page_no=25, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f1fe63e3-5238-499c-b2f5-2e8c6185a8c6'), chunk_index=204, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365412, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='GST Details\nsection\nof the invoice creation page once you enable the parameter EnableJapanConsumptionTax\n( Application.Procure.EnableJapanConsumptionTax ).\n•\nQualified Supplier - This custom field appears in all the line items. The system displays Yes if the\nsupplier Tax Registration Number exists in the SellerTaxRegistrationNumber field. Else, the system\ndisplays No.\nRestrictions\n•', page_no=25, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e6584793-1907-4c20-949e-3807a5b53b05'), chunk_index=205, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365416, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Ariba restricts adding different tax rates for the same tax type at the header level by default. Review the\nprerequisites to configure tax type and rate for header level usage.\nWorkflow of Invoices\nThe following description explains how the taxes are handled in the SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing system.\n•\nScenario 1 - Paper / Self-billing invoices', page_no=25, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('509af535-1acc-4650-a740-3fd12be0ad5f'), chunk_index=206, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365419, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='You need to copy all the tax details from the paper invoice into the system and then add the header level taxes\nmanually.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoicing Process for Japan\nPUBLIC\n25', page_no=25, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a524c216-f07e-4e34-bbaf-aec07aad2547'), chunk_index=207, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365460, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\nScenario 2 - ERS invoices\nThe system summarizes the tax calculations automatically at the header level and the taxes are group based\non the tax type.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nThe tax type have unique tax rates.\n•\nScenario 3 - Invoices originating from SAP Business Network\nThe summary of the taxes of a SAP Business Network invoice gets copied to header level taxes on the SAP', page_no=26, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('81abe754-60f4-4090-ab96-6fc0fca11682'), chunk_index=208, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365464, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Ariba Buying and Invoicing invoice.\nOverview of User Interface Changes\nOnce you enable the parameter EnableJapanConsumptionTax\n( Application.Procure.EnableJapanConsumptionTax ), the following fields are displayed:\n•\nSeller Tax Registration Number - Displays the Tax Registration Number of the supplier on the Requisition\ncreation page.\n•\nSupplier GST ID - Displays the Tax Registration Number of the supplier on the Invoice creation page under the\nHeader Information\nGST Details\nsection.\n26\nPUBLIC', page_no=26, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8b051b30-17f3-42a3-8359-251afbf4b6f9'), chunk_index=209, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365467, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoicing Process for Japan', page_no=26, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b70267db-b262-43e2-824f-f7657c787d4b'), chunk_index=210, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365515, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Contact your Designated Support Contacts (DSCs) to submit a ticket/case in SAP Ariba Connect or SAP for me\nto Ariba Product Support to make the Seller Tax Registration Number field visible on the line-item level of PR, PO,\nInvoice, and Invoice reconciliation documents. This field displays the Tax Registration Number copied from the', page_no=27, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a98f73f1-df98-4503-94f3-b7eccc660e1d'), chunk_index=211, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365519, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='supplier Tax Registration master data in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing system for ERS and on the invoice creation\npage. The Seller Tax Registration Number field will be overwritten by the Supplier GST ID value for Invoices created\nin SAP Business Network.\nRelated Links\n•\nTax Invoicing in Japan in SAP Business Network.\nSample Currency Information File\nThe following table lists the fields in the CurrencyInfo.csv file:\nAmountPrecision\nPricePrecision\nRounding', page_no=27, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cd2bd1cf-93ae-4853-a66a-8466eaf4396a'), chunk_index=212, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365522, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='TaxRounding\nCurrency\nPrecision\n0\n0\nROUNDFLOOR\nROUNDFLOOR\nJPY\n0\nSample Tax Type File\nThe table below describes the fields in the TaxType.csv file required to create tax components or to add taxes to\ninvoices. This file can be used for all variants.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoicing Process for Japan\nPUBLIC\n27', page_no=27, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('543f9b5a-8bf0-4f8a-ba23-da2fda35386d'), chunk_index=213, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365575, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='UniqueName\nName\nCategory\nSalesTax_8\nSalesTax 8 percent\n2\nSalesTax_10\nSalesTax 10 percent\n2\nSample Tax Type Map File\nThe table below describes the fields in the TaxTypeMap.csv file required to successfully exchange purchase orders\nand invoices between SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and SAP Business Network. This file can be used for all\nvariants.\nName\nTaxLineType\nSalesTax_8\nSalesTax_8\nSalesTax_10\nSalesTax_10\nSample Tax Code LookUps', page_no=28, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e9d7644a-a450-481d-a311-e5789998ed80'), chunk_index=214, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365579, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The table below describes the fields in the TaxCodeLookup.csv file required to import tax code lookups for Japan.\nAdditional customizable fields can be added to this file.\nCommodity-\nCode\nShipFrom-\nCountry\nShipToCoun-\ntry\nTaxCode-\nCountry\nTaxCode\nIsAccrual\nRank\ncus_Quali-\nfiedSupplier\n007\nJP\nJP\nJP\nV6\nNo\n1\nNo\n007\nJP\nJP\nJP\nJ2\nNo\n2\nYes\n017\nJP\nJP\nJP\nV6\nNo\n1\nNo\n017\nJP\nJP\nJP\nJ2\nNo', page_no=28, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6d14cfd6-c978-4805-995a-5a2151d63670'), chunk_index=215, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365583, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='2\nYes\nR1133\nJP\nJP\nJP\nV6\nNo\n1\nNo\nR1133\nJP\nJP\nJP\nJ2\nNo\n2\nYes\n004\nJP\nJP\nJP\nV2\nNo\n1\nNo\n004\nJP\nJP\nJP\nJ1\nNo\n2\nYes\n28\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoicing Process for Japan', page_no=28, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9234d423-5225-4a1a-9e7a-c18e38790f6b'), chunk_index=216, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365629, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Commodity-\nCode\nShipFrom-\nCountry\nShipToCoun-\ntry\nTaxCode-\nCountry\nTaxCode\nIsAccrual\nRank\ncus_Quali-\nfiedSupplier\n00105\nJP\nJP\nJP\nV2\nNo\n1\nNo\n00105\nJP\nJP\nJP\nJ1\nNo\n2\nYes\n00305\nJP\nJP\nJP\nV2\nNo\n1\nNo\n00305\nJP\nJP\nJP\nJ1\nNo\n2\nYes\n00707\nJP\nJP\nJP\nV2\nNo\n1\nNo\n00707\nJP\nJP\nJP\nJ1\nNo\n2\nYes\nSample Tax Code Lookup Field Map', page_no=29, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('09cf9161-6c87-4ab2-bbd2-a12cff80f085'), chunk_index=217, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365633, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The table below describes the fields in the TaxCodeLookupFieldMapping.csv file required to import tax code lookup\nfield maps. This file can be used for all ERP systems.\nFieldName\nDottedFieldPath\nLineItemType\ncus_QualifiedSupplier\ncus_QualifiedSupplier\nariba.purchasing.core.ReqLi\nneItem\ncus_QualifiedSupplier\ncus_QualifiedSupplier\nariba.invoicing.core.Invoic\neLineItem\ncus_QualifiedSupplier\ncus_QualifiedSupplier\nariba.invoicing.core.Invoic\neReconciliationLineItem\nSample Supplier Tax Registration Number File\nThe following table lists the fields in the SupplierTaxRegistration.csv file.\nCountry\nSupplier\nTaxRegistrationNumber\nJP\nSU_INTERNAL6932\nJPJWOODMAN926\nJP\n0000000101\nJPJCN9260R001', page_no=29, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('db8b1f77-1764-40b7-9a17-2bbf41393b2f'), chunk_index=218, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365637, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoicing Process for Japan\nPUBLIC\n29', page_no=29, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c06c3011-d3fe-49c4-a99a-8fcfee8243a1'), chunk_index=219, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365727, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Italy SDI Invoices\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice Management can be configured to allow Accounts Payable\n(AP) to edit Italy SDI invoices before the invoice reconciliation document is created. Authorized users can edit\ninvoice header details and can add items, allowances, charges, taxes and tax amounts, and withholding tax. In', page_no=30, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0616530c-7302-4a57-875f-9125a22428fc'), chunk_index=220, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365732, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="addition, to facilitate accounting, administrators can assign a default requester for SDI invoices that don't have one\nalready.\nMembers of the following groups can edit submitted SDI invoices: Invoice Administrator, Invoice Agent, Invoice\nEditor, Invoice Manager, Invoice Specialist.\nWorkflow for SDI Invoices [page 30]\nAdding an Approval Rule for SDI Invoices [page 31]\nWorkflow for SDI Invoices", page_no=30, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('86dfb3fb-b83a-45e4-bae6-92527f202380'), chunk_index=221, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365735, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="This high-level workflow for Italy SDI invoices starts with the supplier submitting the invoice and ends with the\ncreation of the invoice reconciliation (IR) document.\nThe workflow assumes the following:\n•\nThe administrator has configured a default requester for SDI invoices that don't have a requester specified.\n•\nThe invoice approval process routes invoices from Italy to approvers who can edit SDI invoices as needed.\n1.", page_no=30, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('09b0237a-8797-4b68-9476-25201101d5bf'), chunk_index=222, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365739, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The supplier from Italy submits an invoice to SDI.\n2. SDI sends the FatturaPA XML document to TrustWeaver, which converts it to cXML format.\n3. cXML document is sent to SAP Business Network.\n4. SAP Business Network sends the following:\n•\ncXML invoice that SAP Business Network received from Trust Weaver\n•\nThe FatturaPA XML invoice that SDI sent to TrustWeaver and TrustWeaver sent toSAP Business Network\n•', page_no=30, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9abd9714-7ad0-49a7-9580-17d40b6bbaad'), chunk_index=223, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365742, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The SDI delivery receipt\n•\nA PDF file of the invoice, generated in one of the following ways:\n•\nBy TrustWeaver, based on the FatturaPA XML that TrustWeaver received from SDI\n•\nBy SAP Business Network, based on the cXML that SAP Business Network received from TrustWeaver\n5. If no requester is specified, the invoicing solution adds a default requester, and adds the purchasing unit or', page_no=30, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ffbc96b1-ddcc-4dc3-b173-4e9a3f227aa6'), chunk_index=224, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365746, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='business unit based on the default requester.\n6. The invoicing solution routes the invoice to an approver who can edit invoices.\n7.\nThe approver opens the invoice, views the attachment, edits the invoice as needed, and submits the invoice.\n8. When the invoice is fully approved, an IR document is created.\n9. From this point onward, the invoicing process continues as usual.\n30\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide', page_no=30, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e71219e7-d94c-4e8f-a12e-397d3fb7025e'), chunk_index=225, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365750, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Italy SDI Invoices', page_no=30, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9558e8a2-dc3c-4790-a87f-6683e64117db'), chunk_index=226, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365790, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Related Information\nAdding an Approval Rule for SDI Invoices [page 31]\nAdding an Approval Rule for SDI Invoices\nYou can configure your invoice approval process to route SDI invoices to users who can edit them.\nPrerequisites\nMembers of the Customer Administrator or Invoice Administrator group can perform this task.\nContext\nYou add an approval rule with a Field Match condition based on the TaxInvoiceFormat field of the invoice.\nProcedure\n1.', page_no=31, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('621ae842-6997-4ecf-b657-bcf5fdba8d42'), chunk_index=227, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365794, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='From the dashboard, choose\nManage\nApproval Processes\n.\n2. Find the approval process for invoices, open it, and click Edit.\n3. Add an approval rule.\n4. In the Condition section, create a Field Match condition.\n5. Select the field to use.\nFor SDI invoices, use the Invoice.TaxInvoiceFormat field.\n6. Select the value to match.\nFor SDI invoices, enter FPR as the value to match.\n7.', page_no=31, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f2762d9b-130e-49af-90ef-0e8bb207072c'), chunk_index=228, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365798, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='In the Action section of the approval process editor, define the approvers to add for SDI invoices.\n8. Save, check in, and activate the approval process.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nItaly SDI Invoices\nPUBLIC\n31', page_no=31, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('dd3d07aa-5463-4b69-bb64-fda555b728b3'), chunk_index=229, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365891, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Evaluated Receipt Settlement and Automatic\nInvoicing\nThe evaluated receipt settlement (ERS) feature enables buyers to settle goods receipts without receiving invoices\nfrom suppliers. This helps to reduce invoice variances and close purchasing transactions more quickly.\nThis feature is supported in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing.\nThe ERS feature enables automatic creation of invoices after goods receipt transactions are fully approved. SAP', page_no=32, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('050ba486-e916-423d-9da1-cc63d36ae158'), chunk_index=230, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365896, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Ariba Buying and Invoicing creates invoices using the information on purchase orders, no-release order contracts,\nand goods receipts. This reduces invoice variances and makes the invoicing process more efficient by ensuring that\ninvoices are based on goods received.\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing also creates partial invoices if goods are received in batches. For example, if a', page_no=32, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('12fd8f96-1b24-4b6e-abbe-83a34811c923'), chunk_index=231, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365900, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='buyer ordered 15 items and received 10 items, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing creates an invoice for 10 items. SAP\nAriba Buying and Invoicing creates another invoice after the remaining five items are received at a later date. For\ntransactions pertaining to returned goods and receipt adjustments using negative quantities, SAP Ariba Buying\nand Invoicing creates credit memos.', page_no=32, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b2cdec04-8982-4cee-9171-3a7e32bd8f8d'), chunk_index=232, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365903, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When ERS is enabled for no-release order contracts, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing creates invoices for recurring\nand fixed fee payments for items, such as rents and advances on specific dates, based on the payment frequency\nand billing dates configured on the contracts. For details about ERS for no-release contracts, look for the topic\nabout automatic creation of contract-based invoices for evaluated receipt settlement, in the guide Managing\nContract Compliance.', page_no=32, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7274bb4c-cf85-4c26-a8ed-5b092d155480'), chunk_index=233, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365907, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='ERS is controlled by the site configuration parameter Generate invoices for evaluated receipt\nsettlement(Application.Procure.EnableERS) (enabled for self-service).\nContracts That Consist a Mix of ERS and Non-ERS Items\nYour site might allow users to create manual invoices for non-ERS items and automatic invoices for ERS items for\ncontracts that consist a mix of ERS and non-ERS items. This capability is controlled by a feature toggle that SAP\nAriba sets.', page_no=32, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d84c61bf-d324-4f79-b194-b7fbecf9de34'), chunk_index=234, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365911, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Source of Data for Automatically-Generated Invoices\nThe SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing generates invoices using the information in the following documents:\n•\nPurchase orders: The SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing inherits information, such as price, tax codes, charges,\nand payment terms, that are specified for line items on purchase orders. All taxes for invoices are generated', page_no=32, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6c634327-1a98-49de-887c-b34614130161'), chunk_index=235, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 365914, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='automatically from receipts that are based on taxes specified on the associated purchase orders. Allowances\nfor invoices that are generated automatically from receipts are also associated with the information on the\npurchase orders.\n32\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nEvaluated Receipt Settlement and Automatic Invoicing', page_no=32, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('62e84521-bfaf-4c0f-b65a-a3ec2eeaa122'), chunk_index=236, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366018, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\nNo-release order contracts: Similar to purchase orders, the SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing inherits\ninformation such as price, tax codes, and payment terms that are specified for each line item on the contract.\nIn addition, invoices for recurring and fixed fee payments are automatically created based on the pricing terms\nand dates that you schedule on the contracts.\n•', page_no=33, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5a2c5683-5fb4-4f5f-8ed9-c2ed4079646e'), chunk_index=237, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366022, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Goods receipts: The quantity value on the receipt is copied automatically to the invoice.\nEvaluated Receipt Settlement Workflow\nThe following is a high-level workflow for automatic creation of invoices when line items on purchase orders and\nno-release order contracts are marked for ERS transactions:\n1.\nA preparer creates a requisition or a contract request for items that need to be procured from ERS-approved\nsuppliers.', page_no=33, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('58a6862a-ccde-4433-a8f6-033015182a8d'), chunk_index=238, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366025, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='(For contract requests) The preparer configures the Fixed and Recurring Fees details to specify the date at\nwhich items are delivered and the frequency at which services are rendered.\n2. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing includes a member of the Purchasing Manager or the Contract Manager\ngroup as an approver in the approval flow.\n3. The Purchasing Manager or Contract Manager group approver performs the following actions:\n1.', page_no=33, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a0c14fcf-1998-4617-af65-5cee7de32cb1'), chunk_index=239, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366029, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='(For contract requests) Edits the details for fixed and recurring fee items to ensure that the Auto Invoice\nfield is set to Yes.\n2. Edits the details for each line item on the requisition or the contract request to ensure that the ERS\nAllowed field is set to Yes, and then approves the requisition or contract request.', page_no=33, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('90a504bc-0471-4873-894e-53e530c68fc0'), chunk_index=240, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366033, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='4. Other approvers identified in the approval flow approve the requisition or contract request.\n5. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing creates a purchase order or a no-release order contract.\n6. The supplier receives the order and ships the items to the buyer.\n7.\nThe buyer receives the items and approves the receipt transactions.\n8. (For material items) Depending on the quantity of items received, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing generates', page_no=33, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('961c2af6-872f-4abf-a644-f842b6ab4849'), chunk_index=241, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366036, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoices and credit memos with reference to the receipt:\n•\nIf items are fully received, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing automatically creates an invoice and the\ntransaction is passed for payment.\n•\nFor items received in batches, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing automatically creates separate invoices for\neach batch based on the accepted quantity of items, and the invoices are passed for payment.\n•', page_no=33, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('762f4fb3-8d41-43e1-8f60-9c7ce50620e2'), chunk_index=242, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366040, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='For line items on a receipt with negative values for the amount accepted, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing\nautomatically creates a line-item credit memo.\n9. (For fixed and recurring fee items on no-release order contracts) Depending on the frequency and billing\ndate specified on the contract, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing automatically creates an invoice for fixed and\nrecurring fee items on the scheduled date.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide', page_no=33, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('787de95e-4bca-4a7c-a950-1ead1270acce'), chunk_index=243, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366044, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Evaluated Receipt Settlement and Automatic Invoicing\nPUBLIC\n33', page_no=33, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b4f9b69a-d09b-438d-9f09-00fc1bbd5307'), chunk_index=244, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366123, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Non-PO Invoicing\nNon-PO invoices are invoices that are not based on a purchase order. If suppliers send paper invoices, invoice entry\nusers create electronic non-PO invoices in the SAP Ariba invoicing solution. If your business rules allow, suppliers\ncan also create non-PO invoices in SAP Business Network.\nUsers in your site create non-PO invoices by clicking\nCreate\nNon-PO Invoice\non the dashboard. SAP Ariba', page_no=34, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7412a9e9-278f-412f-8227-081183f2451d'), chunk_index=245, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366127, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoicing solutions always treat these invoices as non-PO invoices.\nSuppliers create non-PO invoices using the Create Non-PO Invoice task in their SAP Business Network accounts\nto submit an invoice through SAP Business Network. However, your SAP Ariba invoicing solution treats these\ninvoices as non-PO invoices or PO-based invoices depending on the values the supplier enters in the following\nfields:\n•\nSales Order # only: treated as a non-PO invoice\n•', page_no=34, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4f19584a-d280-4fd5-bf23-0f669aa09c41'), chunk_index=246, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366130, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Customer Order #:\n•\nTreated as a non-PO invoice if the value in the Customer Order # field does not match an existing\npurchase order on SAP Business Network.\n•\nTreated as a PO-based invoice if the value in the Customer Order # field matches an existing purchase\norder on SAP Business Network.\n•', page_no=34, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f4d5f95c-5fbc-42e8-bd46-37bcf55c5ad7'), chunk_index=247, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366134, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Contract # (valid or invalid): treated as a contract-based invoice. If the contract ID is invalid, the invoice\ntriggers an Invoice Unmatched exception.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nSAP Business Network requires suppliers to enter an email address (Sold To) only if they enter a value in the\nSales Order # field. If suppliers submit an invoice with an invalid Customer Order # value and without a valid', page_no=34, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9e932e90-7014-4b64-a039-95029c459e28'), chunk_index=248, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366138, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='email address, your SAP Ariba invoicing solution auto-rejects the invoice by default.\nIn analytical reports on invoices, when suppliers submit an invoice throughSAP Business Network with no specific\norder information (the Sales Order #, Customer Order #, and Contract # fields are all blank), that invoice has the\nInvoice Type of Non-PO. If the supplier submits an invoice with a Customer Order # value that does not match an', page_no=34, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7b3b2234-8f59-4222-b623-d71bdf72da19'), chunk_index=249, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366141, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='existing purchase order on SAP Business Network, that invoice has the Invoice Type of Customer Order.\n34\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoicing', page_no=34, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a8920b20-0e79-46c3-ba17-bcf7b02bf74f'), chunk_index=250, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366205, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="ERP Invoice Copies\nERP invoice copies are information-only copies of invoices that are processed and reconciled in an external ERP\nsystem, sent to SAP Business Network, and copied to SAP Ariba Invoice Management so that you can see all of\nyour company's invoicing activity in it.\nERP invoice copies are always information-only. The ERP system is always the source of truth for ERP invoice", page_no=35, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ca628755-9fc0-450e-ab0c-89c1482664c9'), chunk_index=251, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366209, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="copies, including status updates. They do not have any approval flows or reconciliation activities in SAP Ariba\nInvoice Management. However, by providing information about invoice activity in integrated ERP systems, they\nallow you to see and run reports on invoices across all of your company's invoicing activity in SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement. ERP invoice copies are matched to related contracts, purchase orders, and payments, which are", page_no=35, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1c8b4158-aa96-43d8-ae30-35b757cca0a8'), chunk_index=252, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366212, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="linked from the ERP invoice copy's Invoice page.\nERP invoice copies are automatically approved when they are received and are not editable. You can print and\nadd attachments and comments to ERP invoice copies and their corresponding invoice reconciliations. You cannot\nperform any other actions on them.\nYou can search for ERP invoice copies by choosing ERP Invoice Copy on the Invoice Origin Type search filter.\n\ue05c\xa0Note", page_no=35, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fad86984-55cf-4bcf-8ea5-f8f3eeebcb3c'), chunk_index=253, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366216, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Invoices from SAP Fieldglass are considered ERP invoice copies, but their origin type is Fieldglass Invoice\nCopy.\nYou can't copy ERP invoice copies (including SAP Fieldglass invoices) from search results. In addition, the invoice\npage for ERP invoice copies doesn't include the Copy button.\nIn analytical reports, the Invoice Origin Type field shows ERP Invoice Copy for ERP invoice copies and\nUnclassified for all other invoices.", page_no=35, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4cc440e0-c17f-42b5-85d6-1cce0dacf03c'), chunk_index=254, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366220, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nERP Invoice Copies\nPUBLIC\n35', page_no=35, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b9a4c2cd-2a66-4adb-af9a-baae7e2196c8'), chunk_index=255, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366277, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoice Cancellation by Suppliers\nSuppliers can request to cancel invoices that are sent through SAP Business Network.\nA cancel invoice request is an approvable document that changes the status of the corresponding invoice\nreconciliation document, the original invoice, and the payment request. Suppliers can submit cancel invoice\nrequests if the invoice is still in the process of being reconciled (the status of the corresponding invoice', page_no=36, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4659d145-7d8d-4011-a094-8190d044eb26'), chunk_index=256, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366281, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='reconciliation is Reconciling). They cannot cancel invoices that have already been reconciled (the status of the\ncorresponding invoice reconciliation is Reconciled).\nThe cancel invoice request, as an approvable document, must also go through an approval process; the invoice is\nnot canceled until approval of the request is final. During the approval process, the status of the original invoice', page_no=36, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('741903e6-0c55-49d7-8640-172ee2d93877'), chunk_index=257, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366284, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='document and the corresponding invoice reconciliation are both Canceling. If the cancel invoice request is finally\napproved, the invoice is successfully canceled, the associated invoice, IR, and payment request all change status to\nCanceled and all purchase order and contract accumulators associated with the original invoice are reversed. If the\ncancel invoice request is rejected, there is no change to invoice, invoice reconciliation, or payment request status', page_no=36, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2c6a9e9c-9714-452c-90c9-66c98c6c8f02'), chunk_index=258, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366289, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='or to accumulators, and the SAP Ariba invoicing solution sends an update to SAP Business Network so that the\ninvoice status there is no longer Canceled.\nRelated Information\nInvoice and Invoice Reconciliation Status Flow [page 95]\nCancellation of Approved Invoices in the ERP System\n36\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Cancellation by Suppliers', page_no=36, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c5354d73-9307-4ab4-b439-601c273a271f'), chunk_index=259, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366388, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Taxes on Invoices\nSAP Ariba invoicing solutions support indirect taxes and withholding taxes on invoices.\nIndirect and Withholding Taxes\nIndirect Taxes: Indirect taxes are taxes levied on goods or services, paid by the buyer to the supplier who in turn\npays them to the tax authorities. Examples of indirect taxes are Value Added Tax (VAT), sales tax, and excise duty.\nIndirect taxes are added to the invoice amount.', page_no=37, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4ae98c73-96d4-49fd-a433-76b9f4d15c14'), chunk_index=260, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366392, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Withholding Taxes: In certain countries/regions, withholding tax is required for self-employed suppliers and is\ngenerally paid by the buying organization to the state or federal government tax authorities on behalf of the\nsupplier. The tax percentage rate or tax amount must be entered as a negative number on invoices and a positive\nnumber on credit memos.', page_no=37, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2173741b-8679-473b-b147-95e22e4710d8'), chunk_index=261, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366396, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If an invoice contains indirect taxes and withholding taxes, the invoice summary displays the indirect tax amount\nand withholding tax amount separately; however, the total tax amount excludes withholding tax. The Payable to\nSupplier value is calculated by deducting the withholding tax amount from the gross amount of the invoice.\nTaxes on Invoices Received from SAP Business Network', page_no=37, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9a777cf9-c435-4708-8363-2c2e4f5a311b'), chunk_index=262, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366399, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When SAP Business Network sends an invoice containing taxes to the SAP Ariba invoicing solution, the tax types\napplied on the invoice in SAP Business Network are replaced by the tax types defined in the SAP Ariba invoicing\nsolution based on the tax type mappings defined. If a tax type on the invoice cannot be mapped to a tax type', page_no=37, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a9c630be-3757-4272-a518-50af100c4f02'), chunk_index=263, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366403, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='defined in the SAP Ariba invoicing solution, the tax type is set to a default tax type defined for the site.\nTaxes on Invoices Created in SAP Ariba Invoicing Solutions\nBy default, when you create a PO-based invoice in your SAP Ariba invoicing solution, the taxes on the purchase\norder are not copied to the invoice. You need to apply taxes on the invoice manually based on the paper invoice', page_no=37, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e746bdc9-87be-4f40-b51a-324530485427'), chunk_index=264, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366407, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='received from the supplier. SAP Ariba can configure your site to copy tax, charge, and discount information\nfrom the purchase order by enabling feature SINV-6818: PO-based defaulting of taxes, charges, and discounts on\nmanual invoices.\nYou can apply indirect and withholding taxes on invoices either at the header level or at the line-item level, but', page_no=37, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d7a286ad-f295-4cb9-bc78-904f45fee8ad'), chunk_index=265, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366410, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='not at both. For example, if you apply a withholding tax on the invoice at the header level, you cannot apply any\nwithholding taxes at the line-item level, but you can still apply indirect taxes at the line-item level.\nAt the header-level, you can apply taxes using only tax types. At the line-item level, you can apply taxes using both', page_no=37, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('81fe14f4-a8f8-4f7d-8807-954a69cdafc0'), chunk_index=266, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366414, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='tax types and tax codes, provided you use the same way of applying taxes for all line items; that is, you cannot apply\ntax types on some line items and tax codes on others. If you use tax codes, you can apply up to one indirect tax\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nTaxes on Invoices\nPUBLIC\n37', page_no=37, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d0504d08-b64b-4d1c-af04-632cc52783a1'), chunk_index=267, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366501, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='code and one withholding tax code on a line item. If you use tax types, though you can apply multiple tax types at\nthe header level or on a line item, you cannot apply the same tax type more than once. For withholding tax types,\nyou must specify a negative tax amount. This withholding tax amount is deducted from the invoice amount and', page_no=38, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2f7e871e-72bd-4166-b304-a74b4874db39'), chunk_index=268, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366505, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='tracked separately in the payment request generated for the invoice.\nWhen invoices are sent to SAP Business Network, the tax types on the invoices are replaced by the tax types used\nin SAP Business Network based on the tax type mappings defined.\nVAT Compliance and Support for 0% VAT Rate\nInvoices sent through SAP Business Network can contain VAT details at the header and line-item level. VAT', page_no=38, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('02144b38-359b-4c02-8202-1bc624adb971'), chunk_index=269, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366509, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='information is displayed in the VAT Details area of invoice headers and in line item details. Invoices that contain\nVAT taxes might be also be digitally signed. You can view digital signatures by clicking View Certificate in the\nheader.\nSuppliers who submit invoices on SAP Business Network can indicate that a VAT rate is zero rated or exempt', page_no=38, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('06b36a70-edee-4208-ba5a-6f009d7df9aa'), chunk_index=270, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366513, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='using the Exempt Detail field. Zero rated goods or services are taxable, but the tax rate is 0%. Exempt goods and\nservices are exempt from taxation.\nYour SAP Business Network buyer account administrator can make the Exempt Detail field mandatory or optional\nfor suppliers using the Require explanation for zero-rate VAT invoice rule in your SAP Business Network buyer', page_no=38, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('51a68931-7fa5-438b-8622-2c285940d39e'), chunk_index=271, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366516, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='account. When this rule is enabled, suppliers are forced to provide a reason for a 0% VAT rate. The Exempt Detail\nfield is not available for reporting.\nBuyer-Payable Taxes\nSAP Ariba uses the term buyer-payable tax for item taxes that the buyer pays directly to tax authorities. Depending\non the situation, buyer-payable taxes can also be referred to as direct-pay taxes, self-assessed taxes, or use taxes.', page_no=38, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cedc259d-48da-44ca-a94f-0639649f6dec'), chunk_index=272, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366520, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Buyers and suppliers typically have an understanding of the situations in which an item tax is a buyer-payable tax.\nOften, the buyer's ship-to location determines this. Suppliers don't usually invoice for taxes the buyer pays directly\nbecause buyers don't owe suppliers for them.\nOn sites using Enhanced third-party tax calculation for invoicing\n(Application.Procure.EnhancedTaxCalculationInExternalSystems), the tax calculation engine", page_no=38, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f860934d-493d-477b-a25f-16dc1fe1faaa'), chunk_index=273, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366523, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='determines whether a tax is a buyer-payable tax during invoice reconciliation. Buyers accrue buyer-payable taxes.\nFor details about buyer-payable taxes, see the Tax and Charge Configuration guide.\nRelated Information\nTax and Charge Exception Calculations [page 70]\nPO-Based Defaulting of Taxes, Charges, and Discounts on Manual Invoices [page 41]\nInvoices from SAP Central Invoice Management [page 61]\n38\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nTaxes on Invoices', page_no=38, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('000e994a-f95a-4160-9017-828c26de8272'), chunk_index=274, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366614, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Charges and Discounts on Invoices\nSAP Ariba invoicing solutions support charges and discounts on invoices at the header level as well as at the\nline-item level.\nCharges and Discounts on Invoices Received from SAP Business Network\nWhen an invoice containing charges is received from SAP Business Network, the charge types applied on the', page_no=39, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a9d28e2d-22db-46aa-98c9-43bb3e5e6ca1'), chunk_index=275, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366618, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoice are replaced by the charge types defined in the SAP Ariba invoicing solution based on the charge type\nmappings defined. If a charge type applied on the invoice is not mapped to any charge type in the SAP Ariba\ninvoicing solution, the default charge type Other Charges is used with the SAP Business Network charge type', page_no=39, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ef6e359f-2256-4fa1-a57b-7c21e4489d38'), chunk_index=276, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366622, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='appended to it. For example, if a charge of type Priority Delivery is applied on the invoice in SAP Business Network\nand this charge type is not mapped to any charge type in the SAP Ariba invoicing solution, then the charge type for\nthe charge is displayed as Other Charges - Priority Delivery.', page_no=39, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4a644b16-9beb-4186-b280-c6043de7b09a'), chunk_index=277, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366626, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Discounts are applied to invoices in SAP Business Network either as discounts or as allowances with type as\ndiscount. In both cases, the SAP Ariba invoicing solution consumes the applied discount as a discount. The SAP\nAriba invoicing solution rejects an invoice if multiple discounts or allowances are applied on a line item or at the\nheader level in an invoice.', page_no=39, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('90b076d5-f3d9-461e-ad1a-0e28140d8a11'), chunk_index=278, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366629, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Charges and Discounts on Invoices Created in SAP Ariba Invoicing Solutions\nBy default, when you create a PO-based invoice in your SAP Ariba invoicing solution, the charges and discounts\non the purchase order are not copied to the invoice and you need to apply them manually based on the paper\ninvoice received from the supplier. SAP Ariba can configure your site to copy tax, charge, and discount information', page_no=39, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('59cc344d-0e1c-44ff-8c3b-4b33ad34aabe'), chunk_index=279, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366633, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='from the purchase order by enabling feature SINV-6818: PO-based defaulting of taxes, charges, and discounts on\nmanual invoices.\nYou can apply charges on invoices using the standard shipping and handling charge types as well as the charge\ntypes defined by the customer administrator. You cannot apply the same charge type on the invoice at both the', page_no=39, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9ae7d070-0037-4b86-91c5-9744aa9f2bba'), chunk_index=280, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366637, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='header and line-item level. When invoices are sent to SAP Business Network, the charge types applied on the\ninvoices are replaced by the charge types used in SAP Business Network based on the charge type mappings\ndefined.\nYou can apply only one discount on an invoice at the header or on a line item. You must specify the discount as a\nnegative amount to deduct it from the invoice amount.', page_no=39, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ed3e38f3-ad57-43cc-afda-57c46631bc9d'), chunk_index=281, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366641, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Related Information\nPO-Based Defaulting of Taxes, Charges, and Discounts on Manual Invoices [page 41]\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nCharges and Discounts on Invoices\nPUBLIC\n39', page_no=39, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0a919522-1fc4-402a-b0e5-a7b92fa39e58'), chunk_index=282, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366646, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Allowances in Invoice Reconciliation Documents from Merged Sites\n40\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nCharges and Discounts on Invoices', page_no=40, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ffbf5102-73de-4f4b-98b3-97eecf5fd388'), chunk_index=283, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366732, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="PO-Based Defaulting of Taxes, Charges, and\nDiscounts on Manual Invoices\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing sites can include PO-based defaulting of tax, charge, and discount information.\nUsers entering invoices don't have to enter all tax, charge, and discount information manually.\nWith this feature, the tax, charge, and discount information for the line items is copied from the purchase order.", page_no=41, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('31ae3363-d0b5-4d2b-8e87-8a7d3204ab45'), chunk_index=284, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366737, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='To enable this feature, have your Designated Support Contact (DSC) submit a Service Request (SR). An SAP Ariba\nSupport representative will follow up to complete the request by turning on feature SINV-6818.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nThis feature pertains to invoices the buyer enters on behalf of a supplier. For PO-based invoices submitted by\nsuppliers, the behavior depends on how your SAP Business Network account is configured. A business rule you', page_no=41, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5bfd75bd-26ff-4ce7-98bb-d09ad163a403'), chunk_index=285, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366740, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='set in your SAP Business Network buyer account controls if tax information is copied from the order to the\ninvoice, or if suppliers must manually add taxes to the invoice. The name of that rule is Copy tax from purchase\norder to standard invoice.\nPrerequisites\nIs for sites that support adding taxes, charges, and discounting to requisitions and purchase orders. This capability', page_no=41, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9088819c-0d4c-4827-bbfe-f053bc723ea8'), chunk_index=286, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366744, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="is controlled by the site parameter Application.Procure.EnableTaxesChargesAndDiscount, which SAP\nAriba sets for you.\nRestrictions\n•\nThis feature doesn't apply to invoices for POs that include service lines.\n•\nThe charge type is copied from the PO to the invoice, but the default charge amount on the invoice is always 0.\nUsers fill it in manually.\nBasic Workflow\n1.\nA buyer user creates a requisition with tax, charge, and discount lines.", page_no=41, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d89d172e-6280-4eea-83eb-5b4ba877fe4e'), chunk_index=287, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366748, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='2. After the requisition is approved, the SAP Ariba solution creates the PO and sends it to the supplier.\n3. The supplier sends the goods and sends a paper invoice to the buyer.\n4. A buyer user creates a PO-based invoice on behalf of the supplier and selects the appropriate PO or POs.', page_no=41, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('71f35e03-61ef-4c52-8ba7-3a6ccb013092'), chunk_index=288, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366752, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5. The SAP Ariba solution copies the tax, charge, and discount information for each PO line onto the invoice:\n•\nTax lines, with tax code, tax component, and tax amount\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPO-Based Defaulting of Taxes, Charges, and Discounts on Manual Invoices\nPUBLIC\n41', page_no=41, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a741eaae-1c07-441d-aaad-66ecabd7124c'), chunk_index=289, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366805, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="•\nCharge lines, with charge type (for example, shipping) and an amount of 0 (zero)\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nThe buyer user fills in the charge amount on the invoice. It's not copied from the order.\n•\nDiscount lines, with the discount amount\n6. The buyer user edits the invoice as needed and submits the invoice.\nHow Defaulting Works When There Are Multiple Invoices (Partial Invoicing)\n•", page_no=42, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1b0a435e-22ef-45fa-aa1f-7f68c4f50224'), chunk_index=290, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366809, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Taxes: The default amount is based on the quantity remaining for the line item and the tax rate associated with\nthe tax code. "Quantity remaining" is the quantity that isn\'t already invoiced and reconciled.\n•\nDiscounts: The default amount is based on the discount amount remaining. "Amount remaining" is the amount\nthat isn\'t already invoiced and reconciled.\n•\nCharges: The default amount is always 0 on the invoice.', page_no=42, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2f31ec8d-ceff-479e-8029-1eb995f863df'), chunk_index=291, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366813, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='For example, a PO line item has the following quantity and tax, charge, and discount lines:\n1.\nA buyer user creates an invoice on behalf of the supplier and selects the PO.\n2. The tax and discount amounts are copied from the PO. The default charge amount on the invoice is $0 USD.\n3. The buyer user edits the tax, charge, and discount lines on the invoice as follows:\n42', page_no=42, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('47ae3996-1f96-44b5-88f4-cc92d5268414'), chunk_index=292, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366817, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='PUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPO-Based Defaulting of Taxes, Charges, and Discounts on Manual Invoices', page_no=42, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('993b3af5-f6bb-443a-94e4-ede83fb0b27c'), chunk_index=293, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366856, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='4. The buyer user fills in the rest of the invoice and submits it.\n5. The invoice lines are reconciled.\n6. A buyer user creates another invoice and adds the same PO.\n7.\nOn the new invoice, the default quantity and the default amounts for the tax, charge, and discount lines are as\nfollows:\n8. The buyer user fills in the rest of the invoice and submits it.', page_no=43, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5fadb01e-a391-4d09-a2c1-bbac1a02acf4'), chunk_index=294, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366860, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="What if POs Change Before the Invoice Is Submitted?\nWhen a manual invoice is still in Composing state, and an associated PO changes, the taxes, charges, and\ndiscounts on the invoice are not updated automatically. Any manual edits made on the invoice are preserved.\nIf a user creates an invoice but doesn't submit it right away, they can choose the PO again on the Invoice Entry", page_no=43, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3da74ffb-b411-468c-af14-5121b3e82d9c'), chunk_index=295, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366864, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='page. The latest values are copied from the PO to the invoice, replacing existing values. This ensures that the tax,\ncharge, and discount information is in sync with the latest PO.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPO-Based Defaulting of Taxes, Charges, and Discounts on Manual Invoices\nPUBLIC\n43', page_no=43, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ef6f8a67-8329-4aba-ba07-3dd876402045'), chunk_index=296, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366914, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Price-Adjustment Debits and Credits\nBuyers can reconcile line-item price adjustments from suppliers. Buyers can also enter price-adjustment debit and\ncredit memos on behalf of suppliers.\nA price adjustment results in a line-level debit memo or line-item credit memo against the original invoice. The\nline-item quantity on a price adjustment is the same as the line-item quantity on the original invoice.', page_no=44, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f30d9464-035e-4738-9d89-03d7aab74878'), chunk_index=297, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366918, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="In SAP ERP, price adjustments are represented as subsequent debits and subsequent credits.\nType of price adjustment\nInvoice Type\nPrice reduction\nLine-Item Credit Memo\nPrice increase\nLine-Item Debit Memo\nOnce the price adjustment from the supplier is reconciled and approved in the SAP Ariba solution (often with no\nintervention from the buyer), it's sent to the external ERP system.\nFigure 1: Example: Price-Adjustment Credit Memo", page_no=44, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e769e956-9903-438a-9ead-0697af959902'), chunk_index=298, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366922, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice Management support matching and exception handling for\nprice-adjustment debit and credit memos.\nThe workflow supports all types of invoice lines on PO-based invoices, non-PO invoices, and contract-based\ninvoices.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nSAP ERP doesn't support price adjustments for non-PO or contract-based invoices. Price-adjustment\ndocuments in SAP ERP (referred to as subsequent debits and credits) are always against purchase orders.\n44\nPUBLIC", page_no=44, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('43a694d5-3ee8-4a7e-9833-8ed133b174a1'), chunk_index=299, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 366926, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPrice-Adjustment Debits and Credits', page_no=44, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8fa3c3c2-00ca-4baa-85c5-c49fd948670e'), chunk_index=300, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367002, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="In reporting:\n•\nReports for invoices and invoice reconciliation documents include a Price Adjustment field for line-item debit\nmemos and line-item credit memos to indicate whether they're price adjustments.\n•\nReports for invoices and invoice reconciliation documents include an Invoice Purpose field, which shows the\ninvoice document type (standard, credit memo, line-item credit memo, or line-item debit memo).\nPrerequisites", page_no=45, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2bf493ce-86a1-43f0-a64e-9038cb1b9c21'), chunk_index=301, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367006, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='To allow suppliers to submit price-adjustment credit memos and debit memos through SAP Business Network, in\nyour SAP Business Network account, check the following General Invoice Rules on the Default Transaction Rules\npage:\n•\nAllow suppliers to send line-item credit memo\n•\nPrice Adjustment\n•\nAllow suppliers to send line-item debit memo\n•\nPrice Adjustment', page_no=45, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0eb2be52-0cbb-410d-9d84-0a05f726857c'), chunk_index=302, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367010, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Buyers and suppliers that use their own cXML-enabled applications must upgrade to cXML 1.2.034 or later to\nsupport attributes added to the cXML standard.\nIntegration with External ERP Systems\nIn order for the ERP system to process the documents as price adjustments, it must be configured to process the\nprice adjustment indicator and invoice type information included in the document.', page_no=45, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a70bff6b-6a2b-4491-bef7-02678767af4d'), chunk_index=303, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367013, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Integration with external ERPs other than SAP ERP requires custom work.\nBuyers integrated with SAP ERP using SAP Business Suite Add-On for SAP Business Network integration must\nhave release SP15 or later.\nBuyers integrated with SAP ERP using SAP Ariba Cloud Integration Gateway must have SAP Ariba Cloud\nIntegration Gateway release 2018.09 or later for support of price-adjustment debits and credits.\nIf your external ERP system is SAP ERP:\n•', page_no=45, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e4d72609-caa8-4eb8-91e0-1c94cf7b4ebf'), chunk_index=304, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367017, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This feature works with existing adapters without additional mapping.\n•\nPrice-adjustment debit memos become subsequent debits in the ERP system, and price-adjustment credit\nmemos become subsequent credits.\n•\nPrice adjustments are supported for PO-based invoices only.\nInvoicing Workflow for Price-Adjustment Debits and Credits [page 46]\nEnablement of Price Adjustment Debits and Credits [page 48]\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPrice-Adjustment Debits and Credits\nPUBLIC\n45', page_no=45, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('864cb198-2034-483f-bceb-216903d0cf5a'), chunk_index=305, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367023, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing Workflow for Price-Adjustment Debits and\nCredits\nThis diagram shows a high-level workflow for price-adjustment debit and credit memos. More detailed steps follow.\nFigure 2: High-Level Workflow for Price-Adjustment Debit Memos and Price-Adjustment Credit Memos\n46\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPrice-Adjustment Debits and Credits', page_no=46, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('be806a22-baef-4841-959e-91487cb3ea6c'), chunk_index=306, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367153, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='1.\nAfter sending an invoice, the supplier realizes the price of one of the items needs to be adjusted.\n2. The supplier creates one of the following against a line in the original invoice:\n•\nFor a reduction in the price of an item, a line-item credit memo marked as a price adjustment\n•', page_no=47, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('418609d2-4d5b-46eb-992a-3ddb09e2ce89'), chunk_index=307, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367157, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='For an increase in the price of an item, a line-item debit memo marked as a price adjustment\nThe supplier specifies the change in price, not the new price.\n•\nFor price-adjustment credit memos, the change in price is a negative number because the price is reduced.\n•\nFor price-adjustment debit memos, the change in price is a positive number.', page_no=47, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3f11ce17-7cc1-4377-a0c4-25b18aa27dfc'), chunk_index=308, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367161, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The quantity for the item is the same as the invoiced quantity. The SAP Ariba solution applies the price\nadjustment to the full quantity of the invoiced item.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nBuyers can enter price-adjustment debit and credit memos in cases where the supplier sends a paper-\nbased price adjustment.\n3. Upon receiving the price-adjustment debit or credit memo, the SAP Ariba solution creates an invoice', page_no=47, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('90e8bf33-f96a-463e-b2e3-d50d769e549c'), chunk_index=309, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367165, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='reconciliation document for the price adjustment.\n4. The SAP Ariba solution checks the status of the original invoice.\n•\nIf the IR for the original invoice has a status of Paying, Paid, or Paying Failed, the price-adjustment debit\nor credit memo is reconciled. Amount accumulators are updated on the order and contract (and on the\ngoods receipt in sites that use goods receipt-based invoice verification).', page_no=47, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('10c7e700-7e72-44e1-83a6-3ef3b16ae79e'), chunk_index=310, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367169, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Price-adjustment credit memos are automatically approved. Exceptions might be raised on a price-\nadjustment debit memo. Price-adjustment debit memos are automatically approved as long as the change\nin price doesn't raise a price exception.\n•\nIf the IR for the original invoice does not have a status of Paying, Paid, or Paying Failed, an exception", page_no=47, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('632eb143-af22-40ef-abc2-f815d0482d0c'), chunk_index=311, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367172, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='is raised on the price-adjustment debit or credit memo to prevent it from being sent to the ERP system\nbefore the ERP system receives the invoice. This exception can be cleared in two ways: by approving the\noriginal invoice or by rejecting the price-adjustment debit or credit memo.\nIf the original invoice is in Reconciling status, it’s re-reconciled based on the change in price. Previously', page_no=47, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d17baa17-b4ce-447f-b601-a21b2c464cf9'), chunk_index=312, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367176, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='existing price exceptions might be cleared as a result of a price-adjustment credit memo.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nFor line-item credit memos, individual lines are accumulated even if the Credit Memo References\nUnapproved Invoice Reconciliation exception is raised, because the exception occurs at the header\nlevel, not the line level. This makes it possible for lines on the credit memo to clear exceptions on the', page_no=47, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ce649ce8-a764-4bf2-90b1-4a52973ac67d'), chunk_index=313, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367180, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="original IR. For example, suppose an IR has a price variance exception, and a line-item credit memo\nbrings the price down within the tolerance. In this case, the exception on the original invoice is cleared\neven though the credit memo won't be fully processed until the ERP system receives the invoice.\n5. Ariba sends the price-adjustment debit or credit memo to the external ERP system.\n\ue05c\xa0Note", page_no=47, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1355ccac-3c51-4bb6-bc60-849eed61e670'), chunk_index=314, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367184, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="If your external ERP system is SAP ERP, this feature works with existing adapters without additional\nmapping. Price-adjustment debit memos become subsequent debits. Price-adjustment credit memos\nbecome subsequent credits. Subsequent debits and credits in SAP are always against purchase orders.\nTherefore, you can't use price adjustments for non-PO invoices and contract invoices if your external ERP\nsystem is SAP ERP.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPrice-Adjustment Debits and Credits\nPUBLIC", page_no=47, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('043180a0-4503-40e1-9575-0e4f40b68750'), chunk_index=315, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367187, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='47', page_no=47, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('96b60f75-9ea8-45e4-a34d-b349bf69f7de'), chunk_index=316, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367264, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Prices Used in Reconciling Invoice Documents\nThe following table describes the prices used in reconciling the invoice documents involved with price adjustments.\nInvoice document type\nPrice used for reconciliation\nOriginal invoice\nPrice of line item on original invoice + price-adjustment credit\nThis facilitates clearning of price exceptions on the original\ninvoice. For example:\nPrice on the order = $10\nTolerance = 10%', page_no=48, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('00fcf125-a818-4198-a579-870173f762f1'), chunk_index=317, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367268, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Price on the invoice = $12, more than tolerance allows, excep-\ntion raised on invoice\nPrice-adjustment credit = -$1, exception is cleared because $11\nis within tolerance\nPrice-adjustment credit\nThe value in the Price Change field\nPrice-adjustment debit\nPrice of line item on original invoice + line-item debit\nFor example:\nPrice on the order = $10\nPrice on the invoice = $10\nPrice tolerance = 10%\nPrice-adjustment debit = $2', page_no=48, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cd49f140-fb74-4b9d-9813-87ec2f293949'), chunk_index=318, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367272, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Price adjustment price = $12, more than tolerance allows\nPrice exception is raised on price-adjustment debit memo\nDisputing Price Variance Exceptions\nDisputing price variance exceptions doesn't consider price adjustments. The flow works differently from how some\nusers expect it to. For example, suppose:\n•\nThe price on the PO is 10 USD.\n•\nThe price on the invoice is 13 USD.\n•", page_no=48, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6efb1675-4ba6-4054-94ea-20424292a433'), chunk_index=319, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367276, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A line-item credit memo has a price adjustment of -2 USD.\nIn this scenario, the original IR had a PO price variance (with the setting Field Path To Validate set to\nPriceIncludingReferencedInvoiceAdjustments) because the expected price = 10 USD and the invoice\nprice = 11 USD (13 USD minus 2 USD). If a user disputes the exception and chooses Accept Expected Price, the', page_no=48, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fdbbb098-5b32-44f9-b97b-74c7da951866'), chunk_index=320, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367279, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="price is set to 10 USD. The price-adjustment credit memo isn't considered.\nEnablement of Price Adjustment Debits and Credits\nSome of the functionality for this feature is controlled by site configuration parameters.\n48\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPrice-Adjustment Debits and Credits", page_no=48, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fe66d862-28a1-4e82-85c8-14d52cf874d8'), chunk_index=321, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367370, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\nSelf-service parameters can be changed by your administrator in Ariba Administrator under\nIntelligent\nConfiguration Manager\nManage Configurations\n.\n•\nParameters and other options that are not self-service are set by SAP Ariba and require a case to be submitted.\nTo enable price adjustment debits and credits, set the following parameter to Yes:\nApplication.Invoicing.EnableLineItemPriceAdjustmentInvoices (enabled for self-service)\nSpecifies whether the invoicing solution accepts and reconciles price-adjustment line-', page_no=49, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('52b712a1-6a1f-4810-8097-3558c2b5b4ee'), chunk_index=322, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367374, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='item credit memos and line-item debit memos from SAP Business Network. In addition,\nspecifies whether buyers can manually enter line-item price-adjustment invoices. When this\nparameter is enabled, users entering line-item credit memos can choose between a price\nadjustment and a quantity adjustment.\nTo support reconciliation of price-adjustment credit memos, the following parameter must be set to No:\nApplication.Invoicing.SkipLineCreditMemoExceptions (set by SAP Ariba Support)', page_no=49, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3b561dee-93ac-4019-94c3-54d784f138de'), chunk_index=323, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367377, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This legacy parameter specifies whether line-level credit memos raise exceptions during\ninvoice reconciliation. Administrators can now configure this functionality themselves in the\nInvoice Exception Types UI. To fully enable customer configuration:\n•\nSet Application.Invoicing.LineCreditMemoExceptions to No.\n•\nAdd all categories to\nApplication.Invoicing.LineCreditMemoExceptionLineCategories.\n•\nConfigure the desired behavior in the Invoice Exception Types UI in Ariba\nAdministrator.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nWhen Application.Invoicing.SkipLineCreditMemoExceptions is set to No, customer administrators', page_no=49, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('67c7c7a2-5d53-4e82-b917-0884389a6207'), chunk_index=324, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367381, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='can still prevent specific exceptions on line-item credit memos by using the Apply to Specific Invoice Types\nfield of the exception type.\nTo prevent people from accepting a price-adjustment debit or credit when the original invoice\nhas not been approved, add the exception types CreditMemoReferencesUnapprovedInvoice and\nDebitMemoReferencesUnapprovedInvoice to the following parameter:\nApplication.Invoicing.DisallowAcceptOnExceptionTypes (enabled for self-service)\nThis parameter removes the Accept Invoice option from the Action menu in the invoice', page_no=49, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a8d457cb-c233-4929-a864-7ae2cf91e330'), chunk_index=325, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367385, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='reconciliation user interface for the invoice exception types you specify in a comma-\nseparated list. Enter the exact unique name of the invoice exception types for which to\nremove the Accept Invoice option on the Action menu. Example: POPriceVariance.\nBy removing the option to accept the information provided by suppliers on their invoices\nfor certain invoice exception, you can enforce that you only pay for what was ordered. Note', page_no=49, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cccd7a21-6f4d-416c-bccb-82006a2665a9'), chunk_index=326, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367389, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='that certain geographies require that invoices are paid in full or rejected if there are possible\ninvoice errors.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPrice-Adjustment Debits and Credits\nPUBLIC\n49', page_no=49, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bcffe8bf-3b20-41b8-b637-89422e12dd17'), chunk_index=327, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367438, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Non-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing sites integrated with SAP ERP support one-time vendor invoices.\nBuyers sometimes make one-time purchases from suppliers that aren't in their established list of suppliers. For\nexample:\n•\nA department manager might purchase a cake from a local baker or rent bicycles for a team outing.\n•", page_no=50, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f809b007-de38-4340-8b65-e5db31fad86e'), chunk_index=328, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367442, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="A buyer might use a temporary supplier if the usual supplier can't provide the required goods.\nWith one-time vendor support, when a supplier sends the invoice for such a one-time purchase, Accounts Payable\n(AP) can enter and process the non-PO invoice without adding a new supplier record to their master data. All the\npayment information is stored directly on the invoice.", page_no=50, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2089c578-0d59-4ec4-8a91-03377b9d0d1a'), chunk_index=329, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367446, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="This feature is for non-PO invoices entered by the buyer's AP department and for paper invoices converted via\nthe buyer's invoice conversion service (also known as SAP Ariba Open ICS). The feature is supported on sites\nintegrated with SAP ERP.\nFor information about configuring your site to support one-time vendor invoices, see Non-PO Invoices for One-Time\nVendors in Invoicing Data Import and Administration Guide.", page_no=50, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a9314fb4-cb68-4162-bb7e-073da45aef86'), chunk_index=330, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367449, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Workflows for One-Time Vendor Non-PO Invoices [page 51]\nOne-Time Vendors in SAP Ariba Solutions [page 57]\n50\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors', page_no=50, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f9dcc05c-5c95-498a-9efb-49834bd7975f'), chunk_index=331, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367455, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Workflows for One-Time Vendor Non-PO Invoices\nThe following diagrams and steps explain the process for one-time vendor, non-PO invoices either entered by the\nbuyer or sent from a buyer's invoice conversion service (SAP Ariba Open ICS).\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors\nPUBLIC\n51", page_no=51, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3fa42a2b-f908-46d8-a3f7-c9367e60bd7d'), chunk_index=332, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367460, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Figure 3: Typical One-Time Vendor Invoice Flow\n52\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors', page_no=52, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('60152b2e-7308-4e4e-be68-744fce93e8ce'), chunk_index=333, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367577, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Workflow for Invoices Entered by the Buyer\n1.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group works with SAP Ariba to configure the site to support\none-time vendor, non-PO invoices.\nThis includes configuring the one-time vendor, adding users to a group that allows editing of payment\ninformation on an invoice, modifying the invoice approval process, and working with SAP Ariba to determine', page_no=53, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a1272cf9-2cb5-467b-9cbe-9281e7814a4e'), chunk_index=334, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367581, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='which fields are used for supplier validation and which fields are mandatory for each payment method.\n2. A user creates a non-PO invoice and selects the one-time vendor option, which allows the user to fill in the\nsupplier information.\nThe user can enter payment information if authorized to do so.\n3. The user submits the invoice for approval.\n4. The SAP Ariba solution validates the invoice, checking the following:\n•', page_no=53, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('eb27c834-01df-4e14-a569-83f49449e486'), chunk_index=335, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367585, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Whether the maximum number of invoices allowed has already been reached for the specified supplier\n•\nWhether supplier information or payment information on the invoice has been used for previous one-time\nvendor invoices, and if so, whether the specified supplier name is consistent with the name on previous\ninvoices\n•\nWhether the supplier invoice number has already been used for the specified supplier', page_no=53, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('dd19539f-34ba-4273-8cf9-bfd4f878f638'), chunk_index=336, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367588, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="5. When invoice submission is complete, the approval flow is generated.\n6. If the user who created the invoice didn't enter payment information, an approver in the appropriate group\ndoes so and resubmits the invoice. Then, the SAP Ariba solution validates whether supplier or payment\ninformation on the invoice has been used for previous one-time vendor invoices, and if so, whether the", page_no=53, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5cfce3d3-bed9-4255-9a0e-4bcc5519b3e9'), chunk_index=337, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367592, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='specified supplier name is consistent with the name on previous invoices.\n7.\nThe invoice is approved.\n8. The invoice reconciliation (IR) document is created.\n9. The IR document is reconciled and approved.\n10. In SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing, a payment request is created and exported to the ERP system for payment.\nExported payment requests include the supplier and payment information.', page_no=53, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d729bb8b-ddc1-496b-8585-764cd9ad5730'), chunk_index=338, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367596, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='11. The ERP system receives the payment information and pays the supplier.\n12. The ERP system sends remittance information to SAP Ariba.\nWorkflow for ICS Invoices\n1.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group configures the site to support one-time vendor, non-PO\ninvoices. This includes configuring the one-time vendor, adding users to a group that allows editing of payment\ninformation on an invoice, and modifying the invoice approval process.', page_no=53, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('89f6b435-422b-42bf-9fd3-785b1e03f4bd'), chunk_index=339, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367600, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='2. The buyer informs the ICS provider about the one-time vendor invoice process and gives the ICS provider the\nnecessary information (one-time vendor IDs, cXML information).\n3. ICS provider receives paper invoice from supplier, creates cXML invoice, and sends it to SAP Business Network.\n4. SAP Business Network matches the invoice to the correct one-time vendor and sends the invoice to the SAP\nAriba solution.', page_no=53, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2dce8d64-d391-43d0-bdda-95ff2c616231'), chunk_index=340, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367603, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5. The SAP Ariba solution validates the invoice, checking the following:\n•\nWhether the maximum number of invoices allowed has already been reached for the specified supplier\n•\nWhether supplier or payment information on the invoice has been used for previous one-time vendor\ninvoices, and if so, whether the specified supplier name is consistent with the name on previous invoices\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors', page_no=53, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('46095c7d-fbb9-4c5e-8cc6-4f6668efb098'), chunk_index=341, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367607, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='PUBLIC\n53', page_no=53, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1f717865-adeb-4210-948c-2be5e862a95a'), chunk_index=342, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367667, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="•\nWhether the supplier invoice number has already been used for the specified supplier\n6. If the invoice has validation errors, the status becomes Submitted With Errors, and it's routed to the invoice\nconversion specialist. The invoice conversion specialist corrects any errors.\n7.\nThe invoice is approved and continues through the flow in the same way as a paper invoice.\nExamples", page_no=54, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7831f414-c2df-4cb2-be40-1035cc683433'), chunk_index=343, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367671, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="The examples in this section are based on the following setup.\nSupplier configuration:\n•\nOne-time vendor name: One-off Expenses\n•\nUnique identifier for suppliers on one-time vendor invoices: supplier VAT ID.\n•\nMaximum number of invoices per supplier: 2. Additional invoices display a warning.\nUser configuration:\n•\nThree invoice entry users: A, B, and C.\nUser A can't add payment information to a one-time vendor invoice.", page_no=54, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ef6f5d06-b70b-4304-bbe5-8092f50ac989'), chunk_index=344, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367675, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Users B and C can add payment information to a one-time vendor invoice.\n•\nOne invoice conversion specialist to resolve ICS invoice errors: C (also an invoice entry user).\n•\nOne invoice manager: D.\nApproval process configuration:\n•\nAn approval rule for one-time vendor invoices adds members of the group Edit One Time Vendor Invoice\nPayment Information if the preparer isn't authorized to enter payment information.\n•", page_no=54, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5db74c75-4bf7-4c3e-b923-0db3ca1c5273'), chunk_index=345, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367678, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='An approval rule for one-time vendor invoices adds the Invoice Manager group for invoices with a total amount\nof $500 USD or more.\n•\nAn approval rule adds the invoice conversion specialist for ICS invoices with a status of Submitted With Errors.\n54\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors', page_no=54, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0b182979-fbf4-4df0-971b-3f889808ffdb'), chunk_index=346, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367701, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Example: Basic Paper Invoice\n1.\nUser A creates invoice 01 for supplier Bakery Z with VAT ID DE123456789 without specifying payment\ninformation. The invoice amount is $300 USD.\n2. The invoice is routed to user B for payment information and approval.\n3. User B opens invoice 01, adds payment information, and approves the invoice.\n4. Invoice 01 is fully approved, and the resulting IR document is approved.', page_no=55, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8ab0f113-7542-4a03-ac4b-251f14c51f11'), chunk_index=347, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367705, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5. Payment information is sent to the ERP system, which pays the supplier.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors\nPUBLIC\n55', page_no=55, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a963b758-cd5e-4339-af0b-d4a8973581e1'), chunk_index=348, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367736, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Example: ICS Invoice\n1.\nICS provider sends invoice 02 via ICS cXML for supplier Bakery W with the same VAT ID as in invoice 01. The\ninvoice amount is $250 USD.\n2. Because the VAT ID is the same as with invoice 01 but the supplier name is different, the invoice is routed to\nuser C (invoice conversion specialist) to check the supplier name.', page_no=56, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6013b04a-80da-4922-b7a3-b4d242e27d0d'), chunk_index=349, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367741, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3. User C opens the invoice 02 and sees a message that a previously submitted invoice has the same supplier ID\ninformation but a different name.\n4. User C changes the name to Bakery Z and approves invoice 02.\n5. Invoice 01 is fully approved, and the resulting IR document is approved.\n6. Payment information is sent to the ERP system, which pays the supplier.\n56\nPUBLIC', page_no=56, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5c0ce27f-539d-453a-b52c-58cbfd876bbe'), chunk_index=350, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367744, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors', page_no=56, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b5628d33-ca7f-44f0-bc28-186f99fcd5e1'), chunk_index=351, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367800, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Example: Paper Invoice That Exceeds the Maximum Number of Invoices Allowed\n1.\nUser A creates invoice 03 for Bakery Z with VAT ID DE123456789. The invoice amount is $600.\n2. User A receives a warning that the maximum number of invoices has been exceeded for the specified VAT ID.\n3. User A submits the invoice.\n4. Invoice 03 is routed to user B for payment information and approval.', page_no=57, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('24d3d77f-330f-4271-b37c-0d1125f6a089'), chunk_index=352, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367804, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5. User B opens invoice 03, adds payment information, and approves invoice 03.\n6. Invoice 03 is routed to user D (invoice manager) for approval due to the large amount.\n7.\nUser D approves the invoice.\n8. Invoice 03 is fully approved, and the resulting IR document is approved.\n9. Payment information is sent to the ERP system, which pays the supplier.\nOne-Time Vendors in SAP Ariba Solutions', page_no=57, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cf3fe09e-0372-459c-af65-780c43f44a7f'), chunk_index=353, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367808, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='In SAP Ariba solutions, a one-time vendor is a special type of supplier record. It\'s for a group of suppliers with\nwhom you conduct business only once or rarely.\nThe typical process for one-time vendor invoices is to have a type of vendor record specifically for one-time\nvendor invoices (for example, a vendor record called "One-time Expenses," or several vendors for different types', page_no=57, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ab5f528e-22b1-4b3a-a6fd-bb7d1144e0ad'), chunk_index=354, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367812, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='of expenses, such as "Catering" and "Charitable Donations"). A one-time vendor record represents an account\nfrom which the ERP system pays one-time vendor invoices. When the invoice entry user creates an invoice and\nchecks the one-time vendor option, additional fields let the user choose the type of one-time vendor and enter the\nactual supplier name and payment information. The supplier and payment information is used for payments and', page_no=57, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('985a7dac-cb27-487a-9268-2743af822008'), chunk_index=355, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367815, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors\nPUBLIC\n57', page_no=57, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a5f50777-1426-4569-bcf5-1fbd4904b29b'), chunk_index=356, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367849, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="remittances as well as reporting, and the invoice is registered against the one-time vendor record. The invoice can\nthen be routed for approval if required.\nFigure 4: One-Time Vendor Invoices and Payments\nIn SAP Ariba, one-time vendors don't reference supplier-specific master data such as supplier name and payment\ninformation. Instead, users enter the supplier details directly on the invoice.", page_no=58, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('da09dc00-02f1-41a9-b642-1e4862e0ee51'), chunk_index=357, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367853, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="The one-time vendor record contains an ID that enables invoices to be routed to the appropriate one-time vendor\naccount in your ERP system. One-time vendors are not actual suppliers. The suppliers aren't aware that the buyer\nis processing their invoices using SAP Ariba. They're just sending invoices and getting paid.\nThe ERP system, SAP Business Network, and SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing must all have corresponding one-", page_no=58, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('46060d84-eeda-4647-b58f-3671c40c6e2d'), chunk_index=358, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367857, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='time vendor information for one-time vendor invoices and payments to flow correctly.\n58\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors', page_no=58, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a40997b5-da69-456a-94bc-aa91ca3acb57'), chunk_index=359, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367903, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Supplier export from SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing includes one-time vendor records.\nTable 1: Regular Suppliers Versus the Individual Suppliers Listed on One-Time Vendor Invoices\nRegular supplier\nSupplier on one-time vendor invoice\nA record for the supplier exists in the\nbuyer's ERP system master data and\nSAP Ariba solution as part of master data\nYes\nNo\nBuyer's SAP Business Network account\nhas a record for the supplier\nYes\nNo", page_no=59, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c9ab7b88-4f9c-451d-b06a-d276a40a8566'), chunk_index=360, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367907, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Buyer has an SAP Business Network\ntrading relationship with the supplier\nYes\nNo\nSuppliers can be notified automatically\nwhen invoices are rejected\nYes\nNo\nPayment information (for example, Remit\nTo addresses, bank information) is mas-\nter data associated with the supplier\nYes\nNo\nPayment information for the supplier ex-\nists only on the invoice.\nPayment information is included in pay-\nment exports from the SAP Ariba solu-', page_no=59, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('438f88aa-b5b7-4af7-bd3a-46442ff646d2'), chunk_index=361, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367911, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='tion so the ERP system can pay the sup-\nplier\nYes\nPayment information comes from the\nsupplier record.\nYes\nPayment information comes from the in-\nvoice fields.\nInvoice information can be included in re-\nports\nYes\nYes\nRelated Information\nConfiguration Overview for One-Time Vendor Invoicing\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors\nPUBLIC\n59', page_no=59, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f78be372-1f98-40f6-b5b8-0a61b9814166'), chunk_index=362, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 367916, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Configuring a One-Time Vendor in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing\nConfiguring SAP Business Network to Support One-Time Vendor ICS Invoices\n60\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nNon-PO Invoices for One-Time Vendors', page_no=60, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('109ee159-2a76-4596-8ffd-272947ead2d6'), chunk_index=363, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368002, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoices from SAP Central Invoice Management\nIf your SAP Ariba site is integrated with SAP Central Invoice Management, you can receive and process invoices\nfrom SAP Central Invoice Management.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nFor information about how to integrate an SAP Ariba site with SAP Central Invoice Management, see the SAP\nCentral Invoice Management documentation on the SAP Help Portal.\nWorkflow\n1.', page_no=61, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('24a93d7a-d834-42a4-85ac-027265e7c3f0'), chunk_index=364, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368007, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="An invoice is created in SAP Central Invoice Management through an upload or from an email.\n2. Invoice invoice goes through the document information extraction process in SAP Central Invoice\nManagement.\n3. The invoice is sent to the SAP Ariba solution using an API. (The invoice doesn't go through the tax and account\ndetermination process in SAP Central Invoice Management.)\n\ue05c\xa0Note", page_no=61, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3ac08940-77cb-42eb-88c5-408b0d1f3ab1'), chunk_index=365, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368010, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="The API used in this scenario is an internal SAP Ariba API called the Invoice Management API.\n4. A corresponding invoice is created in the SAP Ariba solution based on the invoice data received.\nLine items are created as non-catalog items.\nIf errors occur when the invoice is created, they're listed on the History tab with Invoice API Error in the Action\ncolumn.", page_no=61, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('83ce8057-1d08-4eb7-a168-8fb0fc0c6a27'), chunk_index=366, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368014, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5. Additional data is filled in based on site configuration parameters, defaulting options, and supplier matching.\n6. The invoice is submitted and has a status as follows:\n•\nIf there are no validation errors, the invoice has a status of Submitted.\n•\nIf the invoice has invalid or missing data based on the requirements of the SAP Ariba site, the status is\nSubmitted with Errors.\n7.', page_no=61, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9c9ed4ef-1105-454e-ae07-f99531f5da30'), chunk_index=367, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368018, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The invoice, when opened, shows a message informing the user that the invoice was generated automatically\nand suggesting a verification of the information.\nThe Invoice Submission Method field contains either Uploaded or Email.\n8. The invoice goes through the approval flow. Authorized users compare the invoice with the information in the\nattached image or invoice file, updating the invoice as needed.\nTax Calculation', page_no=61, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('58a7c0a3-8a3a-4ecc-a4af-30003fe1ce61'), chunk_index=368, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368021, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Keep the following in mind regarding invoices from SAP Central Invoice Management:\n•\nInvoices from SAP Central Invoice Management don't include a field for the taxable amount in the information\nsent by the API. In the SAP Ariba solution, the tax amount is calculated in based on line item amount.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoices from SAP Central Invoice Management\nPUBLIC\n61", page_no=61, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b659e9f9-6788-4aad-a9cd-5945ef5dc72c'), chunk_index=369, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368109, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="This differs from the way taxes are calculated in SAP Central Invoice Management, where the tax amount is\ncalculated based on the tax percentage of the taxable amount.\n•\nOn invoices from SAP Central Invoice Management header-level taxes aren't reflected at the line level as they\nare with regular SAP Ariba invoices.\nApproval Process", page_no=62, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c471c164-cd68-44fb-a3b2-e69723976b6a'), chunk_index=370, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368113, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='We recommend that you update your invoice approval process to add an approver for invoices from SAP Central\nInvoice Management. The approver can compare the electronic invoice with the invoice attachment and ensure\nthat the tax type and other fields are correct. For information, see Creating an Approval Rule for Invoices from SAP\nCentral Invoice Management [page 63].\nConfiguration Options\nWe recommend setting the following parameters:\n•', page_no=62, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1d1e4f88-1661-4e5f-b3c5-73ead861cfbf'), chunk_index=371, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368117, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Specify a user in the parameter Default requester for invoices from invoice API\n(Application.Invoicing.InvoiceAPI.DefaultRequesterUniqueName). Requester information isn't\nextracted in the document information extraction process in SAP Central Invoice Management. Configuring\na default requester can help with auto-filling accounting information on the invoice.\n•\nSet a default commodity code for noncatalog line items using the parameter Commodity code for noncatalog\ninvoice line items (Application.Invoicing.InvoiceCreationDefaultLineItemCommodityCode).\n•", page_no=62, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5521eb69-5822-4949-8276-7e754f3f10a2'), chunk_index=372, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368121, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Set the parameter Application.Approvable.MaxAttachmentSize to at least 20 MB.\nInvoices sent from SAP Central Invoice Management to SAP Ariba have a maximum size of 20 MB.\nThis parameter is controlled by SAP Ariba. Setting it requires submitting case (service request) to SAP Ariba\nSupport.\n•\nMake sure Application.Invoicing.ViewableInvoiceAttachmentExtensions includes all the formats\nsupported in SAP Central Invoice Management: PDF, PNG, JPEG, and TIFF.', page_no=62, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('22650848-998f-4461-88ed-d75fe88ef763'), chunk_index=373, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368124, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter is controlled by SAP Ariba. Setting it requires submitting a case (service request) to SAP Ariba\nSupport.\n•\nIf your site uses the advanced currency precision and rounding feature, consider aligning\nyour site with the precision and rounding used in SAP Central Invoice Management. Currency\nprecision and rounding are controlled by the Enable advanced currency precision and rounding\n(Application.Base.AdvancedCurrencyPrecisionHandling).', page_no=62, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('dbaa0418-b025-40b7-98b3-6d76b10c189d'), chunk_index=374, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368128, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="The following parameter doesn't apply to invoices from SAP Central Invoice Management:\nApplication.Invoicing.EnableTaxesOnShippingAndHandlingItems (set by SAP Ariba Support).\nRestrictions\n•\nPO-based invoices aren't supported. PO-based invoices from SAP Central Invoice Management are treated as\nnon-PO invoices in the SAP Ariba solution.\n62\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoices from SAP Central Invoice Management", page_no=62, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7a999505-71e0-4616-ab79-a4a00a0f8a03'), chunk_index=375, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368189, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="•\nCredit memos aren't supported. Credit memos from SAP Central Invoice Management are treated as regular\ninvoices (with negative amounts) in the SAP Ariba solution.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nIn SAP Central Invoice Management, credit memos uploaded with a negative amount show a positive\namount when viewed in the Manage Supplier Invoices Centrally app. When you view the corresponding", page_no=63, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('72858f41-62eb-4ce9-8010-3fdb8d2b067a'), chunk_index=376, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368193, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoices in the SAP Ariba solution, they have negative amounts. The discrepancy between positive and\nnegative amounts is noted on the History tab.\nRelated Information\nAdvanced Currency Precision and Rounding\nCreating an Approval Rule for Invoices from SAP Central Invoice Management [page 63]\nDefault Requester for Invoices from Invoice API [page 116]\nCommodity code for non-catalog invoice line items [page 114]\nCreating an Approval Rule for Invoices from SAP', page_no=63, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('173c34dd-bac1-4c9b-a532-e94a920d686b'), chunk_index=377, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368197, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Central Invoice Management\nYou can add an approver for invoices loaded from another system into your SAP Ariba solution by an internal\ninvoice management API, for example, invoices from SAP Central Invoice Management. Approvers can compare\nthe newly created electronic invoice with the invoice image and ensure that the tax type and other fields are\ncorrect.\nPrerequisites', page_no=63, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3ec1f0ad-f2a2-4d1d-ad9f-e29c345e9249'), chunk_index=378, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368200, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Members of the Customer Administrator or Invoicing Administrator group can manage approval processes for\ninvoicing.\nThis procedure assumes you're familiar with managing approval processes.\nContext\nWith invoices from other systems, it's especially important for the approver to check and update the tax type. Tax\ntypes differ from one system to another. Also, some information can change due to the defaulting configured in the\nSAP Ariba site.", page_no=63, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b4794696-c710-4f8a-8b91-cd142c716bd1'), chunk_index=379, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368204, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoices from SAP Central Invoice Management\nPUBLIC\n63', page_no=63, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3b714431-d1a8-4fe3-bd9c-5ed347f76570'), chunk_index=380, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368277, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='\ue05c\xa0Note\nThe API used in this scenario is an internal SAP Ariba API called the Invoice Management API.\nProcedure\n1.\nChoose\nManage\nApproval Processes\n.\n2. Find and open the approval process you want to edit, and choose Edit in the approval process editor.\n3. In the Approval Process Diagram section, add an approval rule, filling in a rule title and description.', page_no=64, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6d367389-8241-40fe-8977-72cb8db91eb0'), chunk_index=381, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368281, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='4. In the Condition section, add a Field Match condition.\n5. Choose\nSelect\nSelect Field\n.\nThe Select Field popup opens.\n6. Scroll to find one of the following fields, and click Select for the field you want to use:\nOption\nDescription\nLoadedFrom\nTo define an approver to handle all invoices from SAP Central\nInvoice Management.\nInvoiceSubmissionMethod\nTo define separate approvers based on how the invoice was', page_no=64, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a6a34855-e023-4ffd-a936-051345f281b1'), chunk_index=382, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368285, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='created in SAP Central Invoice Management, that is, whether\nthe invoice came from an email or from an upload.\n7.\nFrom the second Select button, choose Select Value.\n8. In the Value field, enter one of the following.\n•\nIf your condition is based on the LoadedFrom field, enter 11.\nThe value 11 represents invoices that were uploaded by the API.\n•', page_no=64, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d2338373-69cc-4b9e-81fd-122863eafea8'), chunk_index=383, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368288, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If your condition is based on the InvoiceSubmissionMethod field, enter Upload or Email.\nEnter Upload for invoices uploaded into SAP Central Invoice Management:\nOr enter Email for invoices created in SAP Central Invoice Management from an emailed invoice:\n9. (Optional) To apply the rule only to invoices with validation errors, in the Condition section, add another Field\nMatch condition.\na. Select the HasValidationError field.', page_no=64, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f12eaabf-897d-498b-97b2-4e8847c35a1b'), chunk_index=384, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368292, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='b. From the second Select button, choose Select Value.\n64\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoices from SAP Central Invoice Management', page_no=64, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6acecdfa-7474-4d75-b6fa-901512c4c199'), chunk_index=385, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368298, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='c. In the Value window, select True.\nThe following example shows a condition to capture invoices that were loaded using the API and have at least\none validation error.\n10. Add an action for the approval rule.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoices from SAP Central Invoice Management\nPUBLIC\n65', page_no=65, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b2cad63b-2530-4129-90b4-b493ed420b60'), chunk_index=386, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368357, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Invoice Reconciliation Processes\nHere's a list of topics that provide overviews of various processes related to invoice reconciliation.\nAutomatic Reconciliation [page 66]\nRe-Reconciliation [page 68]\nAuto-Reconciliation of Invoices When Full Credit Is Received [page 69]\nTwo-Way Invoice Matching in SAP Ariba Invoice Management [page 69]\nTax and Charge Exception Calculations [page 70]\nSupplier Bank Details Processing [page 72]\nGoods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification [page 74]\nAutomatic Reconciliation", page_no=66, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('45b6b590-fc4d-4091-9bb2-7342c3611129'), chunk_index=387, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368361, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Automatic reconciliation determines whether an invoice is automatically accepted, automatically rejected, or\nrouted to exception handlers and approvers for further processing.\nYour SAP Ariba invoicing solution automatically reconciles invoices as the first part of the reconciliation process.\nAutomatic reconciliation consists of the following steps:\nStep 1: Match\nThe matching process links each invoice reconciliation document (IR) to one or more orders or contracts and links', page_no=66, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('45c60755-7ddf-49a2-80e1-7c1e87fc4ae0'), chunk_index=388, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368364, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='each item on the IR to one or more line items on those orders or contracts.\nStep 2: Determine Whether to Validate or Skip\nThe automatic reconciliation process determines whether the validation of the IR can be skipped. Validation is\nskipped if the total amount of the invoice is below a specified threshold amount. In the default configuration, the', page_no=66, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('dd7f1503-89ab-48a3-bcbc-040b6a1e114c'), chunk_index=389, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368368, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='skip amount is set to 5, which represents an amount in the default currency for your site.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nThe skip amount does not apply to credit memos. Your site might also be configured to skip exceptions in\nline-level credit memos entirely.\n66\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes', page_no=66, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a8b17768-bb37-4949-b622-6652ec120827'), chunk_index=390, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368452, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Step 3: Validate\nInvoices that are not skipped during Step 2 are validated. During validation, invoice line item and amount values\nare compared to the corresponding line item and amount values on the associated purchase order or contract (or\nthe receipt, in the case of goods receipt-based invoice verification), and discrepancies trigger invoice exceptions.', page_no=67, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3d164d62-6a2b-4990-9d12-e5f4997b927a'), chunk_index=391, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368456, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="The approval rules for IRs configured in your site are executed to draw an approval graph and route the IR to the\nappropriate exception handlers and approvers.\nStep 4: Determine Whether to Auto-Accept\nInvoices are automatically accepted if the header amount is less than a specified threshold amount or less than\na specified percentage of the original order. Auto-accepted invoices are automatically reconciled, and your site's", page_no=67, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5605520b-0c24-4e3a-b022-21f10447eda3'), chunk_index=392, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368460, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="auto-acceptance configuration is based on your organization's business processes and policies for allocating\nresources to manually reconcile invoices that meet certain criteria for importance. In the default configuration,\nthe auto-accept amount is set to 10, which represents an amount in the default currency for your site, and the\nauto-accept percentage is set to 15.", page_no=67, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a6e92b27-27f5-45a0-b949-97dc11587d34'), chunk_index=393, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368464, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='For example, suppose you have a $100 purchase order that has not yet been invoiced, and an IR for $11, which\nrepresents slightly more than 9% of the order amount. Since the auto-accept percentage is 15%, the invoice is\nautomatically reconciled.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nCredit memos are never considered for auto-acceptance.\nStep 5: Determine Whether to Auto-Reject', page_no=67, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('17993f15-389a-4812-b6bd-49e747a5639e'), chunk_index=394, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368468, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoices are automatically rejected if an invoice exception is triggered which is defined for automatic rejection. For\nexample, in the default configuration, the Invalid Invoice Date exception causes an invoice to be auto-rejected. An\nInvalid Invoice Date exception is triggered if the invoice date is earlier than the associated purchase order date.\nAuto-rejected invoices are sent back to the supplier with the status Rejected. Suppliers on SAP Business Network', page_no=67, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f855e904-0bd7-4716-a4cd-507334c295c7'), chunk_index=395, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368471, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="can resubmit rejected invoices there after correcting errors. Depending on your site's configuration, resubmitted\ninvoices might use the same invoice number of a new unique invoice number. Resubmitted invoices re-enter the\ninvoicing process at the beginning.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nCredit memos are never considered for auto-rejection.\nIf your site supports invoice rejection reason codes, for auto-rejected invoices, the rejection reason code is set to\nAutoRejection.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide", page_no=67, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9f629b56-743f-436e-89f6-85c56865ba6b'), chunk_index=396, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368475, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoice Reconciliation Processes\nPUBLIC\n67', page_no=67, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('69fa9ac1-71a0-406d-8719-fa3feb483f75'), chunk_index=397, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368561, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Step 6: Notify Exception Handlers/Approvers\nIf the invoice is not auto-rejected, the IR enters the approval process configured for your site. IRs show a status\nof Reconciling until they are fully reconciled. Your site's approval rules determine whether or not the IR requires\nmanual approval, even if no exceptions are raised. They also determine which exception handlers are assigned to\nmanually resolve different types of exceptions.\nRelated Information", page_no=68, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3b9a092b-1044-4049-9d23-e240131e9bcd'), chunk_index=398, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368565, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Re-Reconciliation [page 68]\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Reconciling Invoices [page 119]\nRe-Reconciliation\nRe-reconciliation updates an invoice reconciliation (IR) document whenever you receive against an outstanding\norder or contract.\nUnless your site is configured to prohibit re-reconciliation (determined by site configuration parameters that SAP\nAriba sets), IR documents are automatically re-reconciled whenever you receive against an outstanding order or', page_no=68, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('946f2133-1e35-4e73-891f-dfc86302f4fe'), chunk_index=399, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368569, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="contract. An order or contract might have hundreds of unreconciled IRs; re-reconciliation allows to automatically\nupdate those IRs to clear exceptions as new data comes in so that invoice handlers only have to resolve exceptions\nthat are valid at the time of reconciliation.\nUpdates to reconciled accumulators don't trigger re-reconciliation of IRs.\nUpdates to invoice exception types don't trigger automatic re-reconciliation, either. Members of the Invoice", page_no=68, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0dc24048-88c6-430f-b6b9-b4b807d00cd8'), chunk_index=400, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368573, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Adminstrator and Customer Adminstrator groups can manually re-reconcile an invoice against the latest invoice\nexception types using the Update Exceptions button.\nThe following example demonstrates the re-reconciliation process:\n1.\nAn order contains one line item with a quantity of 100.\n2. The supplier creates an invoice (INV-1) against the order with a quantity of 20. No receipts have been submitted\nyet.', page_no=68, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ae068491-827a-4b66-8687-176bca7958da'), chunk_index=401, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368576, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="3. The supplier creates a second invoice (INV-2) with a quantity of 30.\nAt this point, both IR documents have the following PO Received Quantity Variance exceptions:\n•\nINV-1 shows PO Received Quantity Variance - The invoice item's quantity, 20, is greater than the order\nitem's received quantity, 0.\n•\nINV-2 shows PO Received Quantity Variance - The invoice item's quantity, 30, is greater than the order", page_no=68, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4463b1c6-438d-4094-9faf-077fc2fe7d01'), chunk_index=402, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368580, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="item's received quantity, 0.\n4. 21 items are received against the order, which causes re-reconciliation of the two IR documents associated with\nthe order.\nNow, both IRs have the following updated PO Received Quantity Variance exceptions:\n•\nINV-1 shows the PO Received Quantity Variance exception as cleared.\n68\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes", page_no=68, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0b3fb4db-348d-4e17-9936-8f95d9c67ea3'), chunk_index=403, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368661, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="•\nINV-2 shows PO Received Quantity Variance - The invoice item's quantity, 30, is greater than the order\nitem's received quantity, 21.\nIf your site does not allow re-reconciliation, the original exceptions in Step 3 of the example continue to show on the\nIRs even as more items are received against the order.\nRelated Information\nAutomatic Reconciliation [page 66]\nAuto-Reconciliation of Invoices When Full Credit Is Received [page 69]", page_no=69, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5299d0b6-9cbd-4012-a556-539641c93521'), chunk_index=404, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368666, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Auto-Reconciliation of Invoices When Full Credit Is\nReceived\nIf you receive a line-item credit memo for the full quantity of an invoice, any exceptions on the IR document are\naccepted automatically.\nThis is because line-item credit memos for the full invoiced quantity serve the purpose of reversing the invoice.\nAutomatically accepting the exceptions on the IR document prevents users from having to resolve them manually.', page_no=69, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8113c1cf-25e5-4d40-bfa2-35225669f9f7'), chunk_index=405, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368669, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Only a single line-item credit memo fully reverses invoice. If two line-item credit memos are received for the same\ninvoice, and the second line-item credit memo has a credited quantity that is the full quantity of the invoice, any\nexceptions on the invoice must be resolved manually.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nIf the Ignore Auto Accept option is enabled for an invoice exception type, exceptions of that type are not', page_no=69, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0b880cda-31d1-4daa-977e-e66b76f12437'), chunk_index=406, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368673, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='accepted automatically, even if a line-item credit memo for the invoiced quantity is received.\nTwo-Way Invoice Matching in SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement\nTwo-way matching between invoices and purchase orders allows you to reconcile invoices for items that do not\nrequire a receipt.\nThe default matching in invoice reconciliation is between invoice, purchase order, and receipt. However, many', page_no=69, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c6346004-bd9f-4739-b3f5-b9028d152772'), chunk_index=407, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368677, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='ERPs allow a two-way match between invoices and associated orders for line items that do not require a receipt.\nThese ERP systems typically include an indicator on purchase order lines that specifies whether or not receiving is\nrequired for those lines (in SAP ERP, the indicator is the GR Based IV check box).', page_no=69, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9e6b647d-3bd7-4423-96cf-eeeddaac729f'), chunk_index=408, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368680, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="If you want to use two-way matching, your site must be configured to map the ReceivingType extrinsic in the\ncXML OrderRequest document to the Purchase Order page in your site. If a line item's ReceivingType is set to\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes\nPUBLIC\n69", page_no=69, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c442003f-384a-4925-8ae8-55fbd27db6cc'), chunk_index=409, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368774, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="4, it does not require a receipt and the invoice can be reconciled with two-way matching to the order only. If a line\nitem's ReceivingType is set to any value other than 4, including a blank, it requires a receipt and reconciliation\nrequires three-way matching between invoice, purchase order, and receipt.", page_no=70, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c795eb54-15b9-448c-95d4-a2765b389230'), chunk_index=410, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368778, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='On the Order Details page for purchase order lines with ReceivingType set to 4, the Receipt Required field is set\nto No.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nSome ERP systems indicate whether or not a receipt is required at the header level rather than the line level.\nIf this is the case for your integrated ERP system, the custom mapping of ReceivingType to the Purchase', page_no=70, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f25d3100-abea-42fd-ac15-643e5eadad2e'), chunk_index=411, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368782, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Order page in your site must include a way to set the receipt required indicator at the line level in keeping with\nyour company's business practices and needs.\nTax and Charge Exception Calculations\nInvoice tax exceptions are generated in the invoice reconciliation document in the following cases:\n•\nTax amounts specified on the purchase order and invoice do not match.\n•", page_no=70, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('40254ac3-d399-4d17-bc19-18a351a27db5'), chunk_index=412, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368785, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The tax amounts on the invoice do not match the tax amounts calculated using the tax tables and tax code\nlookup.\n•\nThe tax amount on the invoice is a buyer-payable tax. This case\napplies only to sites using Enhanced third-party tax calculation for invoicing\n(Application.Procure.EnableTaxCalculationInExternalSystems).\nTax Exceptions for Indirect Taxes\nTwo invoice exception types are used to capture variances in the tax amounts of purchase orders and invoices. The', page_no=70, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('12e14964-9d3a-4b40-9cfa-d4330a6c7cc6'), chunk_index=413, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368789, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='PO Tax Amount Variance invoice exception type captures the variances in the header-level tax amounts, while the\nPO Line Tax Amount Variance invoice exception type captures the variances in the line-level tax amounts. You can\nonly accept the invoice tax amounts to resolve these exceptions. These invoice exception types are available only in\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing.', page_no=70, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7ce2bc54-db69-49d9-be0d-0872038ffc3f'), chunk_index=414, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368793, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The Under Tax Variance and Over Tax Variance invoice exception types capture variances in the tax amounts\nspecified on invoices and those calculated using the tax tables. These invoice exception types validate the amounts\nagainst tolerances defined in your configuration.\nThe Tax Calculation Failed invoice exception type flags cases where the system cannot calculate the applicable', page_no=70, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7ebd5ef0-ef83-42af-9977-9692451a840a'), chunk_index=415, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368796, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='taxes based on the tax code lookup and tax tables. This invoice exception type validates the amounts against\ntolerances defined in your configuration. Exceptions use a percentage tolerance. Absolute tolerances are not\nappropriate for this exception type.\n70\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes', page_no=70, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d0eac6f1-6258-44aa-acd6-cbc62f0db02f'), chunk_index=416, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368879, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Tax Exceptions for Withholding Taxes\nTax exceptions for withholding taxes are generated only when the withholding tax amount on the invoice does not\nmatch the calculated withholding tax amount.\nThe Withholding Tax - Under Tax Variance and Withholding Tax - Over Tax Variance invoice exception types\ncapture variances in the withholding tax amounts specified in invoices and those calculated using the tax tables.', page_no=71, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('740cb46a-99cf-46e8-96af-3d531cfeac44'), chunk_index=417, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368883, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The Withholding Tax Calculation Failed invoice exception type flags cases where the system cannot calculate the\nwithholding tax based on the tax code lookup and tax tables. To resolve the Withholding Tax Calculation Failed\nexception, you need to update your tax code lookup and recalculate taxes on the invoice reconciliation document. If', page_no=71, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('63be31a8-e840-4a77-a0a8-1be2769bdba6'), chunk_index=418, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368886, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='the tax code lookup has the correct tax data, it means that a withholding tax is not applicable on the invoice. in such\ncases, you can reject the invoice reconciliation. These invoice exception types are available in SAP Ariba Buying and\nInvoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\nAs withholding taxes are entered as negative numbers on invoices, the system considers their absolute amounts', page_no=71, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('830639e2-39d5-479d-ab8d-2a755ea5cc48'), chunk_index=419, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368890, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='when calculating tax variance exceptions. For example, if the withholding tax amount specified on an invoice is -20\nand the expected tax amount is -30, the Withholding Tax - Under Tax Variance exception is generated.\nWithholding taxes are calculated at either the header level or the line-item level as explained in the table below.\nInvoice has withholding taxes at...\nWithholding taxes are auto-generated in invoice reconcilia-\ntion at...\nHeader level', page_no=71, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d524b99d-337a-4943-8887-69c96c981df8'), chunk_index=420, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368893, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Header level\nLine-item level\nLine-item level\nNeither\nHeader or line-item level based on a site configuration parame-\nter\nBuyer-Payable Tax Exceptions\nThe Buyer Payable Tax exception applies only to sites using Enhanced third-party tax calculation for invoicing\n(Application.Procure.EnhancedTaxCalculationInExternalSystems). The exception means that the\nthird-party tax calculation engine marked the tax as a buyer-payable tax.', page_no=71, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7ab8fc67-327d-41f3-bc97-7052a13d3397'), chunk_index=421, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368897, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Buyer-payable taxes are tax lines the buyer pays directly to tax authorities rather than paying the supplier. The\namount owed to the supplier is 0. The calculated buyer-payable tax is accrued.\nFor more information, see the Tax and Charge Configuration topics.\nCharge Exceptions\nCharge exceptions are generated in invoice reconciliation documents when the charge amounts specified on\npurchase orders and invoices do not match.', page_no=71, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('34fa3fe6-8427-498c-ac25-5c71d53208d8'), chunk_index=422, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368901, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Two invoice exception types are used to capture variances in the charge amounts of purchase orders and invoices.\nThe PO Charge Amount Variance invoice exception type captures the variances in the header-level charge\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes\nPUBLIC\n71', page_no=71, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e27cf64c-7f33-488e-b719-2e007d076cdf'), chunk_index=423, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368995, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='amounts, while the PO Line Charge Amount Variance invoice exception type captures the variances in the\nline-level charge amounts. You can only accept the invoice charge amounts to resolve these exceptions. These\ninvoice exception types are available only in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing.\nRelated Information\nTaxes on Invoices [page 37]\nCharges and Discounts on Invoices [page 39]\nSupplier Bank Details Processing', page_no=72, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ac075b07-8c5b-46c4-9b71-f4ffcff1ddcd'), chunk_index=424, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 368999, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Suppliers can send updated bank details in cXML invoices over the SAP Business Network to your SAP\nAriba invoicing solution. Your site can be configured to receive these details and process them during invoice\nreconciliation. The details can also be included in approved and reconciled invoices transmitted to SAP Business\nNetwork.\nTo configure this functionality for you site, have your Designated Support Contact (DSC) log a Service', page_no=72, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3874fb5e-8a48-46a2-ad1a-86364513150e'), chunk_index=425, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369002, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Request (SR). SAP Ariba Support will follow up to complete the request by setting the parameter\nApplication.Invoicing.SupportSupplierBankInfoOnInvoices.\nThe following bank details can be processed in your SAP Ariba solution:\n•\nBank ID Type\n•\nBank ID\n•\nBank Account ID\n•\nBank Account Type\n•\nIBAN\n•\nBranch Name\n•\nAccount Name', page_no=72, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('44bfd0b7-46aa-49b0-bed5-e0ff5369095c'), chunk_index=426, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369006, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='By default, the same bank details that are received in the incoming cXML invoices are included in the outgoing\nreconciled invoices. However, if a user edits the remittance location during the invoice reconciliation process, then\nthe bank details associated with the selected remittance location (if available in the SAP Ariba solution) take\nprecedence and are updated in the outgoing invoices. If bank details associated with the selected remittance', page_no=72, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1345fef3-b0cd-4377-b7eb-e8d916ec9e27'), chunk_index=427, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369009, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='location are not available, then no bank details are included in the outgoing reconciled invoices.\nThis feature helps the SAP Ariba solution find the correct remittance location. Following are more details about the\nprocessing of bank details if Application.Invoicing.SupportSupplierBankInfoOnInvoices\xa0is set to Yes:\n•\nIf the supplier SAP Business Network account has one payment method configured in their remittance', page_no=72, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('be76c77e-3ecb-4149-8077-427a35384609'), chunk_index=428, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369013, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="information, the corresponding invoice created in the SAP Ariba solution uses the payment method and\nreceiving bank information from the cXML invoice.\n•\nIf there's no remittance information configured in the supplier's SAP Business Network account, the SAP Ariba\nsolution uses default values for the payment method and receiving bank on the invoice. To get the default", page_no=72, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('adbab8cf-4998-4acc-b4a8-42a8eaf7e225'), chunk_index=429, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369017, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='values, the SAP Ariba solution finds the first remittance location of the supplier location, and then finds the\n72\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes', page_no=72, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ddbea4a2-39fb-4a01-a1f1-0be6800cbe36'), chunk_index=430, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369082, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="payment method with the smallest rank of all payment methods defined for that remittance location. This\ncapability only works if the payment method is ACH or Wire.\n•\nThe SAP Ariba solution uses the following additional fields to look up right Remit To address: ABA Routing\nnumber, Swift ID, iBanID, Account ID.\n•\nFor IR documents, if there's no matching remittance location in the SAP Ariba solution, the remittance location", page_no=73, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('708d08fd-e5e5-486f-aae2-7198a7cd3ad5'), chunk_index=431, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369086, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="on the invoice is used.\nSee also the self-service parameter Application.Invoicing.RemittanceLocationUsingRemitToId,\nRemit To on invoice reconciliations is from invoice.\n•\nIf an invoice from SAP Business Network doesn't have a remittance location, it's not rejected in\xa0the SAP Ariba\nsolution.\nData import and export tasks that import invoicing and payment data include the following fields that specify bank\ndetails:\n•\niBanID\n•\nBranchName\n•\nAccountName", page_no=73, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('dec48bcf-1940-4bf3-b52c-37d5c3cb8e9a'), chunk_index=432, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369090, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The following table lists the data import tasks and the associated CSV files that contain these fields:\nData Import/Export Task\nCSV File(s)\nImport Supplier Bank Payment Locations\nExport Supplier Bank Payment Locations\nSupplierPaymentBankLocation.csv\nImport Remittance Location Data (Consolidated File)\nExport Remittance Location Data (Consolidated File)\nRemittanceLocationConsolidated.csv\nImport Buyer Bank Payment Locations\nExport Buyer Bank Payment Locations\nBuyerPaymentBankLocation.csv\nImport Remittances\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nExport of the bank details fields is currently supported', page_no=73, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e24967eb-de8a-4aa8-8f21-9443c0da2794'), chunk_index=433, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369094, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='only when using File channel. You cannot export these\nfields using Web services.\nRemittance.csv\nRemittanceDetails.csv\nRelated Information\nRemit To on invoice reconciliations is from invoice [page 129]\nSupplier Location Matching on Invoices\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes\nPUBLIC\n73', page_no=73, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bc8a0883-deb4-4642-8bdb-8b243658d884'), chunk_index=434, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369160, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice Management support invoice verification based on goods\nreceipts.\nThis feature is for businesses that require invoices for certain goods to be based on the price and quantity at\nthe time of shipping the goods rather than when the purchase order was placed. Goods receipt-based invoice', page_no=74, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1b33eae2-8982-4b34-9a65-36af85af9254'), chunk_index=435, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369164, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="verification supports a delivery-based invoicing process, where suppliers create invoices based on ship notices,\nand invoice quantities and prices are reconciled against receipts. Buyers can create multiple receipts for one ship\nnotice, so each invoice line can reference multiple receipts.\nOptionally, you can enable users to edit the matched quantities when manually matching receipts to invoice lines.\nBy default, the system determines matched quantities, and they're not editable.", page_no=74, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('58ed5b29-8e75-4253-9020-c863ef971a4b'), chunk_index=436, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369168, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='There are two ways receipts are matched to invoice lines:\n•\nUsing ship notice IDs. Goods receipt-based invoice verification uses the ship notice ID on the invoice and the\nreceipts as the common key to match receipts to invoice lines. This ID can be a ship notice, delivery note,\nor other unique identifier of the shipment. Suppliers can create one ship notice for multiple shipments using', page_no=74, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2d2395a6-0f9e-46e5-aeaf-69ffec57fe08'), chunk_index=437, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369171, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='different shipping options, and you might create multiple receipts, so each invoice line can reference multiple\nreceipts.\n•\nIn the absence of ship notice IDs, match invoices to receipts based on the purchase order they reference.\nWorkflow for Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing [page 75]\nWorkflow for Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification in SAP Ariba Invoice Management [page 79]', page_no=74, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('01c6575a-cbd0-4604-ad51-b60d396f6689'), chunk_index=438, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369175, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Workflows for Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification Without Ship Notice IDs [page 82]\nRelated Information\nConfiguring goods receipt-based invoice verification\n74\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes', page_no=74, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b2f5277d-e6d0-4e76-ba4e-be6b03707323'), chunk_index=439, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369181, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Workflow for Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification in\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing\nThe diagram shows a high-level workflow of the goods receipt-based invoice verification process. More detailed\nsteps follow.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes\nPUBLIC\n75', page_no=75, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0c52e11f-e19b-470d-a561-b96055797dab'), chunk_index=440, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369186, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Figure 5: High-Level Workflow of Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing\n76\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes', page_no=76, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9fc69465-26d7-420e-85fa-277dccf201a1'), chunk_index=441, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369341, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="1.\nA customer administrator configures some suppliers for goods receipt-based invoicing. This setting is for\nsupplier locations.\n2. The buyer creates a requisition in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing.\nEach requisition line item includes the field Goods Receipt-based Invoice Verification. The value of this field\n(Yes or No) is copied from the supplier location. Users can't edit this field.", page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('307dd7e2-7f3d-479e-a6c6-df448baa9cbc'), chunk_index=442, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369346, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3. The buyer submits the requisition, which goes through the approval process. When the requisition is approved,\nan order is generated and sent to SAP Business Network.\nPurchase orders exported to external ERP systems include a field to indicate whether the supplier is configured\nfor goods receipt-based invoice verification.\n4. SAP Business Network receives the order and sends it to the supplier.', page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('689c1f20-b15b-475c-b949-2933c88e5603'), chunk_index=443, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369349, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5. On SAP Business Network, the supplier optionally confirms the purchase order.\n6. The supplier ships the ordered items. The supplier might also send a ship notice with reference to the order.\n7.\nA receiving agent receives the items in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing, specifying an ID for the shipment in', page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('09ce58c2-5437-4aff-8860-daf6498b6ff8'), chunk_index=444, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369353, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='the Ship Notice field of the receipt header. The ID can be a ship notice ID, delivery note, or other shipment\nidentifier.\n8. For each receipt item marked for goods receipt-based invoice verification, the value in the Ship Notice field is\ncopied to the receipt line.\n9. The supplier invoices the buyer in one of the following ways:\n•', page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3dac39ef-8ea9-4cfd-a130-b7d2d7b09a1a'), chunk_index=445, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369357, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="By creating an invoice manually in their SAP Business Network account. SAP Business Network validates\nthe invoice based on configured business rules. After the invoice passes validation, it's sent to SAP Ariba\nBuying and Invoicing.\n•\nBy creating an invoice in their invoicing back-end system and sending it to the buyer through SAP Business\nNetwork as a cXML or EDI invoice. SAP Business Network validates the invoice based on configured", page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('735b4d0d-c043-4845-ac1a-accbf11b4805'), chunk_index=446, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369360, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="business rules. After the invoice passes validation, it's sent to SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing.\n•\nBy sending a paper invoice to the buyer, who then enters the invoice as an electronic copy into SAP Ariba\nBuying and Invoicing. A Receipts chooser on the invoice lets buyers choose the receipts the invoice applies\nto.", page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1fe7c0ad-8017-4598-87ff-45a78e145932'), chunk_index=447, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369364, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='10. When an electronic invoice arrives from the supplier, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing checks whether at least\none associated receipt exists.\nIf an associated receipt exists, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing creates an invoice reconciliation (IR)\ndocument. (This step might be delayed if your site is configured with a delay period using the parameter\nApplication.Invoicing.DaysToDelayIRCreation.)', page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3aeadf1a-f524-4df9-98f3-3bc650020487'), chunk_index=448, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369368, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If no associated receipts exist, and if a reconciliation delay period is configured, the invoice status is set to\nAwaiting Receipts until one of the following has occurred:\n•\nA receipt is created in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing.\n•\nThe invoice reconciliation delay period has expired.\n•\nAn invoice administrator has manually started the reconciliation process for the invoice.', page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('99b5bb83-a2fe-469e-a3e1-97cc251e7659'), chunk_index=449, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369371, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='11. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing creates an IR document and verifies the following for any invoice line where the\nassociated order line indicates that goods receipt-based verification is required:\n•\nThe quantity of items on the invoice and the receipts match within the defined tolerance limits.\n•\nThe unit price of items on the invoice and the receipts match within the defined tolerance limits.\n•', page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bd10658c-065e-4968-a3e7-b33d9249943c'), chunk_index=450, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369375, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The amount for items on the invoice and the receipts match within the defined tolerance limits.\n12. Invoice agents reconcile exceptions in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing. Receiving managers can reconcile\nexceptions related to missing receipt references, receipt quantity variances, and missing shipment references.\nIf no matching receipts are found based on the Ship Notice field, the invoice line items can be manually', page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f3915722-3cf6-42d2-b601-1db8448fe9f7'), chunk_index=451, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369379, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='matched to available receipts for the order. One reason that SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing might not find\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes\nPUBLIC\n77', page_no=77, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('41533776-2d09-4177-af7c-61ffb433889a'), chunk_index=452, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369456, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='associated receipts is because of user error, where an incorrect shipment identifier was entered on the receipts\nor the invoice.\n13. When the IR document is approved, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing sends a payment request, including\nassociated receipt references, to the external ERP system for payment.\nReturns and Line-Item Credit Memos\nReturns are processed as negative receipts that are linked to an existing receipt. When SAP Ariba Buying and', page_no=78, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('138c3a65-08a4-4464-8b72-5dd0bff39e71'), chunk_index=453, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369460, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing receives a return, it recalculates the Available Qty for the original receipt. For example, if receipt R1 has a\nquantity of 10 boxes, and the receiving agent rejected 2 boxes, the available quantity for R1 now is 8.\nLine-item credit memos include a reference to the original invoice, which means any receipts attached to the', page_no=78, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c0659a54-8674-4010-a979-2ef00b2d4841'), chunk_index=454, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369464, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='original invoice are used when matching the credit memo. Line-item credit memos affect goods receipts as follows:\n•\nThe invoiced quantity, or allocated quantity, decrements based on a negative quantity in the line-item credit\nmemo.\n•\nThe available quantity increments.\nOverallocation and Underallocation of Receipts to Invoice Lines\nSAP Ariba Invoice Management handles overallocation and underallocation of available receipts to invoice lines as\nfollows:\n•', page_no=78, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('00849fa2-e370-4938-892f-a015eb9bd618'), chunk_index=455, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369468, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If the exception handler selects more receipts than required based on the invoiced quantity, SAP Ariba Buying\nand Invoicing drops any overallocated receipts. If the last receipt in the list leads to a greater total received\nquantity than the invoiced quantity, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing matches only the required quantity. The\nremaining (not matched) quantity is available for allocation to other invoices.\n•', page_no=78, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c51775c5-bdba-4b5a-b43a-fd336f321783'), chunk_index=456, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369471, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If the exception handler selects fewer receipts than required to match the invoice quantity, SAP Ariba Buying\nand Invoicing accepts the underallocation after confirmation by the user and generates a Receipt Quantity\nVariance exception. Subsequent exception handlers can then either add additional matching receipts, or\nresolve the exception by accepting the invoiced quantity.\nRelated Information\nWorkflows for Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification Without Ship Notice IDs [page 82]\n78\nPUBLIC', page_no=78, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cdf6c249-9b40-4529-b01d-17ef220bba8c'), chunk_index=457, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369475, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes', page_no=78, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ff85e01b-aaf3-4261-a532-91b9b6f71a6c'), chunk_index=458, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369481, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Workflow for Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification in\nSAP Ariba Invoice Management\nThe diagram shows a high-level workflow of the basic goods receipt-based invoice verification process. More\ndetailed steps follow.\nFigure 6: High-Level Workflow of Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes\nPUBLIC\n79', page_no=79, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f5112720-4bc9-4dda-87fb-856c71723710'), chunk_index=459, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369628, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='1.\nThe buyer sends an approved purchase order for one or more items from an integrated ERP system to SAP\nBusiness Network.\n2. SAP Business Network receives the order, sends it to the supplier, and sends a copy of the order to SAP Ariba\nInvoice Management.\n3. On SAP Business Network, the supplier optionally confirms the purchase order.', page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0267c64d-c590-4ff2-bf9b-220d8c83e1ab'), chunk_index=460, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369632, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='4. The supplier ships the ordered items and sends a ship notice with reference to the order.\n5. The buyer receives the items in the ERP system, and the ERP system sends a copy of the receipt to SAP Ariba\nInvoice Management. The copy of the receipt must include the ship notice number, which might be manually\nentered by the receiving agents.', page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bba671fe-2a6a-4a85-8b60-7f00987c8d64'), chunk_index=461, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369636, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='6. The supplier invoices the buyer by using one of the following options:\n•\nBy creating an invoice manually in their SAP Business Network account. In this case, the business rules\nensure that suppliers can only invoice for shipped quantities when creating the invoice from the purchase\norder. The rules also ensure that the invoice includes the ship notice reference. After the invoice passes the', page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a5110c6d-3a2c-4bad-a566-a252d194b57c'), chunk_index=462, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369640, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="SAP Business Network validation, it's sent to SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\n•\nBy creating an invoice in their invoicing backend system and sending it to the buyer via SAP Business\nNetwork as a cXML or EDI invoice. SAP Business Network validates the invoice based on the business\nrules. For example, if the supplier referenced an incorrect ship notice on the invoice or if the ship notice ID", page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('74eeccd5-2c9e-43a7-ab76-9fff26abff17'), chunk_index=463, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369644, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='is missing, SAP Business Network rejects the invoice.\n•\nBy sending a paper invoice to the buyer, who then enters the invoice as an electronic copy into SAP Ariba\nInvoice Management. After the invoice is approved, an invoice copy is sent to the suppliers to allow them to\ntrack the invoice and payment approval process.\n7.', page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d30a04c3-ed70-4c3d-a3c0-e9e91cb029fd'), chunk_index=464, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369647, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Ariba Invoice Management checks if at least one associated receipt exists for the invoice.\nIf an associated receipt exists, SAP Ariba Invoice Management creates an invoice reconciliation document\n(unless your site is configured with a delay period using the parameter Days to delay creating an IR\ndocument( Application.Invoicing.DaysToDelayIRCreation).\nIf no associated receipts exist, and if a reconciliation delay period is configured, the invoice is set to the status', page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('513fb75d-18d4-425f-9c36-05b75cd617af'), chunk_index=465, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369651, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Awaiting Receipts until one of the following has occurred:\n•\nSAP Ariba Invoice Management has received one or more applicable receipts from the ERP system.\n•\nThe invoice reconciliation delay period has expired.\n•\nAn invoice administrator has manually started the reconciliation process for the invoice.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nAs with all status changes, the change from Submitted to Awaiting Receipts might take some time,', page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('76156e07-f54d-4e9f-b157-7f289827e95b'), chunk_index=466, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369655, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='depending on how many documents your site is processing.\n8. SAP Ariba Invoice Management creates an invoice reconciliation document and verifies the following for any\ninvoice line where the associated order line indicates that goods receipt-based verification is required:\n•\nThe quantity of items on the invoice and the receipts match within the defined tolerance limits.\n•', page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d939ae97-4cf7-4fdc-bac8-9d8b5dfd777c'), chunk_index=467, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369658, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="The unit price of items on the invoice and the receipts match within the defined tolerance limits.\n9. Invoice agents reconcile exceptions in SAP Ariba Invoice Management. If matching receipts based on the ship\nnotice ID can't be found, invoice agents can manually match the line item on the invoice to available receipts", page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fcc62a47-eaef-49cf-8002-411c76d6b9aa'), chunk_index=468, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369662, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='for the order. One reason that SAP Ariba Invoice Management might not find associated receipts is because of\nuser error, where the incorrect ship notice ID was entered on the receipts or the invoice.\n10. SAP Ariba Invoice Management includes a member of the Receiving Manager group to reconcile exceptions\nrelated to missing receipt references, receipt quantity variances, and missing ship notice references.', page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3cca22c7-78ce-4928-80b0-caf8b23db494'), chunk_index=469, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369666, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='11. SAP Ariba Invoice Management sends the invoice reconciliation to the external ERP system. In the ERP system,\nthe invoice reconciliation lines are split based on matching receipt lines (multiple InvoiceDetailOrder\nsegments for each line item on the invoice reconciliation).\n80\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes', page_no=80, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0d2b1411-e08f-4d7c-a6a0-a6e6e87fc0a2'), chunk_index=470, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369756, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Line-level ship notice information isn't included for items marked for goods receipt-based invoice verification.\n12. If no external approval of the invoice reconciliation is required, the invoice is approved for payment in SAP\nAriba Invoice Management, an invoice status update is sent to the supplier on SAP Business Network, and SAP\nBusiness Network sends the approved invoice to the ERP system.", page_no=81, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c170d615-acbf-40df-a0bf-91085793b99b'), chunk_index=471, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369760, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If external approval of the invoice reconciliation is required, a user in the ERP system reconciles any exceptions\nand approves the invoice reconciliation there. The ERP system then sends the status update to SAP Business\nNetwork, which updates the invoice status for suppliers and sends the status update to SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement.\nReturns and Line Item Credit Memos', page_no=81, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ccd328a4-eeba-454f-b3d9-5db97f8c2f92'), chunk_index=472, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369764, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Returns are processed as negative receipts that are linked to an existing receipt. When SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement receives a return, it recalculates the Available Qty for the original receipt. For example, if receipt\nR1 has a quantity of 10 boxes, and the receiving agent rejected 2 boxes, the available quantity for R1 now is 8.', page_no=81, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('82b52ff5-fd48-469d-be5c-00b8a668d559'), chunk_index=473, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369768, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Line item credit memos include a reference to the original invoice, which means any receipts attached to the\noriginal invoice are used when matching the credit memo. Line item credit memos affect goods receipts as follows:\n•\nThe invoiced quantity, or allocated quantity, decrements based on a negative quantity in the line item credit\nmemo.\n•\nThe available quantity increments.\nOverallocation and Underallocation of Receipts to Invoice Lines', page_no=81, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d1d5511a-4e03-422d-83f2-2fda299d3563'), chunk_index=474, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369772, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Ariba Invoice Management handles overallocation and underallocation of available receipts to invoice lines as\nfollows:\n•\nIf the exception handler selects more receipts than required based on the invoiced quantity, SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement drops any overallocated receipts. If the last receipt in the list leads to a greater total received\nquantity than the invoiced quantity, SAP Ariba Invoice Management matches only the required quantity. The', page_no=81, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d51bba3c-0654-4ca8-8cc3-a371c0bb8481'), chunk_index=475, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369775, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='remaining (not matched) quantity is available for allocation to other invoices.\n•\nIf the exception handler selects fewer receipts than required to match the invoice quantity, SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement accepts the underallocation after confirmation by the user and generates a Receipt Quantity\nVariance exception. Subsequent exception handlers can then either add additional matching receipts, or\nresolve the exception by accepting the invoiced quantity.\nRelated Information', page_no=81, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('86c96315-7efe-4648-88ff-2f90c3d37bae'), chunk_index=476, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369779, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Workflows for Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification Without Ship Notice IDs [page 82]\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes\nPUBLIC\n81', page_no=81, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3a427148-f622-4fe2-976e-5ece3e1b6ec2'), chunk_index=477, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369863, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Workflows for Goods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification\nWithout Ship Notice IDs\nThe following workflows illustrate how invoices are matched to receipts when the invoice doesn't include a ship\nnotice ID.\nThese workflows apply to sites that allow invoices without ship notice IDs to be automatically matched to receipts\nbased on purchase order. The SAP Ariba solution matches the invoice to the receipt for the same purchase order.", page_no=82, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5cbb5fb3-ebac-4132-a7e8-0bbb3ff78aad'), chunk_index=478, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369867, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If there are multiple available receipts, they are picked in the ascending order based on when the receipts were\ncreated.\nBasic Flow\n1.\nThe buyer sends the supplier an order for items marked for goods receipt-based invoice verification.\n2. The buyer receives the items and creates a receipt that includes a ship notice ID.\n3. The supplier sends an invoice for the items.', page_no=82, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5e983616-4fa3-44c2-b0a0-429345ae3d49'), chunk_index=479, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369871, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="4. The SAP Ariba solution checks the invoice for a ship notice ID.\n5. If the invoice doesn't include a ship notice ID, the SAP Ariba solution looks for a receipt for the purchase order\nthat's referenced on the invoice, and matches the invoice to that receipt.\n6. The SAP Ariba solution raises quantity variance or price variance exceptions as appropriate.", page_no=82, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b6b4ef74-8b64-4da1-8223-94c751f18630'), chunk_index=480, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369874, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When the Invoice Comes in Before the Receipt Is Created\nIn this workflow, the buyer manually matches additional receipts to the invoice to resolve the exception. If a\nquantity variance exception is raised after the invoice is matched to receipts for the same PO, the only way to\nresolve it is to manually match any additional receipts to the invoice.\n1.', page_no=82, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5bc30073-5f4b-4639-8978-845cca6e4341'), chunk_index=481, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369878, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="The buyer sends the supplier an order for items marked for goods receipt-based invoice verification.\n2. The supplier sends an invoice for the items. The invoice doesn't include a ship notice ID.\n3. Upon receiving the invoice, the SAP Ariba solution looks for but doesn't find a matching receipt.\n4. The SAP Ariba solution raises a Matching Receipt Not Found exception against the invoice because the\nreceipt doesn't exist yet.", page_no=82, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('79e5f1ee-d26e-43b6-a7ed-8a471a045d4a'), chunk_index=482, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369882, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="5. The buyer creates a receipt for the order. The receipt includes a ship notice ID.\n6. The SAP Ariba solution matches the invoice to the receipt and clears the Matching Receipt Not Found\nexception.\nWhen There Are Multiple Receipts for the Purchase Order That's Referenced on the Invoice\n1.\nThe buyer sends the supplier an order for an item marked for goods receipt-based invoice verification. The", page_no=82, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9fcabb7f-f5b4-4c69-b6cf-31dcc4b5390e'), chunk_index=483, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369886, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='quantity of the item is 100.\n2. The buyer receives 20 of the items and creates a receipt. The receipt includes a ship notice ID.\n82\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes', page_no=82, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8836ab72-e1ec-4430-a3b3-ed6f3d44cefa'), chunk_index=484, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369943, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="3. The buyer receives 20 more of the items and creates a receipt. The receipt includes a ship notice ID. (The ship\nnotice ID can be either the same as or different from the one on the previous receipt.)\n4. The supplier sends an invoice for 30 of the items. The invoice doesn't include a ship notice ID.", page_no=83, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7fcaf6cd-e5b0-4e8c-a5f3-dd0fbfbfff3d'), chunk_index=485, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369948, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5. The SAP Ariba solution matches the invoice to both receipts, matching a quantity of 20 for the first receipt and\na quantity of 10 for the second receipt.\nWhen a Quantity Variance Exception Is Raised After the Invoice Is Matched to Receipts for the\nSame Purchase Order\n1.\nThe buyer sends the supplier an order for an item marked for goods receipt-based invoice verification. The', page_no=83, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('79e6c38c-88b5-4f45-a028-7ed38e18df8a'), chunk_index=486, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369951, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="quantity of the item is 100.\n2. The buyer receives 20 of the items and creates a receipt. The receipt includes a ship notice ID.\n3. The supplier sends an invoice for 30 of the items. The invoice doesn't include a ship notice ID.\n4. The SAP Ariba solution matches the invoice to the receipt.\n5. A Receipt Quantity Variance exception is raised.", page_no=83, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f25763cb-b4c9-4d48-8ea2-4e35c3854396'), chunk_index=487, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369955, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="6. The buyer receives 20 more of the items and creates a receipt. The receipt includes a ship notice ID. (The ship\nnotice ID can be either the same as or different from the one on the previous receipt.)\n7.\nThe SAP Ariba solution continues to match the invoice to the first receipt only. It doesn't automatically match", page_no=83, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a61eeb8d-ab66-42be-b4f2-01add983c4e9'), chunk_index=488, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 369959, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='the invoice to the second receipt. The invoice reconciliation document still has a Receipt Quantity Variance\nexception.\n8. The buyer manually matches the second receipt to the invoice.\n9. The SAP Ariba solution clears the Receipt Quantity Variance exception.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice Reconciliation Processes\nPUBLIC\n83', page_no=83, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d39272dc-6278-4b74-8101-28773fdcf97f'), chunk_index=489, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370055, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Payment Processes\nHere's a list of topics that provide overviews of various processes related to the payment of invoices.\nExternal System Payment Model [page 84]\nInvoices from Subcontractors [page 85]\nPayment Terms [page 87]\nDiscount Management [page 89]\nExternal System Payment Model\nPayment models determine where payments are scheduled. SAP Ariba supports the External System payment\nmodel, which means payments are scheduled and processed through an external ERP system.", page_no=84, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('23e66e79-9020-4932-adb3-67f80531e5de'), chunk_index=490, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370059, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The previously available Ariba Pay payment model option is no longer available to customers who are not already\nusing it.\nThe payment process consists of the following phases:\n•\nThe payment scheduling phase, in which you review and finalize a payment request\n•\nThe payment settlement phase, in which the actual payment is executed', page_no=84, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('eed775be-6ae0-443f-b904-f2d487559668'), chunk_index=491, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370063, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='In the external system payment model, initial scheduling of payments occurs in the SAP Ariba invoicing solution,\nbut the final payment scheduling and payment processing occurs in the external system. The following steps\ndescribe the payment process for external system payments:\n1.\nThe SAP Ariba invoicing solution initially schedules the payment based on the payment terms [page 87]\ndefined in the invoice.', page_no=84, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f952f18a-ee6a-45d1-9af8-08adf06b3132'), chunk_index=492, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370067, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='2. SAP Ariba Invoice Management sends invoices approved for payment through your SAP Business Network\naccount in cXML format to your external ERP system. SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing send approved invoices\nin OK-to-Pay files to the external system.\n3. The external system creates a matching invoice record and schedules the payment.\n4. Remittance information is imported from the external system into your SAP Ariba solution , and the invoice', page_no=84, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c0440898-add1-45ce-aa8d-f319624023de'), chunk_index=493, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370071, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='reconciliation is marked Paid after the remittance data is received and the clearance period defined for the\npayment method has passed for all payment (remittance) transactions associated with the invoice.\nWhen the external system creates a matching invoice record, it sends an update back to SAP Ariba, where the\ninvoice reconciliation is updated with the external system invoice ID. Your external system can submit payment', page_no=84, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4db749fb-6cb9-4e3c-9b6a-f1915e6d9639'), chunk_index=494, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370074, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='request updates and remittance information through the payment integration toolkit to SAP Business Network to\nensure that payment-related information is synchronized between SAP Business Network, your SAP Ariba invoicing\nsolution, and the external system.\nWhen an IR is approved, the associated payment request status changes to Scheduled. If you get back payment\nremittance data from your external system, the system then generates a payment transaction with a status of', page_no=84, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6caafde3-bd26-4a45-bda3-32b45adb58da'), chunk_index=495, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370078, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Paid. If the data indicates that the invoice was not paid in full (underpayment), the system creates a new payment\n84\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Processes', page_no=84, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7474971d-02b6-4dd9-931b-a12e468defb4'), chunk_index=496, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370164, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='request document for you to track and process payment of the outstanding balance. The ID of the new payment\nrequest is the same as the original payment request, plus a suffix, such as -1.\nUnderpayments and overpayments are noted on the History tab of the IR document.\nIf the payment is canceled by the external system, when that cancellation data is received, a payment transaction', page_no=85, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9302d616-d982-42a4-9373-b6273ef2e0ed'), chunk_index=497, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370168, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='with the status Cancelled is created in the SAP Ariba invoicing solution.\nIf your external system fails to create an associated invoice for the payment, the payment request remains in\nScheduled status and the IR status changes to Push Failed. The History tab of the payment also notes that the\npush has failed.\nPayments for advance payment documents in SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing', page_no=85, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3578b1b4-706b-4e71-a37d-e45cb8e28ed5'), chunk_index=498, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370172, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The payment process for advance payment documents is similar to that of invoices. Approved advance payments\nare exported to the external system for payment processing, using the web services or file channel. The status\nof the advance payment document changes to Paying when the external system sends an acknowledgment for\nthe advance payment document. The external system then processes the payment and sends the remittance', page_no=85, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0da56b27-0d09-441d-a33a-8ab672e8e3f3'), chunk_index=499, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370175, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='information. The status of the advance payment document changes to Paid when remittance information is\nreceived for its entire amount.\nRelated Information\nPayment Document Status Flow [page 92]\nAdvance Payment Workflow [page 9]\nAdvance Payment Status Flow [page 99]\nInvoices from Subcontractors\nBusinesses in some regions are required to categorize their suppliers as subcontractors to ensure timely', page_no=85, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('883e43a1-32c9-41c6-92ac-bca58589bec3'), chunk_index=500, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370179, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='payments of the orders placed with such suppliers. To ensure that subcontractors are paid on time, invoices from\nsubcontractors have payment schedules tied to the date of delivery.\nIf your site supports subcontractor information on receipts, the Date Delivered field from the receipt is used to\ncalculate payment due date. The Date Delivered field is shown on the payment request.', page_no=85, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('73c710e6-f138-4d99-a2b5-f15ac6f9d69d'), chunk_index=501, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370183, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The following parameters control support for subcontractor information in the procurement process:\n•\nIdentify purchase orders for subcontractors\n(Application.Procure.EnableSupplierAsSubContractor)\n•\nInclude subcontracting details in receipts\n(Application.Procure.EnableSubcontractingForReceiving)\nWhen buyers receive an item from a supplier marked as a subcontractor, they fill in the Date Delivered field on the\nreceipt. That date is then used to calculate the payment schedule.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Processes\nPUBLIC\n85', page_no=85, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9839788d-2a81-45ad-8601-5d209c5f766f'), chunk_index=502, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370280, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If a receipt has multiple items with different delivery dates, the payment request uses the earliest delivery date.\nMore specifically, the payment request uses the earliest date of all approved receipts and their receipt items\n(including rejected items) at the time the invoice reconciliation (IR) document was fully reconciled and approved.\nThis is the case regardless of which PO items are on the invoice.', page_no=86, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('350987b1-5a52-42cb-944b-e846bfd3d9a4'), chunk_index=503, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370285, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="If the buyer reconciles and approves an invoice from a subcontractor before receiving the items, the payment\nschedule is determined in the same way as for non-subcontractor invoices. Receipts approved after an invoice has\nbeen reconciled and approved don't affect the payment schedule.\n\ue094\xa0Restriction\nSubcontractor information is not supported for summary (or multi-PO) invoices. A summary invoice is", page_no=86, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('63b93084-a624-4eae-896f-e340d2bd2520'), chunk_index=504, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370289, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='an invoice associated with multiple purchase orders. The payment schedule for multi-PO invoices from\nsubcontractors is not based on delivery date.\n\ue16d\xa0Example\nPayment flow for a receipt with multiple delivery dates\n1.\nA purchase order contains Item 1 and Item 2.\n2. On the receipt, Date Delivered for Item 1 is July 3, 2020. Date Delivered for Item 2 is August 15, 2020.', page_no=86, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0393a0ee-0a5d-4917-8077-d89961f9d13d'), chunk_index=505, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370292, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3. The supplier sends an invoice for one or both items.\n4. The IR document is reconciled and approved.\n5. On the payment request, the Date Delivered is July 3, 2020, the earliest delivery date of both items.\n\ue16d\xa0Example\nPayment flow for items received after the first invoice is reconciled and approved\n1.\nA purchase order contains Item 1, Item 2, and Item 3.', page_no=86, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bd9df541-2d26-4fc0-985a-2eb416bf94ea'), chunk_index=506, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370296, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="2. The receipt has multiple delivery dates:\n•\nDate Delivered for Item 1 is October 2, 2020.\n•\nDate Delivered for Item 2 is October 11, 2020.\n•\nItem 3 hasn't been received yet.\n3. The supplier invoices for one or two of the items.\n4. The IR document is reconciled and approved.", page_no=86, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e1744aac-5c26-418d-862b-00da83dca8a1'), chunk_index=507, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370300, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5. On the payment request, the Date Delivered is October 2, 2020, the earliest delivery date on the receipt.\n6. Item 3 is received. On the receipt, Date Delivered for Item 3 is September 30, 2020.\n7.\nThe supplier sends a second invoice for the order. The IR document is reconciled and approved.\n8. On the payment request for the second invoice, Date Delivered is September 30, 2020.\nRelated Information', page_no=86, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('32c3f49f-93b0-40a2-9017-aa568f5c235c'), chunk_index=508, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370303, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Subcontractor Information for Suppliers on Requisitions\nReceipts for Orders from Subcontractors\n86\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Processes', page_no=86, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7cd2c7f6-f1c9-49b2-8180-3bbbb5c176be'), chunk_index=509, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370390, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Payment Terms\nPayment terms specify when a supplier must be paid for an invoice and define any discounts available for early\npayment.\nAn administrator configures payment terms in your site. They are stored with supplier information and appear on\npurchase orders, invoices, and IRs. Payment terms typically include:\n•\nA unique ID, such as PT1\n•\nA title, such as Net 45, 2%/30, 3%/20\n•', page_no=87, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('45166f93-bf49-416c-b14a-e6668b5ef388'), chunk_index=510, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370394, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A description that can indicate the number of days within which the payment must be made and related\ninformation, such as discounts offered for early payments or other incentives\nFor example, you might see payment terms displayed as:\nID\nPT1\nTitle\nNet 45, 2%/30, 3%/20\nDescription\nNet amount due in 45 days, 2% discount if paid in 30 days, 3%\ndiscount if paid in 20 days\nTerms', page_no=87, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b0360cf5-50f5-4da9-bc34-45c78a7b2ba6'), chunk_index=511, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370398, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Pay in days Discount\n45 0%\n30 2%\n20 3%\nThe system compares payment terms that appear on invoices with payment terms defined in the\nrelated purchase order or contract. If the payment terms do not match, the system creates an\ninvoice exception that must be reconciled. (If you want to avoid these exceptions and enforce', page_no=87, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b7b270bb-6156-4872-8e79-7284dce15702'), chunk_index=512, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370402, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='the payment terms on the PO or contract, you can have SAP Ariba set the site parameter\nApplication.Invoicing.InvoiceTypesThatOverridePaymentTerms.)\n\ue201\xa0Caution\nAll payment terms are assumed to be NET payment terms and are displayed as such to suppliers on SAP\nBusiness Network. Support for non-NET payment terms, such as EOM payment terms, can be configured\nthrough a customization project.\n\ue05c\xa0Note', page_no=87, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('60503992-254c-4f3e-a588-aef93a95c4a2'), chunk_index=513, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370405, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='In the default configuration, only standard line items (not additional charges such as taxes or shipping) are\nincluded when payment discounts are calculated. Your site might be configured to include additional line item\ntypes in discount calculations.\nIf the default payment terms at the header level of the initial purchase order to be updated when the', page_no=87, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fe1e7278-e1ba-409b-92e7-79d246967ddf'), chunk_index=514, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370409, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='subsequent version of the purchase order is created, enable the Update default payment terms at the\nheader level of the initial purchase order when the subsequent version of the purchase order is created\n(Application.Purchasing.UpdateDefaultPaymentTermsOnPOHeader) parameter to prevent the mismatch\nin the payment terms between the initial and subsequent versions of the purchase orders. For more information,\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Processes\nPUBLIC\n87', page_no=87, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0fc44636-98ba-40aa-91c1-fd6f555da253'), chunk_index=515, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370487, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="see Update default payment terms at the header level of the initial purchase order when the subsequent version of\nthe purchase order is created.\nPayment Date and Due Date Calculations\nPayment date and due date are calculated based on your site's configuration and the payment terms on the\ninvoice.\nThe payment terms on the invoice and the payment policy configuration for your site determine the payment date", page_no=88, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0458c938-d01f-45ae-9b89-d7950ac9f8a4'), chunk_index=516, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370491, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='and the due date for a payment request. The payment date determines when the payment is processed, taking\ninto account any available discounts, and the due date determines the last day the payment can be made without\nbecoming overdue.\nThe following settings control payment date and due date calculations:\n•\nYour payment policy configuration: take maximum discount, take no discount, or take applicable discount\n•', page_no=88, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('200b588c-83c4-4bd1-b0bc-46e076fceef4'), chunk_index=517, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370495, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Your site's configuration: by default the effective date for the payment due date calculations is the invoice\nreconciliation approval date, but your site might use the invoice delivery date or due date instead.\nThe following examples demonstrate how the due date and payment date are calculated based on the payment\nterms and system configurations.\nExample: No Discount, Effective Date Is Approval Date", page_no=88, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('80e2ea87-4362-44aa-a152-a15df911c1a1'), chunk_index=518, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370499, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Payment terms are Net 30, no discount, and the invoice reconciliation is approved on June 1.\nIn this example, the payment date and the due date are set to July 1.\nExample: No Discount, Effective Date Is Delivery Date\nPayment terms are Net 30, no discount, and the item is delivered on June 1.\nIn this example, the payment date and the due date are set to July 1.', page_no=88, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c4b356db-f5db-4e23-95b8-6fb9f7036966'), chunk_index=519, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370502, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If there are multiple items on the receipt with different delivery dates, the earliest delivery date is used as the\neffective date.\nExample: Take Maximum Discount, Effective Date Is Approval Date\nThe payment terms are Net 30 days, 20 days 2%, 15 days 3%. The invoice reconciliation is approved on June 1.', page_no=88, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('94a47b5a-888f-4d7b-8192-7de54d995e9b'), chunk_index=520, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370506, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='In this example, the due date is set to July 1, the payment date is June 16, and the discount applied to the payment\nis 3%.\n88\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Processes', page_no=88, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2a87fe23-65d8-4074-a438-0d5b977d8526'), chunk_index=521, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370574, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Example: Take Applicable Discount, Effective Date Is Invoice Date\nThe payment terms are Net 30 days, 20 days 2%, 15 days 3%. The invoice date is May 15. the invoice reconciliation\nis approved on June 1.\nIn this example, the due date is July 1, the payment date is June 4, and the discount applied to the payment is 2%.\nExample: Take No Discount, Effective Date Is Approval Date', page_no=89, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bfe34727-b1cc-4e9d-b4e9-66487e6cbc90'), chunk_index=522, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370578, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The payment terms are Net 30 days, 20 days 2%, 15 days 3%. The invoice date is May 15. The invoice reconciliation\nis approved on June 1.\nIn this example, the due date and the payment date are set to July 1 and no discount is applied.\nExample: Take No Discount, Effective Date Is Invoice Date', page_no=89, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ff4657ab-075b-43e2-8b01-e424c690fbc8'), chunk_index=523, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370582, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The payment terms are Net 30 days, 20 days 2%, 15 days 3%. The invoice date is May 15. The invoice reconciliation\nis approved on June 1.\nIn this example, the due date and the payment date is set to June 14 and no discount is applied.\nRelated Information\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Managing Payment Documents [page 137]\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices [page 101]', page_no=89, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('beb0044c-afa8-4152-a5e0-2cce9c2b7a53'), chunk_index=524, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370586, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoices from Subcontractors [page 85]\nDiscount Management\nDiscount management allows you and your suppliers to agree to early payment in exchange for discounts.\nDiscount management is a process that allows you and your suppliers to request or offer early payment in\nexchange for discounts from the supplier. Early payment can be initiated by your organization and offered to\nselected or all suppliers, or by the supplier.', page_no=89, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('dcc9f671-1596-493e-84f3-ee45f7379b1b'), chunk_index=525, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370589, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='In order to take advantage of discount options, your external system must be configured to flag payment proposals\nfor early discount, and your SAP Business Network account must be enabled and configured for discount\nmanagement.\nDiscount management requires ERP integration using the payment integration toolkit. The discount management\nprocess flow depends on the features enabled in your site and the integration options you have implemented. Ariba\nprovides the following options:', page_no=89, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('229af4af-9231-42ad-8557-ae1691092afd'), chunk_index=526, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370593, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Processes\nPUBLIC\n89', page_no=89, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c4f05bba-27d5-4b00-9085-0d971c7b2300'), chunk_index=527, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370682, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\nIntegration using the Payment Request file (OK-to-pay file) generated in SAP Ariba Procurement solutions. If\nyour site is configured for SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing only, then this is the only integration option.\n•\nIntegration through cXML. If your site is configured for SAP Ariba Invoice Management only, then this is the\nonly integration option.\nDiscount Process with OK-to-Pay File Integration [page 90]', page_no=90, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('eebea314-3d7f-469e-b56a-ae113be6d398'), chunk_index=528, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370686, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Discount Process with for CXML Integration [page 91]\nDiscount Process with OK-to-Pay File Integration\nThe following steps describe the discount management process in sites with payment request file (OK-to-pay file)\nintegration:\n1.\nAfter an invoice is fully reconciled and approved, your SAP Ariba invoicing solution sends a payment request\n(payment proposal) to SAP Business Network.', page_no=90, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('57d3c17a-7ef6-42e4-9c64-fe2e099d471f'), chunk_index=529, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370690, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='2. The payment request file (OK-to-pay file) is exported from your SAP Ariba invoicing solution and imported into\nan external ERP system.\n3. Depending on the ERP implementation, payment managers review the payment requests in the external\nERP system and flag invoices allowed for discounting, or invoices are automatically selected for discount\nmanagement in the ERP.', page_no=90, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6d102694-48ce-45e8-b34c-3c2a212438fc'), chunk_index=530, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370694, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='4. When the payment request is created in the ERP, and every time the payment request is updated in the ERP,\na payment request update operation is sent to SAP Business Network from the ERP through the payment\nintegration toolkit. Payment requests that are allowed for dynamic discounting have the cXML extrinsic\nelement immediatepay set to yes in the PaymentProposalRequest document you send to SAP Business\nNetwork.', page_no=90, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e66ac5a2-c193-49b4-b68a-4f6fece8be08'), chunk_index=531, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370697, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='5. When SAP Business Network detects that an invoice is allowed for early payment, it sends email notifications\nto alert the supplier (if buyer-initiated) or the payment manager in your organization (if supplier-initiated) to\nreject or accept the offer. Discount negotiations are managed entirely on SAP Business Network.\n6. Once the offer is accepted, a payment request download operation is sent to the ERP from SAP Business', page_no=90, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('40177763-8b9e-4d4a-9a7d-543ed950bd22'), chunk_index=532, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370701, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Network through the payment integration toolkit.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nNeither the updated nor the negotiated payment proposals will be available in your SAP Ariba invoicing\nsolution.\n7.\nAfter the payment has been made in the ERP, the payment remittance transactions are sent to SAP Business\nNetwork through the payment integration toolkit.\n8. SAP Business Network sends the payment remittance information to your SAP Ariba invoicing solution.\nRelated Information', page_no=90, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('26f2235a-1c55-452b-88f4-f7b7f4b948d1'), chunk_index=533, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370705, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Discount Management [page 89]\n90\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Processes', page_no=90, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d9af8722-17f2-46e7-98d6-c4de3fb5cd95'), chunk_index=534, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370774, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Discount Process with for CXML Integration\nThe following steps describe the discount management process in sites with cXML integration:\n1.\nAfter an invoice is fully reconciled and approved, the SAP Ariba solution sends an invoice status update to SAP\nBusiness Network.\n2. The cXML invoice is downloaded from SAP Business Network to the external ERP through an adapter, which\ncreates a payment proposal (payment request) in the ERP.', page_no=91, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('68ad12af-1da6-4170-81b0-e86949c997d5'), chunk_index=535, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370778, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3. Depending on the ERP implementation, payment managers review the payment requests in the external ERP\nsystem and flag payment requests allowed or discounting or payment requests are automatically selected for\ndiscount management in the ERP. Payment requests that are allowed for dynamic discounting have the cXML\nextrinsic element immediatepay set to yes in the PaymentProposalRequest document you send to SAP\nBusiness Network.', page_no=91, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6090dfdc-ad02-4d12-80b9-4e4c40b76b52'), chunk_index=536, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370781, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='4. The adapter pulls the payment proposals (Pay Me Now for invoices proposed for early payment) from the\nERP and sends them to SAP Business Network, which creates a new payment proposal transaction on SAP\nBusiness Network.\n5. When SAP Business Network detects that an invoice is allowed for early payment, it sends email notifications', page_no=91, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2875ee11-e150-4c47-acb6-2e12a0b7c597'), chunk_index=537, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370785, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='to alert the supplier (if buyer-initiated) or the payment manager in your organization (if supplier-initiated) to\nreject or accept the offer. Discount negotiations are managed entirely on SAP Business Network.\n6. Once the offer is accepted, a payment proposal update operation is sent to the external system from SAP\nBusiness Network through the adapter and the payment request is updated in the SAP Ariba solution. Users', page_no=91, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('90fea7c7-562a-49cc-bfd7-f070d548e34e'), chunk_index=538, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370789, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='can view the payment requests, but they cannot update them.\n7.\nAfter the payment has been made in the ERP, the payment remittance transactions are sent to SAP Business\nNetwork through the payment integration toolkit (the payment integration toolkit allows submitting payment\nbatch information, which is not available if payment remittance information is transmitted through an adapter.)', page_no=91, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a665ae00-94cb-4e79-8fcb-a54609195f73'), chunk_index=539, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370792, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='8. SAP Business Network sends the payment remittance information to your SAP Ariba invoicing solution.\nRelated Information\nDiscount Management [page 89]\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Processes\nPUBLIC\n91', page_no=91, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('646eada1-4355-49c0-8f2c-02022aca2d06'), chunk_index=540, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370850, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Payment Document Status Flow\nYour invoicing solution updates the status of payment documents at various points in the invoice reconciliation and\npayment process.\nThe status flow described in the following table is for the External Pay payment model only.\nActivity\nInvoice Reconciliation\n(IR) Status\nPayment Request Sta-\ntus\nPayment Transaction\nStatus\nSAP Business Network\nrouting status/invoice\nstatus\nAn invoice is approved\nReconciling\nProcessing\nn/a\nAcknowledged/Sent\nReconcile an invoice', page_no=92, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cd30abd6-62ed-44c8-b869-456b64ee6ce3'), chunk_index=541, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370854, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='reconciliation (IR) docu-\nment\nReconciling ->\nApproving\nProcessing\nn/a\nAcknowledged/Sent\nAn IR document is ap-\nproved\nPaying\nScheduled\nn/a\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\nApprove an IR (IR sent\nto ERP for additional\nreconciliation or appro-\nval. Not applicable in\nSAP Ariba Buying and\nInvoicing-only sites)\nApproving -> Awaiting\nExternal Reconciliation\nProcessing\nn/a\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\nERP fails to create in-\nvoice reconciliation (not\napplicable in SAP Ariba\nBuying and Invoicing-\nonly sites)', page_no=92, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f7de4ad0-b7b9-4873-bc1c-b8e26db5aa9f'), chunk_index=542, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370858, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Awaiting External\nReconciliation -> Push\nFailed\nProcessing\nn/a\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\nERP fails to create\ninvoice for scheduled\npayment (SAP Ariba In-\nvoice Management)\nPaying -> Push Failed\nProcessing\nn/a\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\nERP fails to create\ninvoice for scheduled\npayment (SAP Ariba\nBuying and Invoicing-\nonly sites that use the\nAsynchronous or Direct\nPush payment request\nsending option)\nPaying -> Paying Failed\nSending\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\n92\nPUBLIC', page_no=92, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e55e9b9a-235c-43b9-b261-f68e484c18fa'), chunk_index=543, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370862, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Document Status Flow', page_no=92, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('21e8b8b7-869a-404f-b297-6becaae5e7ce'), chunk_index=544, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370915, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Activity\nInvoice Reconciliation\n(IR) Status\nPayment Request Sta-\ntus\nPayment Transaction\nStatus\nSAP Business Network\nrouting status/invoice\nstatus\nERP reconciles IR and\nsends Invoice Status\nUpdate Request (SUR)\n(not applicable in SAP\nAriba Buying and In-\nvoicing-only sites)\nAwaiting External\nReconciliation ->\nPaying\nProcessing ->\nScheduled\nn/a\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\nERP moves reconciled\ninvoice back to Process-\ning in the ERP (invoice\nin SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement is an ERP', page_no=93, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('acfa860f-0b41-49d4-95b2-80934c13a35c'), chunk_index=545, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370919, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="invoice copy) (SAP ERP\nand Oracle ERP only)\nPaying -> Awaiting\nExternal Reconciliation\nProcessing ->\nScheduled\nn/a\nn/a\n(Optional and depend-\ning on your site's con-\nfiguration) SAP Busi-\nness Network receives\na payment proposal re-\nquest update from the\nERP system\nPaying\nScheduled\nn/a\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\nPayment remittance\ndata is received\nPaying\nScheduled -> Paying\nPaid\nAcknowledged/Paid\nPayment clearance pe-\nriod has passed (de-\npending on your site's", page_no=93, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('abe51cf2-67b6-466f-81df-bbcd0dc34420'), chunk_index=546, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370923, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='configuration, either the\nclearance period is\nspecified per payment\nmethod or your site\nreceives a payment re-\nmittance update with\nstatus Cleared through\nSAP Business Network)\nPaying -> Paid\nPaying -> Paid\nPaid -> Cleared\nAcknowledged/Paid\nDeny a cancel invoice\nCanceling ->\nReconciling\nProcessing\nn/a\nAcknowledged/Sent\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Document Status Flow\nPUBLIC\n93', page_no=93, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e9e30465-eb9d-45f4-bb6f-68675ad45988'), chunk_index=547, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370959, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Activity\nInvoice Reconciliation\n(IR) Status\nPayment Request Sta-\ntus\nPayment Transaction\nStatus\nSAP Business Network\nrouting status/invoice\nstatus\nInvoice is canceled or\nreversed in ERP system\nwhile the IR document\nis in Paying or Paying\nFailed status\nPaying or Paying Failed\n-> Rejected\nPaying->Rejected\nPayment requests can\nalso be rejected\nwhen they have a\nstatus of On Hold,\nSending, Scheduling,\nor Scheduled.\nn/a\nAcknowledged/\nRejected\nERP cancels invoice', page_no=94, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6032be18-bfcb-4c86-9646-5a146d527a71'), chunk_index=548, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 370963, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='while the IR document\nis in Paid status\nPaid -> Paying ->\nRejected\nPaid->Rejected\nPaying\nERP cancels invoice (in-\nvoice in SAP Ariba In-\nvoice Management is an\nERP invoice copy) (SAP\nERP and Oracle ERP\nonly)\nPaying ->Rejected\nRejected\nn/a\nRelated Information\nExternal System Payment Model [page 84]\n94\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nPayment Document Status Flow', page_no=94, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ec7e3673-6e03-4d59-9711-fb8b11cdfd65'), chunk_index=549, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371026, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoice and Invoice Reconciliation Status Flow\nYour SAP Ariba invoicing solution updates the status of invoice and invoice reconciliation documents, and\nassociated payment requests, at different stages of the invoice and invoice reconciliation workflow.\nActivity\nInvoice status\nInvoice reconciliation\nstatus\nPayment request sta-\ntus\nSAP Business Network\nrouting status/invoice\nstatus\nReceive an invoice from\nthe ERP\nSubmitted\nn/a\nn/a\nAcknowledged/Sent\nCreate an invoice in\nyour SAP Ariba solution\nSubmitted\nn/a', page_no=95, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('20ae18a2-6519-4b5e-859e-20fd1154097b'), chunk_index=550, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371030, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='n/a\nn/a\nReceive an invoice from\nSAP Business Network\n(not sent by an invoice\nconversion service)\nSubmitted or\nSubmitted with Errors\n(if there are validation\nerrors, for example, due\nto policies configured in\nthe SAP Ariba solution)\nn/a\nn/a\nAcknowledged/Sent\nReceive an invoice that\nwas sent to SAP Busi-\nness Network by an in-\nvoice conversion serv-\nice (ICS)\nSubmitted or\nSubmitted with Errors\n(if there are validation', page_no=95, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('37281b7d-111b-41cc-ba32-16038ea7d11e'), chunk_index=551, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371034, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='errors, for example, in-\ncomplete or image-only\ninvoices)\nn/a\nn/a\nDepends on the situa-\ntion. See Invoice Valida-\ntion and Exception Han-\ndling on SAP Business\nNetwork.\nImport an external\ncXML invoice using an\nHTTP API\nSubmitted or\nSubmitted with Errors\n(if there are validation\nerrors)\nn/a\nn/a\nn/a\nReceive an invoice from\nSAP Central Invoice\nManagement through\nan API\nSubmitted or\nSubmitted with Errors\n(if there are validation', page_no=95, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('30d72418-1a14-4f87-8184-656f84592cc6'), chunk_index=552, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371038, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='errors, for example, in-\ncomplete or image-only\ninvoices)\nn/a\nn/a\nn/a\nReceive an information-\nonly invoice from SAP\nBusiness Network 1\nLoaded\nn/a\nn/a\nn/a\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice and Invoice Reconciliation Status Flow\nPUBLIC\n95', page_no=95, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1a36b487-3e97-4d5f-8c3b-70afd730673f'), chunk_index=553, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371098, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Activity\nInvoice status\nInvoice reconciliation\nstatus\nPayment request sta-\ntus\nSAP Business Network\nrouting status/invoice\nstatus\nApprove an invoice\nSubmitted ->\nApproved -> (CC\nInvoice to AN 2) ->\nReconciling\nReconciling\nProcessing\nAcknowledged/ Sent\nReconcile an invoice\nreconciliation (IR)\nReconciling\nReconciling ->\nApproving\nProcessing\nAcknowledged/Sent\nReject an IR\nReconciling ->\nReconciled\nRejected\nn/a\nAcknowledged/\nRejected\nReceive a cancel invoice\nfrom SAP Business Net-\nwork\nLoaded -> Canceling\nReconciling ->\nCanceling', page_no=96, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f413f123-ce1c-4833-9456-30ace7172f3d'), chunk_index=554, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371102, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='n/a\nAcknowledged/Sent\nApprove a cancel in-\nvoice\nCanceling -> Canceled\nCanceling -> Canceled\nn/a\nn/a\nDeny a cancel invoice\nCanceling ->\nReconciling\nCanceling ->\nReconciling\nProcessing\nAcknowledged/Sent\nInvoice is automatically\ncanceled after the\ncorresponding service\nsheet is rejected.\nSubmitted -> Canceled\nn/a\nn/a\nAcknowledged/\nCanceled\nApprove an IR (no addi-\ntional external ERP rec-\nonciliation required)\n(For sites that use\nthe Default payment re-\nquest sending option)\nReconciling ->\nReconciled', page_no=96, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a4d21a07-a849-46d1-a614-021d351ede87'), chunk_index=555, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371106, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Approving -> Approved\n-> Paying\nProcessing ->\nScheduled\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\nApprove an IR (no addi-\ntional external ERP rec-\nonciliation required)\n(SAP Ariba Buying and\nInvoicing-only sites that\nare configured to use\nthe Asynchronous or\nDirect Push payment\nrequest sending option)\nReconciling ->\nReconciled\nApproving -> Approved\n-> Paying\nProcessing -> Sending\n-> Scheduled\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\n96\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice and Invoice Reconciliation Status Flow', page_no=96, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7ff5f52e-1ba4-4134-9b82-0e5c6cfa1293'), chunk_index=556, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371162, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Activity\nInvoice status\nInvoice reconciliation\nstatus\nPayment request sta-\ntus\nSAP Business Network\nrouting status/invoice\nstatus\nERP fails to create\ninvoice for scheduled\npayment (SAP Ariba In-\nvoice Management)\nReconciled\nPaying -> Push Failed\nProcessing\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\nERP fails to create\ninvoice for scheduled\npayment (SAP Ariba\nBuying and Invoicing-\nonly sites that use\nthe Asynchronous or\nDirect Push payment\nrequest sending option)\nReconciled\nPaying -> Paying Failed\nSending\nAcknowledged/', page_no=97, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b10cefb0-b5e1-41fb-99de-5c3fbea4d552'), chunk_index=557, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371166, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Approved\nApprove an IR (IR sent\nto ERP for additional\nreconciliation or appro-\nval. Not applicable in\nSAP Ariba Buying and\nInvoicing-only sites)\nReconciling\nApproving -> Awaiting\nExternal Reconciliation\nProcessing\nAcknowledged/Sent\nERP fails to create in-\nvoice reconciliation (not\napplicable in SAP Ariba\nBuying and Invoicing-\nonly sites)\nReconciling\nAwaiting External\nReconciliation -> Push\nFailed\nProcessing\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\nERP reconciles IR and\nsends Invoice Status\nUpdate Request (SUR)', page_no=97, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b03782bd-e57d-4984-b755-20af0261b86f'), chunk_index=558, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371169, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='(not applicable in SAP\nAriba Buying and In-\nvoicing-only sites)\nReconciling ->\nReconciled\nAwaiting External\nReconciliation ->\nPaying\nProcessing ->\nScheduled\nAcknowledged/\nApproved\nERP cancels invoice (in-\nvoice in SAP Ariba In-\nvoice Management is an\nERP invoice copy) (SAP\nERP and Oracle ERP\nonly)3\nReconciled\nPaying -> Canceled\nCanceled\nn/a\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice and Invoice Reconciliation Status Flow\nPUBLIC\n97', page_no=97, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0033148b-9d1e-4abf-b8af-74c95038e565'), chunk_index=559, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371248, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Activity\nInvoice status\nInvoice reconciliation\nstatus\nPayment request sta-\ntus\nSAP Business Network\nrouting status/invoice\nstatus\nERP moves reconciled\ninvoice back to Process-\ning in the ERP (invoice\nin SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement is an ERP\ninvoice copy) (SAP ERP\nand Oracle ERP only)3\nReconciled ->\nReconciling\nPaying -> Awaiting\nExternal Reconciliation\nProcessing\nn/a\nERP cancels invoice\nwhile the IR document\nis in Paying or Paying\nFailed status', page_no=98, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b9f7c5f6-23e0-4a76-858a-cccfed4bac28'), chunk_index=560, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371253, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Reconciled -> Rejected\nPaying or Paying Failed\n-> Rejected\n(Rejected automatically\nin SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement. In SAP\nAriba Buying and In-\nvoicing, rejected when\nForce Reject button is\nclicked.)\nPaying -> Rejected\nAcknowledged/\nRejected\nERP cancels payment\ntransaction while the IR\ndocument is in Paid sta-\ntus\nReconciled -> Paying\nPaid -> Paying\nPaying\nn/a', page_no=98, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bf66c5bf-fe91-4869-8bc9-e256b6043c51'), chunk_index=561, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371257, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='1Information-only invoices can only be submitted by suppliers through SAP Business Network. Typically, a supplier\nwill cancel an information-only invoice after submitting a final invoice.\n2 The CC Invoice to AN status applies only for invoices created manually in your invoicing solution on behalf of a\nsupplier who is enabled on SAP Business Network. The supplier can view the CC invoice and track its status on SAP\nBusiness Network.', page_no=98, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('878c3232-4114-4ec5-97a4-38a9ddf2ff13'), chunk_index=562, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371260, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='3ERP invoice copies are information-only copies of invoices that are managed and reconciled entirely in the external\nERP system. Each ERP invoice copy has a corresponding information-only invoice reconciliation. Neither document\nis editable. ERP invoice copies are only available in sites enabled for SAP Ariba Invoice Management and for SAP\nFieldglass invoices in SAP Ariba Buying solutions integrated with SAP Fieldglass .\n.\nRelated Information\nForced Reconciliation of CC Invoices', page_no=98, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d840e4f9-4cda-4f22-bab0-13f27343999e'), chunk_index=563, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371264, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoice Reconciliation for Documents in Paying or Paying Failed Status\nInvoice Reconciliation for Documents in Rejecting Status\nInvoice Reconciliation for Documents Awaiting External Reconciliation\nInvoice Reconciliation for Documents in Approved Status\n98\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nInvoice and Invoice Reconciliation Status Flow', page_no=98, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d127f532-d24a-48dd-8a77-e25d6f56f8f2'), chunk_index=564, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371330, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Advance Payment Status Flow\nThe status of an advance payment document is updated at different stages of its workflow.\nAction\nStatus\nCreate an advance payment\nComposing\nSubmit the advance payment\nComposing to Submitted\nApprove the advance payment\nSubmitted to Approved\nExport the advance payments to the ERP system\nApproved\nErrors received from the ERP system\nApproved to Composing\nCancel an advance payment in the Approved state.\nApproved to Canceling', page_no=99, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('adc042a2-c8fa-49ae-b481-7945f7ede21d'), chunk_index=565, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371334, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Receive the acknowledgment for an advance payment from the\nERP system\nApproved to Paying\nReceive the remittance information from ERP system\nPaying to Paid\nForce pay an approved advance payment if an acknowledg-\nment is not received from ERP system\nApproved to Paid\nOne of the following actions apply:\n•\nReceive the remittance information for all line items on an\nadvance payment from the ERP system.\n•', page_no=99, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('aa29bbc4-288a-4442-80cd-c24559913baf'), chunk_index=566, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371337, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Force pay an advance payment in the Paying state if re-\nmittance information is not received from the ERP system.\nPaying to Paid\nCancel an advance payment in Approved state\nApproved to Canceling\nOne of the following actions apply:\n•\nReceive the acknowledgment for a cancelled advance pay-\nment from the ERP system.\n•\nForce cancel an advance payment in the Cancelling state', page_no=99, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fdd80420-0459-451e-a420-eb83707b5f77'), chunk_index=567, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371341, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='an acknowledgment for the cancelled advance payment is\nnot received.\nCanceling to Canceled\nForce cancel an advance payment in Canceling state if ac-\nknowledgment is not received for the cancelled advance pay-\nment\nCanceling to Canceled\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nAdvance Payment Status Flow\nPUBLIC\n99', page_no=99, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('352a3894-4d0e-43fc-8725-5a60a88a3ef6'), chunk_index=568, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371347, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Action\nStatus\nRemittance information for an advance payment has been re-\nceived from the ERP system, while the advance payment is\nmarked for cancellation.\nCanceling > Paying > Paid\nCancel invoice while the IR document is in Paid status.\nPaid > Paying\n100\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nAdvance Payment Status Flow', page_no=100, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('14e47adb-7ed9-423b-8cfa-9cda7b7a24bc'), chunk_index=569, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371457, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Creating\nand Managing Invoices\nSome of the functionality for supplier contacts is controlled by configuration options that SAP Ariba Support sets\nfor you. These parameters apply to SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\nApplication.Invoicing.AdaptAmountFromANForAmountBasedReceivingWithAdvancedPricing (set by SAP\nAriba Support)\nEnsures that the item amount is calculated correctly for items with advanced pricing and', page_no=101, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e4c97f2b-f66d-40ac-acbc-650279a26513'), chunk_index=570, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371461, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='amount-based receiving on invoices from SAP Business Network. This parameter affects\nitems with both of the following:\n•\nAdvanced pricing details (also known as PBQ)\n•\nAmount-based receiving\nFor example, a quantity-based service item might have advanced pricing to show how the\nprice is calculated, and amount-based receiving because the item is provided as a service.', page_no=101, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('99fb3cba-6562-4c60-ad9b-65136b9bff01'), chunk_index=571, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371465, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When set to Yes, this parameter adapts the item amount calculation to compensate for the\nfact that SAP Business Network always sends quantity = 1 for items with amount-based\nreceiving.\nApplication.Invoicing.AdjustSplitAllocationOnQtyChange (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nFor invoice line items split by quantity and amount, this parameter determines whether split\nallocations adjust proportionately to reflect quantity changes. This parameter is for invoices', page_no=101, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6b94d6de-6bb7-4e1a-bf12-9b7747c83337'), chunk_index=572, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371469, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='entered by the buyer when lines are split by quantity and amount. If this parameter is set to\nYes, when a user changes the quantity of a line item, the split quantities are automatically\nadjusted in a way that maintains the original split proportions. For example, suppose an\nitem quantity of 10 is split 3 ways into 4, 2, and 4. If the item quantity changes to 5, and this', page_no=101, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ffd076dd-ffd1-4fbe-b97c-ab86e84c34ef'), chunk_index=573, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371473, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="parameter is set to Yes, the splits become 2, 1, and 2. If this parameter is set to No, when a\nuser changes the quantity of a line item, the split quantities doesn't change. The user has to\nupdate the allocation manually.\nApplication.Invoicing.IgnoreZeroLineShipping (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether zero amount line level shipping lines are allowed on cXML", page_no=101, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fd687716-ba0a-4915-b89d-f7e300a7b051'), chunk_index=574, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371476, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoices. When this parameter is set to Yes, zero amount shipping lines are not created at\nthe line level. When set to No, zero shipping lines are retained. Ariba Support can also set\nthe parameter to No to retain zero amount shipping lines in IRs. The default value for this\nparameter is Yes.\nApplication.Contract.MasterAgreement.AllowCollaborativeInvoicing (set by SAP Ariba\nSupport)', page_no=101, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8e8eb75d-394e-4d62-85e0-f86fdeb76d3f'), chunk_index=575, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371480, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter specifies whether suppliers on SAP Business Network can punch in to\nyour invoicing solution to create invoices against no-release-order contracts directly in your\ninvoicing solution. The default setting is No. When this parameter is set to Yes, contract\nagents can override the value on the contract request (allow invoicing against contract).\nThis field is only displayed for contracts where Release Required is set to No.', page_no=101, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9ea4869a-451c-493e-b289-d958cdebb0d0'), chunk_index=576, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371483, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Application.Invoicing.AllowReusingInvoiceNumberAcrossCalendarYear (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices\nPUBLIC\n101', page_no=101, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0620237e-180c-4b25-ac64-332fa7d48da3'), chunk_index=577, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371597, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Specifies whether supplier invoice numbers from the previous year can\nbe reused in a new year. The yearly end date is determined by\nthe supplier location's fiscal year. This parameter applies to invoices\nthat have one of the statuses listed in the self-service parameter\nApplication.Invoice.AllowReusingInvoiceNumber. This parameter is ignored if\nthe parameter Application.Base.AribaNetworkOrganizationSyncOption (set by", page_no=102, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('121fd2c8-c793-4dbd-9ec8-c5c45de0c3fe'), chunk_index=578, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371601, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Ariba) is set to NoSync or if the fiscal year end date is missing for the supplier on SAP\nBusiness Network.\nApplication.Invoicing.UseSupplierLocationFromOrderOnInvoice (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nSpecifies whether PO-based invoices always use the supplier location of the matching\norder. If this parameter is set to Yes, the supplier location on the matching order overrides', page_no=102, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('80991b89-0f95-4c2b-9125-261102e0556a'), chunk_index=579, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371605, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="any user edits to supplier location on the invoice. If this parameter is set to No, users' edits\nto the supplier location on the invoice are retained.\nApplication.Invoicing.AllowSupplierToCreateCompliantContractInvoice (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether or not suppliers can create a contract invoice in their SAP\nBusiness Network account and punch into the invoicing solution from SAP Ariba to retrieve", page_no=102, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('aac6064f-ac88-4905-bc27-6d38d96240b9'), chunk_index=580, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371609, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='the contract and add items. The invoice is validated according to SAP Business Network\ncountry/region-based rules and buyer-specified contract pricing. The default setting is Yes\nfor sites enabled on or after Release 12s2.\nApplication.Invoicing.AllowLegalEntityCodeAtSplitLevel (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether or not line-level accounting distributions on invoices\ninclude the Company Code field in SAP-integrated sites. If enabled, the Company Code', page_no=102, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9ce98832-b46e-43ab-ad07-8c61487968bc'), chunk_index=581, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371613, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='field does not show at the header level of the invoice; it shows at the line level instead. The\ndefault setting is No.\nApplication.Invoicing.AutoInvoiceLineCreation\nEnables the automatic creation of invoice line items from the PO details or receipt\ninformation in ICS invoices. Setting this parameter to Yes allows customers to submit\nelectronic invoices that do not contain any line item information to SAP Business Network.', page_no=102, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bc75aa0b-bc9d-4128-bf1a-d09ea00ef94f'), chunk_index=582, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371616, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='By default, this parameter is set to No.\nApplication.Invoicing.Enabled (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nDetermines whether the site includes functionality for viewing and reconciling invoices.\nWhen set to Yes, authorized users can view and reconcile invoices. When set to No, users\ncannot view or reconcile invoices.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nThis parameter does not control the ability to create or edit invoices. That is controlled\nby group membership.', page_no=102, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e282fd34-525a-49dd-ada9-dbdf9df5806a'), chunk_index=583, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371620, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Application.Invoicing.EnableTaxesOnShippingAndHandlingItems (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether or not users can add shipping and special handling lines\non invoices and specify taxes for those lines. When this parameter is set to Yes, the Add\nShipping Item and Add Special Handling Item buttons appear on the Add Items page\nwhen users are creating invoices. To add taxes to a shipping or special handling line, the', page_no=102, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a753ee50-a53c-420b-af32-0884501c15d4'), chunk_index=584, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371624, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='user selects Add Taxes at Line Level, which causes the Add Taxes button to appear next to\neach line. The default setting is No.\n102\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices', page_no=102, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0a75c152-f728-45b9-8eb0-e92db82f6e17'), chunk_index=585, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371722, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='\ue094\xa0Restriction\nTaxes cannot be added to charges at header-level.\nApplication.Invoicing.CalculateTaxesOnNetAmount (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nSpecifies whether line-level discounts are taken into account when percentage taxes\nare calculated on invoices. This parameter does not apply to invoice reconciliation (IR)\ndocuments.\n•\nWhen set to Yes, percentage taxes are calculated on the invoice net amount (the invoice\nbase amount minus the discount). The taxable amount includes the discount.\n•', page_no=103, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('11cecc95-c5b9-4b26-a5b4-562f2ba8879d'), chunk_index=586, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371727, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When set to No, percentage taxes are calculated on the invoice base amount.\nApplication.Invoicing.UseTLCTaxEngine (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter is used to specify if you want to use the enhanced tax computation engine\nor a third-party tax calculation engine for taxes applied on invoices.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nIf Application.Invoicing.CopyTaxCodesFromInvoiceToIR is set to Yes, the tax', page_no=103, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f397c1e3-3181-4ac2-a4c7-c7f79b252f5d'), chunk_index=587, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371730, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='code on an invoice tax line is copied to the corresponding IR tax line regardless of\nwhether the site is using the enhanced tax computation engine.\nApplication.Procure.EnableAccountingForWithholdingTaxInInvoiceAndIR (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether users can manage accounting information for\nwithholding taxes on invoices and invoice reconciliation documents. If set to Yes, users\ncan perform tasks, such as configure accounting splits for withholding taxes and mass edit', page_no=103, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6d61acc9-42a2-42a8-8389-a75a0cbc5d86'), chunk_index=588, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371734, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='tax accounting information for withholding taxes.\nThe default value of this parameter is No.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nTo manage withholding taxes on invoices and invoice reconciliation documents, the\nApplication.Invoicing.UseTLCTaxEngine parameter must be enabled.\nApplication.Invoicing.SkipAmount (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies a threshold amount below which the system skips validation of\nan invoice. The value represents an amount in the default currency. This parameter is used', page_no=103, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a50b394f-64fb-429b-8437-41e1fdea77c4'), chunk_index=589, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371738, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="by the invoice validation rules in the default configuration. If a site's configuration defines\ncustom validation rules, they might or might not use this parameter. The default value is 5.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nBy default, validation of credit memos is never skipped. If an invoice has a negative\namount (and therefore is a credit memo), it always raises an invoice exception. If the\nparameter Application.Invoicing.SkipLineCreditMemoExceptions is set to", page_no=103, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c4a6f2b6-2679-47c5-a197-c9bc7f40eb07'), chunk_index=590, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371741, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Yes, only header-level credit memos raise exceptions.\nApplication.Settlement.PaymentRequestSendMethodOption (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies a method for sending payment requests, which in turn defines\nwhether or not the status of invoice reconciliation and payment request documents in your\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices\nPUBLIC\n103', page_no=103, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('be610caa-b8bd-4f6a-bf6b-b23b042203d7'), chunk_index=591, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371874, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoicing solution depends on the success or failure of invoices in integrated ERP systems.\nThe following values are valid settings for this parameter:\n•\nDefault: the default value for the parameter. In this case, the status of the invoice\nreconciliation and payment request in your invoicing solution does not change based on\nthe success or failure of the invoice in the ERP system. You must use this setting if you', page_no=104, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c77a99a6-e69a-4508-9f31-fd3ba3428c2c'), chunk_index=592, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371878, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='export payment requests using SAP Integration Suite, managed gateway (formerly SAP\nAriba Cloud Integration Gateway).\n•\nAsynchronous Push: the recommended setting for sites that use file-based\nintegration between SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and the ERP system. In this case,\nthe status of the invoice reconciliation and payment request in SAP Ariba Buying and\nInvoicing changes based on the success or failure of the invoice in the ERP system. This', page_no=104, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b7130e6e-fb9f-4560-97e8-767e51613832'), chunk_index=593, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371882, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='value is not applicable to SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\n•\nDirectPush: the recommended setting for sites that use web services-based\nintegration between SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and the ERP system. In this case,\nthe status of the invoice reconciliation and payment request in SAP Ariba Buying and\nInvoicing changes based on the success or failure of the invoice in the ERP system. This', page_no=104, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3fd18a2c-71d4-4dda-9389-b7db47bde13e'), chunk_index=594, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371886, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='value is not applicable to SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\nApplication.Invoicing.InvoiceTypesThatOverridePaymentTerms (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nSpecifies the types of cXML invoices for which the payment terms are always defaulted\nfrom the invoice source (the PO or contract, depending on the type of invoice). The\npayment terms passed in the cXML are ignored for such invoices. Valid values for this\nparameter are POInvoice and ContractInvoice. The default value is empty list.', page_no=104, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('44720c41-d25b-4d22-9b38-b2a6919e2d7e'), chunk_index=595, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371890, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="This parameter enables buyers to enforce that the payment term they specified for a PO or\ncontract is the payment term that ends up on invoices related to that PO or contract. If the\nsupplier specifies a different payment term on the invoice, it's overridden by the payment\nterm the buyer specified for the PO or contract. When this parameter isn't set, if an invoice", page_no=104, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0cb2a73a-fcd3-481c-83f2-c01549ed84e2'), chunk_index=596, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371894, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='from the supplier contains payment terms that differ from those in the PO or contract, an\nexception is raised.\nApplication.Invoicing.MaxInvoiceAttachmentPagesToPNG (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies the maximum number of pages of an attachment file on the\nInvoice Entry page that can be converted to PNG format when users choose to view the\nattachment. By default, this value is set to 15.\nApplication.Invoicing.AttachmentsInApprovalNotifications (set by SAP Ariba Support)', page_no=104, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('01bc4831-0c30-4b95-a4f4-8e9f44d26225'), chunk_index=597, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371898, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Determines whether users can receive attachments in email approval notifications for\ninvoice reconciliation documents, cancel invoice requests, and invoices. Setting this\nparameter to Yes adds the checkbox Exclude attachments from approval notifications\nto invoice-related email notification preferences. By default, attachments are included. If\nattachments total more than 10MB, no attachments are included.\nSetting this parameter to Yes may affect email approval performance.\nThis parameter is applicable when the parameter', page_no=104, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4647dea9-3c8b-4a67-8fe1-d6cf29fc2e97'), chunk_index=598, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371902, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Application.Base.EmailApprovalEnabled is set to Yes.\nApplication.Invoicing.EnforcePurchaseOrgSupplierValidation (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether or not the supplier field in invoices and invoice\nreconciliations is validated against the list of suppliers associated with the invoice\npurchasing organization. This parameter is only applicable for sites integrated with SAP.\n104\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices', page_no=104, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8224d589-a2b1-4dff-9a26-5f433e523e2a'), chunk_index=599, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 371999, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When this parameter is set to Yes, the search for suppliers when creating an invoice or\ninvoice reconciliation is filtered, so that the list includes only suppliers associated with the\nsame invoice purchasing organization as the user viewing the list.\nApplication.Invoicing.AllowOneTimeVendorInvoices (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nEnables the one-time vendor invoicing feature, which allows buyers to enter invoices for', page_no=105, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1e41782d-d5a0-49d8-bb75-0eba5fab4bbc'), chunk_index=600, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372003, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="infrequent or one-time vendors that don't have a supplier record in the SAP Ariba solution.\nBuyers can also receive one-time vendor invoices via SAP Ariba invoice conversion services\n(ICS). When this parameter is set to Yes:\n•\nCustomers can configure the one-time vendor invoicing feature, with the help of SAP\nAriba.\n•\nThe invoice entry page for non-PO invoices includes fields for creating one-time vendor\ninvoices.", page_no=105, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('de59f070-dfd1-43c1-8c6a-4cca4e17e601'), chunk_index=601, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372007, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Application.Invoicing.RespectEditabilityForCopyAccounting (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nDetermines whether copying line item accounting depends on field editability conditions\nsuch as group membership. If set to Yes, when the user clicks Copy Accounting, the\nsystem checks the editability of the split accounting fields and only copies the values if the\neditability conditions are met.\nApplication.Invoicing.SupportSupplierBankInfoOnInvoices (set by SAP Ariba Support)', page_no=105, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3c52286e-9ac3-41cb-b21e-dab723892008'), chunk_index=602, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372011, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Determines whether the SAP Ariba solution processes the supplier bank details in cXML\ninvoices (in the payment method extrinsic) and whether the supplier bank details in cXML\ninvoices from SAP Business Network are used on invoice reconciliation (IR) documents.\nSetting this parameter to Yes helps the SAP Ariba solution find the correct remittance\nlocation.\nSuppliers might send updated bank details in cXML invoices over SAP Business Network.', page_no=105, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('23f5f4f1-59c1-4d70-b887-45e26828df25'), chunk_index=603, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372015, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="This parameter applies to cXML invoices transmitted between SAP Business Network\nand the SAP Ariba invoicing solution. It's most likely to pertain to SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement sites and merged sites that include both SAP Ariba Invoice Management and\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing.\nIf this parameter is set to No, the SAP Ariba solution doesn't process updated bank", page_no=105, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('42397bcf-9920-4232-b307-e9d910f63bad'), chunk_index=604, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372018, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='details in invoices sent by suppliers. Supplier-specified bank details are not included in\nthe reconciled invoices sent to SAP Business Network for payment processing.\nIf this parameter is set to Yes, the following bank details can be received and processed\nduring the invoice reconciliation process and are included in the reconciled invoices sent to\nSAP Business Network:\n•\nBank ID Type\n•\nBank ID\n•\nBank Account ID\n•', page_no=105, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6c38b653-b921-48da-aa98-6ab437db10b6'), chunk_index=605, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372022, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Bank Account Type\n•\nIBAN\n•\nBranch Name\n•\nAccount Name\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices\nPUBLIC\n105', page_no=105, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('efcab166-7408-45d2-a0ee-cdf1fb560b5e'), chunk_index=606, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372086, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Self-Service Site Configuration Parameters for\nCreating and Managing Invoices\nAllow editing of taxes and charges on invoices [page 106]\nGenerate invoices for evaluated receipt settlement [page 107]\nEnable evaluated receipt settlement and automatic invoicing for service items [page 108]\nApply account determination rules to ERS invoices [page 109]\nGenerate short invoice numbers for ERS invoices [page 109]\nEmpty Reference Date field for contract punch-in items [page 110]', page_no=106, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8a8a27b2-693c-4a4f-a8d9-329834c19906'), chunk_index=607, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372091, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Support price-adjustment credit and debit memos [page 111]\nGet latest catalog prices for contract-based invoices [page 111]\nAllow split accounting [page 112]\nAllow export and import of accounting distribution [page 112]\nCopy tax codes from invoice to IR document [page 113]\nCommodity code for non-catalog invoice line items [page 114]\nAllow invoice number reuse [page 114]\nSend attachments associated with documents to ERP system [page 115]', page_no=106, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c6ccd1c5-809e-4860-b4ae-e75615ba45db'), chunk_index=608, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372094, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Default Requester for Invoices from Invoice API [page 116]\nRequire comments to supplier for invoice denial [page 116]\nReuse existing invoice payload ID for copy requests to Ariba Network [page 117]\nAllow editing of taxes and charges on invoices\nSpecifies whether users can add, edit, and delete taxes and charges on invoices from SAP Business Network.', page_no=106, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('dc98935e-1b79-47e5-af2c-c6aa9890bfda'), chunk_index=609, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372098, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Setting this parameter to No prevents editing taxes and charges on all SAP Business Network invoices except Italy\nSDI invoices and invoices sent by an invoice conversion service (ICS).\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.AllowEditingTaxesAndChargesOnAribaNetworkInvoices\nName\nAllow editing of taxes and charges on invoices\nDefault value\nNo\nThis parameter provides a way to handle invoices from suppliers who can't provide accurate tax information.", page_no=106, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7c0458c5-7cfa-43e4-9899-ab97c6dab0a8'), chunk_index=610, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372102, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='For example, some buying organizations enter withholding taxes manually on invoices from certain geographical\nlocations.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\n106\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices', page_no=106, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3272474f-6f86-4201-b05e-bcacc2e70269'), chunk_index=611, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 372177, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Related Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nGenerate invoices for evaluated receipt settlement\nDetermines whether invoices are automatically generated from approved receipts for suppliers that are configured\nfor evaluated receipt settlement (ERS).\nID\nApplication.Procure.EnableERS\nName\nGenerate invoices for evaluated receipt settlement\nDefault value\nNo\nThe evaluated receipt settlement (ERS) feature enables buyers to settle goods receipts without receiving invoices', page_no=107, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bc7041e6-6e20-465e-826e-29d7dfbc6858'), chunk_index=612, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 373900, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='from suppliers. This helps to reduce invoice variances and close purchasing transactions more quickly.\n•\nIf this parameter is set to Yes, invoices are automatically created when receipts are fully approved (SAP Ariba\nBuying and Invoicing) or imported from the external system (SAP Ariba Invoice Management).\nAlso, the ERSAllowed flag becomes available in the SupplierLocation.csv (legacy supplier import) and\nSupplierLocationConsolidated.csv import files to allow buyers to configure suppliers for ERS.', page_no=107, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5222f9f3-2303-409a-bbe1-c8a8bcbf9d57'), chunk_index=613, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 373908, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\nIf this parameter is set to No, invoices must be created manually from approved receipts.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Parameters\nTo enable ERS for service items, in addition to the Application.Procure.EnableERS parameter, set the\nfollowing parameter to Yes:\nEnable evaluated receipt settlement and automatic invoicing for service items,\nApplication.Procure.EnableERSForServiceItems', page_no=107, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ca3b3f2b-85ae-4c52-adb1-23362cfbb11f'), chunk_index=614, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 373912, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If your site uses approvable details determination rules, see also the parameter Apply account determination rules\nto ERS invoices [page 109], Application.Invoicing.ApplyApprovableDeterminationRulesToERS.\nContracts That Consist a Mix of ERS and Non-ERS Items\nManual invoicing is supported on contracts that have a mix of ERS and non-ERS items. To have your site configured\nto support manual invoicing against contracts with a mix of ERS and non-ERS items, have your Designated Support', page_no=107, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fc1bc0e3-ff51-4f2f-bac0-a9d2822c1eb9'), chunk_index=615, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 373915, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Contact (DSC) file a Service Request (SR). SAP Ariba Support will follow up to complete the request by turning on\nfeature SINV-8138.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices\nPUBLIC\n107', page_no=107, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e944f5cf-6e49-44e0-9681-c420c1350cc8'), chunk_index=616, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 373980, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Related Information\nEnable evaluated receipt settlement and automatic invoicing for service items [page 108]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nEnable evaluated receipt settlement and automatic\ninvoicing for service items\nDetermines whether invoices are generated automatically from approved service sheets for suppliers\nthat are configured for Evaluated Receipt Settlement (ERS). This parameter is effective only if the\nApplication.Procure.EnableERS parameter is set to Yes.\nID\nApplication.Procure.EnableERSForServiceItems\nName', page_no=108, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1e660cd1-0991-4e38-8948-6a3b6e648f95'), chunk_index=617, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 373985, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Enable evaluated receipt settlement and automatic invoicing for service items\nDefault value\nNo\nIf both this parameter and the Application.Procure.EnableERS parameter is set to Yes, invoices are created\nautomatically when service sheets are fully approved (SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing) or imported from external\nsystems (SAP Ariba Invoice Management). In addition, users can create correction service sheets with reference to', page_no=108, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('690db1b0-dae8-48f6-9cc5-fdab7e3b2159'), chunk_index=618, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 373988, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoiced service sheets for ERS items or a mix of ERS and non-ERS items.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nFor planned child items, taxes are not defaulted to service invoices from service purchase requisitions. When\ncreating an invoice, users must also enter tax, charge, and discount information.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nGenerate invoices for evaluated receipt settlement [page 107]', page_no=108, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1398e7df-f7a6-416e-91f2-63e36719250f'), chunk_index=619, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 373992, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Intelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\n108\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices', page_no=108, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8160a47d-817f-434b-b7f7-0358b14e3b71'), chunk_index=620, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374068, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Apply account determination rules to ERS invoices\nOn sites that use approvable details determination rules (advanced defaulting based on lookup tables, line-item\nfields, and expressions), specifies whether the rules apply to invoices generated automatically through the\nevaluated receipt settlement (ERS) feature.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.ApplyApprovableDeterminationRulesToERS\nName\nApply account determination rules to ERS invoices\nDefault value\nNo\nThis parameter applies to sites that use both of the following features:\n•\nEvaluated receipt settlement', page_no=109, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e0410b3b-0c46-49e1-a7c1-fc2cf8b69161'), chunk_index=621, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374072, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\nAdvanced defaulting based on lookup tables, line-item fields, and expressions. This advanced defaulting is a\nway to determine the accounting values for each accounting field in an approvable.\nPossible values for this parameter are Yes and No.\n•\nWhen set to Yes, the account defaulting set by your approvable details determination rules rules is applied to\nERS invoices.\n•', page_no=109, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('97fc0a6b-3fc4-4588-9cf8-4158dfb93de6'), chunk_index=622, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374076, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When set to No, the rules do not apply to ERS invoices.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nGenerate invoices for evaluated receipt settlement [page 107]\nEnable SAP ERP evaluated receipt settlement (ERS)\nEnable evaluated receipt settlement and automatic invoicing for service items [page 108]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration', page_no=109, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ad1ad083-2e55-43a9-9f1e-ac11a826246e'), chunk_index=623, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374080, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Advanced Defaulting Based on Lookup Tables, Line-Item Fields, and Expressions\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nGenerate short invoice numbers for ERS invoices\nSpecifies how to generate invoice numbers for ERS invoices, which affects their length. By default, invoice numbers\nfor scheduled fee invoices are created by combining the unique IDs of the receipt and the invoice, such as:', page_no=109, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e5275821-b047-439b-931f-ab76d3bf4ef5'), chunk_index=624, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374083, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='RCXXXXINVYYYY. If this parameter is set to Yes, the invoice numbers are based on receipt unique ID only, such as:\nRCXXXX.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.GenerateERSInvoiceNumberByReceiptIDOnly\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices\nPUBLIC\n109', page_no=109, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e9ddfe70-21a5-4016-8d57-16223da14e31'), chunk_index=625, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374129, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Name\nGenerate short invoice numbers for ERS invoices\nDefault value\nNo\nIf your ERP system requires short invoice numbers, you can set this parameter to Yes.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nGenerate short invoice numbers for ERS fee invoices\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nEmpty Reference Date field for contract punch-in\nitems', page_no=110, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8569f2c3-40f2-4d0d-99e1-2f0c8319e316'), chunk_index=626, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374133, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When suppliers punch in to the customer catalog to add line items to an invoice, determines whether the\nReference Date field is empty by default. If set to No, the Reference Date field is set to the current date.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.DefaultEmptyReferenceDateForContractPunchInLineIte\nms\nName\nEmpty Reference Date field for contract punch-in items\nDefault value\nNo\nWhen set to , suppliers must set the reference date manually.', page_no=110, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e7db2232-14e9-40d3-aab7-26504db8b22a'), chunk_index=627, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374137, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='We recommend customizing your SAP Business Network account to validate reference dates before invoice\nsubmission.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\n110\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices', page_no=110, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('065801d8-f3cb-4257-aae5-64479c14c79c'), chunk_index=628, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374187, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Support price-adjustment credit and debit memos\nSpecifies whether your site accepts and reconciles price-adjustment line-item credit memos and line-item debit\nmemos from SAP Business Network and whether buyers can enter line-item price-adjustment invoices. When set\nto Yes, users entering line-item credit memos choose between a price adjustment and a quantity adjustment.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.EnableLineItemPriceAdjustmentInvoices\nName\nSupport price-adjustment credit and debit memos\nDefault value\nNo', page_no=111, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1ef16e86-eebf-467d-b97c-39ee5d11ce15'), chunk_index=629, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374191, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nPrevent acceptance of specific invoice exceptions [page 127]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nPrice-Adjustment Debits and Credits [page 44]\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nGet latest catalog prices for contract-based invoices\nDetermines whether contract-based invoices get pricing for items from the current customer catalog or from the', page_no=111, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('32d4809f-78fb-4f4c-ac69-8d08ee6f2889'), chunk_index=630, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374195, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='contract. If set to Yes, when a contract-based invoice is created, the invoice gets the latest item prices from the\ncustomer catalog. If set to No, the invoice uses the prices set in the contract.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.RepriceItemsForContractBasedInvoices\nName\nGet latest catalog prices for contract-based invoices\nDefault value\nNo\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration', page_no=111, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c2389c51-a5b8-4d84-a9d3-74da9f325713'), chunk_index=631, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374199, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Parameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices\nPUBLIC\n111', page_no=111, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1445f16e-96d3-4e67-a7db-e9a0cb0dd2c7'), chunk_index=632, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374266, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Allow split accounting\nEnables or disables split accounting on line item level. If set to Yes, users can create accounting distributions at the\nline level in requisitions, service sheets, invoices, and invoice reconciliation documents.\nID\nApplication.Approvable.AllowSplitAccounting\nName\nAllow split accounting\nDefault value\nYes\nThis parameter doesn't apply to non-PO invoices created in guided buying.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.", page_no=112, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('254581e0-a1e2-41c2-9fea-aa8b7704227e'), chunk_index=633, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374270, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Related Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nAllow export and import of accounting distribution\nDetermines whether export and import of accounting distributions is allowed on requisitions, service sheets,\ninvoices, and invoice reconciliations.\nID\nApplication.Procure.AllowAccountingExportAndImport\nName\nAllow export and import of accounting distribution\nDefault value\nNo\nPossible values for this parameter are Yes and No.\n•', page_no=112, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e67377f4-614b-4daa-a665-219f0e71a9ee'), chunk_index=634, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374274, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If set to Yes, users authorized to edit a document can export the accounting distributions from the document\nto an Excel file to edit or add accounting distributions offline, and then import the edited file to update the\naccounting information on the document.\n•\nIf set to No, users cannot import or export accounting distributions on documents.', page_no=112, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2067cc85-ab66-44e1-b4ac-45503d2cb484'), chunk_index=635, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374277, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter is applicable for sites enabled for split accounting, which is controlled by the parameter Allow split\naccounting, Application.Approvable.AllowSplitAccounting.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\n112\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices', page_no=112, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a8383320-d00e-46d8-bc74-e949a1705fac'), chunk_index=636, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374343, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Related Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nCopy tax codes from invoice to IR document\nDetermines whether the tax codes for tax lines on invoice reconciliation (IR) documents originate from the\ncorresponding tax line on the invoice.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.CopyTaxCodesFromInvoiceToIR\nName\nCopy tax codes from invoice to IR document\nDefault value\nNo\nPossible values for this parameter are Yes and No.\n•', page_no=113, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('35585175-6b0a-4b77-97e0-5d00d8c04633'), chunk_index=637, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374347, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="If set to Yes, the tax code on an invoice tax line is copied to the corresponding IR tax line. If there's no valid tax\ncode that matches the invoice line, tax calculation fails on the IR.\nIf an invoice tax line has no tax code specified, the tax code for the IR is determined by a tax code lookup.\n•", page_no=113, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('081a0f5a-62e8-4564-9e97-de13d8d0b8ea'), chunk_index=638, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374351, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If set to No (the default), the tax code on the IR might be different from that on the invoice. The tax code is\ncalculated using a lookup. The lookup used depends on which tax computation engine your site is using, as\ndetermined by Application.Invoicing.UseTLCTaxEngine.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nIf the tax code on an IR is different from what’s expected, it might be because the site’s tax configuration needs', page_no=113, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('57eacee5-2657-4ca2-a00b-f219bb914aaa'), chunk_index=639, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374354, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='correcting. Address any tax configuration issues before you consider setting this parameter to Yes.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices\nPUBLIC\n113', page_no=113, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('eab4c8f2-1f75-49b0-ac31-b03ab3a3a018'), chunk_index=640, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374422, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Commodity code for non-catalog invoice line items\nSpecifies the default commodity code value for non-catalog line items on invoices. Accounting values associated\nwith the commodity code are also set for the non-catalog line items. The commodity code must be a valid value for\nthe system commodity code domain set for your site.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.InvoiceCreationDefaultLineItemCommodityCode\nName\nCommodity code for non-catalog invoice line items\nDefault value\nNot applicable', page_no=114, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('aa0a5d79-b42f-421f-bab8-4d40147a76c6'), chunk_index=641, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374426, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter applies to any invoice sent from SAP Business Network or created manually that includes non-\ncatalog line items.\nIf the value of this parameter is blank, users must enter a valid commodity code for non-catalog line items on\ninvoices.\nWhen a non-PO, PO-based, or contract-based invoice line uses the default commodity code defined by this', page_no=114, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('618d99f0-2acb-49a1-ada1-e86afd6fd25c'), chunk_index=642, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374430, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='parameter, the header-level line accounting value gets its default value from the commodity export map entry\n(CEME) settings, unless your site is configured to prevent that behavior. This behavior is controlled by feature\ntoggle CDN-13865, Prevent Header Level Charges Accounting Defaulting From CEME.\nThe system commodity code domain for your site is set by the parameter\nApplication.ClassificationCode.SystemCommodityCodeDomainName, which is set by SAP Ariba.', page_no=114, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8a36208c-e1e5-4878-8ef0-093ca01d4f7b'), chunk_index=643, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374434, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nAllow invoice number reuse\nDetermines whether users can reuse invoice numbers for failed, canceled, denied, and rejected invoices. Specify\nthe statuses for which you allow invoice number reuse. Valid values are: Failed, Canceled, Denied, Rejected.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.AllowReusingInvoiceNumber\nName\nAllow invoice number reuse', page_no=114, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e7f9da48-b944-45d3-92ee-836521af2e9e'), chunk_index=644, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374437, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Default value\nAn empty list\nThis parameter pertains to the Supplier Invoice Number field on invoices received from the supplier through SAP\nBusiness Network.\n114\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices', page_no=114, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6c336998-8bfb-441d-bc68-2e9b651540f0'), chunk_index=645, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374488, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nA related parameter allows the reuse of invoice numbers from the previous year. For more information, refer to\nAllow invoice number reuse in subsequent years\nRelated Information\nCase-insensitive matching for payment updates\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nSend attachments associated with documents to ERP\nsystem', page_no=115, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('91ba5904-421a-40b8-8b50-7120d0c35f20'), chunk_index=646, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374492, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Determines whether attachments associated with documents are sent to the ERP system.\nID\nApplication.Procure.AllowAttachmentToERP\nName\nSend attachments associated with documents to ERP system\nDefault value\nNo\nIf set to Yes, when documents, such as service sheets or invoices are sent to the external ERP system for\nreconciliation action, file attachments associated with those documents are also sent to the external system.', page_no=115, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e87f437e-bf99-44c7-b659-47cefb0123e4'), chunk_index=647, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374496, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If set to No, file attachments are not included when the associated documents are sent to the extenal system.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices\nPUBLIC\n115', page_no=115, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cf00a075-c597-4861-8459-8a5b6f1d7b5f'), chunk_index=648, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374557, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Default Requester for Invoices from Invoice API\nSpecifies a default requester for invoices created through an invoice management API. Enter a valid user name. The\nrequester is used in determining the default purchasing unit or business unit on the invoice. If you don't set this\nparameter, the requester value is AribaSystem.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.InvoiceAPI.DefaultRequesterUniqueName\nName\nDefault requester for invoices from invoice API\nDefault value\nNot applicable", page_no=116, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f9cfed74-3e70-4150-a588-fabe8acd6bab'), chunk_index=649, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374561, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter is applicable to invoices from SAP Central Invoice Management.\nThe requester of an invoice is the user specified in the On Behalf Of field. Configuring a default requester can\nhelp with auto-filling accounting information on the invoice. Users with the appropriate permissions can change the\nrequester as needed.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nThe API used to create invoices based on invoices from SAP Central Invoice Management is an internal SAP', page_no=116, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4592847f-4436-4ae8-a5ea-c5c152c6610c'), chunk_index=650, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374565, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Ariba API called the Invoice Management API.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nInvoices from SAP Central Invoice Management [page 61]\nRequire comments to supplier for invoice denial\nSpecifies whether an approver must add comments to the supplier when denying an invoice document.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.RequireCommentsToSupplierOnInvoiceDenial\nName', page_no=116, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e55e8022-de17-4e36-84e9-2849d1882036'), chunk_index=651, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374568, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Require comments to supplier for invoice denial\nDefault value\nNo\nThis parameter is applicable to invoices created on SAP Business Network.\n116\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices', page_no=116, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c0658374-14fc-4a1f-ae64-d119ecd5cff7'), chunk_index=652, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374644, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Regardless of this parameter setting, users who deny an invoice (INV) document can enter comments for the\nsupplier in the Comments to Supplier field in the user interface. Setting this parameter to Yes turns on the\nfollowing additional functionality:\n•\nUsers can include comments to suppliers when denying invoices through email approval. Comments can be\nentered in the space provided in the message body of the email notification.\n•', page_no=117, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9ca80e5c-3ff0-4bc6-8fdd-c92b5252e7cf'), chunk_index=653, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374648, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Comments to the supplier are mandatory for invoice denials.\nThe points in the following table pertain to comments submitted through email approval.\nParameter Setting\nApproval Notification Format (User's\nPreference)\nBehavior\nYes\nCompact text\nWhen the user enters a comment while\ndenying the invoice in email, those com-\nments are treated as comments to the\nsupplier and meet the requirement.\nNo\nCompact text\nWhen the user enters a comment while", page_no=117, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('022103d9-18fb-462b-aad8-3c571357e318'), chunk_index=654, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374652, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='denying the invoice in email, those com-\nments are treated as internal.\nYes\nPlain text\nThe user must enter a comment in the\nComments to Supplier field to meet the\nrequirement.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nRequire comments to supplier for invoice rejection [page 128]', page_no=117, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e4d3d677-46f8-4e92-9c36-d9d801f28fe2'), chunk_index=655, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374656, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Approval Notification Format Preferences\nReuse existing invoice payload ID for copy requests\nto Ariba Network\nDetermines whether SAP Ariba reuses the existing invoice payload ID to prevent duplicate invoice creation on SAP\nBusiness Network when the copy from central invoice (CC) to Ariba Network (AN) step fails.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.ReuseExistingInvoicePayloadIdForCCToAN\nName\nReuse existing invoice payload ID for copy requests to Ariba Network\nDefault value\nNo', page_no=117, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('27b7ba68-eff5-4865-8d8f-f637fa0faa49'), chunk_index=656, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374660, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When set to\u202fYes, the existing invoice payload ID is reused for subsequent CC to AN attempts.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices\nPUBLIC\n117', page_no=117, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6ce21492-da1e-4366-90a8-6fc97caa09e8'), chunk_index=657, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374667, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When set to\u202fNo (default), a new invoice payload ID is generated for each CC to AN attempt.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\n118\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Creating and Managing Invoices', page_no=118, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('93d93f00-d85c-4ba1-91dc-76945868e84f'), chunk_index=658, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374780, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for\nReconciling Invoices\nSome of the functionality for supplier contacts is controlled by configuration options that SAP Ariba Support sets\nfor you. These parameters apply to SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\nApplication.Invoicing.RequireApprovalOnSequentialNodeWithSameApprover (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nOn invoice reconciliation (IR) documents, determines the behavior of the approval flow', page_no=119, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4bdb85ff-b535-4c44-a9b8-9330285d52c7'), chunk_index=659, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374784, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="when a user who's in two subsequent approval group nodes edits the IR and approves\nit on behalf of the first group. This parameter is applicable when the edit rule Edit With\nResubmit is enabled. For example, suppose the approval flow includes Group A and\nGroup B in sequential approval nodes, and user 1 belongs to both groups. When User 1", page_no=119, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('56edc814-a735-46e0-bbba-5f196ccfbb94'), chunk_index=660, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374788, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='approves on behalf of Group A, the approval node for Group B either requires approval or is\nautomatically approved, depending on how this parameter is set.\nApplication.Invoicing.InvoiceEntryAllowEditLineDescription (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter controls whether or not users are allowed to edit item descriptions on\nPO-based invoices. The default setting is No.\nApplication.Invoicing.AllowLegalEntityCodeAtSplitLevel (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether or not line-level accounting distributions on invoices', page_no=119, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7595243c-8cb9-4492-9152-cacddc2ff0b0'), chunk_index=661, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374792, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='include the Company Code field in SAP-integrated sites. If enabled, the Company Code\nfield does not show at the header level of the invoice; it shows at the line level instead. The\ndefault setting is No.\nApplication.Invoicing.AutoAcceptAmount (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies a threshold for auto-accepting invoice reconciliation documents', page_no=119, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('741bf8ba-d29d-41ae-8be1-3e2f094655cb'), chunk_index=662, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374796, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='based on the total amount of the IR. If the IR amount is less than or equal to the value\nspecified in this parameter, the reconciliation engine auto-accepts the IR. The value for this\nparameter is an amount in the default currency. The default value is 10.\nApplication.Invoicing.AutoAcceptPercentage (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies a threshold for auto-accepting invoice reconciliation documents', page_no=119, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('83aa82ae-16c8-4296-9fe6-aeb88f8683c2'), chunk_index=663, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374799, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='based on the total amount of the IR as a percentage of the total amount left to invoice on\nthe associated purchase order. The value of this parameter is a decimal value, such as .10.\nThe default value is .15, meaning that the reconciliation engine auto-accepts an IR if its total\nis 15% or less of the amount left to invoice on the purchase order amount.', page_no=119, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cf5fa6ae-77f2-4604-8a60-8a0edff96fca'), chunk_index=664, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374803, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Application.Invoicing.SkipAmount (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies a threshold amount below which the system skips validation of\nan invoice. The value represents an amount in the default currency. This parameter is used\nby the invoice validation rules in the default configuration. If a site's configuration defines\ncustom validation rules, they might or might not use this parameter. The default value is 5.\n\ue05c\xa0Note", page_no=119, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('84a2b95e-8b54-42c9-a65c-762f203658fa'), chunk_index=665, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374848, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='By default, validation of credit memos is never skipped. If an invoice has a negative\namount (and therefore is a credit memo), it always raises an invoice exception. If the\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Reconciling Invoices\nPUBLIC\n119', page_no=119, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('75437277-6203-4d47-b9c9-7f0c48b46dd1'), chunk_index=666, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374947, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='parameter Application.Invoicing.SkipLineCreditMemoExceptions is set to\nYes, only header-level credit memos raise exceptions.\nApplication.Invoicing.SkipLineCreditMemoExceptions (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis legacy parameter specifies whether line-level credit memos raise exceptions during\ninvoice reconciliation. Administrators can now configure this functionality themselves in the\nInvoice Exception Types UI. To fully enable customer configuration:\n•\nSet Application.Invoicing.LineCreditMemoExceptions to No.\n•\nAdd all categories to\nApplication.Invoicing.LineCreditMemoExceptionLineCategories.\n•', page_no=120, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bdab23ec-f0f2-4984-8ab9-f9dee433bf94'), chunk_index=667, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374952, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Configure the desired behavior in the Invoice Exception Types UI in Ariba\nAdministrator.\nApplication.Invoicing.LineCreditMemoExceptionLineCategories (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis legacy parameter specifies which categories of line items are\nvalidated for exceptions in line-item credit memos. It's applicable if legacy\nparameter Application.Invoicing.SkipLineCreditMemoExceptions is set to No.\nAdministrators can now configure this functionality themselves in the Invoice Exception\nTypes UI. To fully enable customer configuration:\n•\nSet Application.Invoicing.SkipLineCreditMemoExceptions to No.\n•", page_no=120, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('52fd58fe-697b-4bbb-bc1a-7f16e2f5b73a'), chunk_index=668, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374955, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Add all categories to\nApplication.Invoicing.LineCreditMemoExceptionLineCategories. Valid\nvalues (not case sensitive): RegularLine, HandlingCharge, SpecialCharge,\nDiscount, FreightCharge, TaxCharge, WHTTax\n•\nConfigure the desired behavior in the Invoice Exception Types UI in Ariba\nAdministrator.\nApplication.Invoicing.UseTLCTaxEngine (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter is used to specify if you want to use the enhanced tax computation engine\nor a third-party tax calculation engine for taxes applied on invoices.\n\ue05c\xa0Note', page_no=120, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bcc55a50-f1db-4e89-9154-063dbea87cfc'), chunk_index=669, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374959, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If Application.Invoicing.CopyTaxCodesFromInvoiceToIR is set to Yes, the tax\ncode on an invoice tax line is copied to the corresponding IR tax line regardless of\nwhether the site is using the enhanced tax computation engine.\nApplication.Invoicing.RejectRequiresNoMoreApprovals (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether or not invoice reconciliation document approvers are\ndeactivated after one approver rejects the IR. When this parameter is set to Yes, IR', page_no=120, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5eb14914-bb09-4642-9db6-c1bf79148bfc'), chunk_index=670, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374963, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='documents are finally rejected when any approver used the Reject button. When this\nparameter is set to No, rejected IRs must be approved (in other words, an approver\nmust approver the rejection) before it is finally rejected, and the Cancel Reject button\nis available. The default value is Yes.\nApplication.Invoicing.DisableRereconciliationOfRelatedIRsForContract (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether or not related invoice reconciliations are automatically', page_no=120, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('32ebebb4-e5e6-4a40-9494-18c90cd45bf6'), chunk_index=671, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 374966, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='re-reconciled when contract accumulators are updated. When this parameter is set to No,\nupdates to accumulators in contracts trigger re-reconciliations of related IRs based on\nthose updated. The default value is No.\n120\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Reconciling Invoices', page_no=120, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('796b5365-f5ff-4d72-b58b-66890221b707'), chunk_index=672, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375065, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Application.Invoicing.DisableRereconciliationOfRelatedIRsForOrder (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether or not related invoice reconciliations are automatically\nre-reconciled when purchase order accumulators are updated. When this parameter is set\nto No, updates to accumulators in puchase orders trigger re-reconciliations of related IRs\nbased on those updates. The default value is No.\nApplication.Invoicing.EnableTaxesOnShippingAndHandlingItems (set by SAP Ariba Support)', page_no=121, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('320ce666-fd5f-442a-8422-61e85e710f36'), chunk_index=673, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375069, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter specifies whether or not users can add shipping and special handling lines\non invoices and specify taxes for those lines. When this parameter is set to Yes, the Add\nShipping Item and Add Special Handling Item buttons appear on the Add Items page\nwhen users are creating invoices. To add taxes to a shipping or special handling line, the', page_no=121, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bcf04231-c633-4b0e-85dd-6116b849e20a'), chunk_index=674, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375073, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='user selects Add Taxes at Line Level, which causes the Add Taxes button to appear next to\neach line. The default setting is No.\n\ue094\xa0Restriction\nTaxes cannot be added to charges at header-level.\nApplication.Procure.EnableAccountingForWithholdingTaxInInvoiceAndIR (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether users can manage accounting information for\nwithholding taxes on invoices and invoice reconciliation documents. If set to Yes, users', page_no=121, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0a3b1575-df5b-4d23-9195-932031ef5d52'), chunk_index=675, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375077, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='can perform tasks, such as configure accounting splits for withholding taxes and mass edit\ntax accounting information for withholding taxes.\nThe default value of this parameter is No.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nTo manage withholding taxes on invoices and invoice reconciliation documents, the\nApplication.Invoicing.UseTLCTaxEngine parameter must be enabled.\nApplication.Invoicing.EnableEnhancedManualMatch (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether the enhanced user interface for manual matching of', page_no=121, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c09c6839-d60a-462d-a469-9ae228a5601c'), chunk_index=676, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375081, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='invoice lines with order or contract lines is enabled.\nThe default value of this parameter is Yes.\nApplication.Invoicing.MaxInvoiceAttachmentPagesToPNG (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies the maximum number of pages of an attachment file on the\nInvoice Entry page that can be converted to PNG format when users choose to view the\nattachment. By default, this value is set to 15.\nApplication.Budget.EnableFundsManagement (set by SAP Ariba Support)', page_no=121, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('78c566ef-d51a-4c54-be67-dcf496e2f732'), chunk_index=677, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375084, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='(Applicable for sites integrated with SAP ERP) The\nApplication.Budget.EnableFundsManagement parameter specifies whether the Get\nFunds Management Details option is visible on requisitions and invoice reconciliation\ndocuments.\nWhen set to Yes, the Get Funds Management Details option is available on requisitions\nand invoice reconciliation documents. When users select this option, Funds Management\naccount assignment fields are populated with relevant accounting information fetched from\nthe external ERP system.', page_no=121, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('2c74b314-9f83-41c8-876e-b50f18d6a256'), chunk_index=678, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375088, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Reconciling Invoices\nPUBLIC\n121', page_no=121, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e25b5569-c3ee-4069-a65f-7d4e60ad987c'), chunk_index=679, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375094, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When set to No, the Get Funds Management Details option is not visible on requisitions\nand invoice reconciliation documents.\nThe default value for this parameter is No.\n122\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Reconciling Invoices', page_no=122, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a8adb675-6592-4193-aa6a-386b9f82025e'), chunk_index=680, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375158, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Self-Service Site Configuration Parameters for\nReconciling Invoices\nInclude accounting info for charge lines in IR cXML [page 123]\nInvoice exception types for accrued tax payments [page 124]\nGenerate default withholding tax at the header level [page 125]\nAlways display Reject button for IRs in Approving [page 125]\nRequire reason codes for invoice rejection [page 126]\nPrevent dispute of invoices [page 126]\nPrevent acceptance of specific invoice exceptions [page 127]', page_no=123, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('72fa2cf4-83ab-4174-a1c0-c649cf75ccfd'), chunk_index=681, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375162, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Require comments to supplier for invoice rejection [page 128]\nRequire invoice reconciliation in the ERP system [page 129]\nRemit To on invoice reconciliations is from invoice [page 129]\nEnable goods receipt-based invoice verification [page 131]\nMatch receipts to invoices without ship notices [page 131]\nAllow edits to matched quantity in receipt matching [page 132]\nDays to delay creating an IR document [page 133]', page_no=123, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('cc2549d9-4fcb-4209-ac85-5a01822e2ad2'), chunk_index=682, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375166, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Third-party tax calculation for buying and invoicing [page 134]\nEnhanced third-party tax calculation for invoicing [page 134]\nEnhanced warnings for force actions on invoices and payments [page 135]\nUse receipt unit price to validate invoice unit price [page 135]\nInclude accounting info for charge lines in IR cXML\nDetermines whether accounting information is included in tax, shipping, special handling, and discount lines in', page_no=123, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fb9782ab-f04d-44fa-a2c7-b845f70cc65a'), chunk_index=683, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375169, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='the exported cXML for invoice reconciliation (IR) documents. When set to Yes, accounting information for invoice\ncharge lines is included cXML invoice exports from sites that send IR documents to SAP Business Network.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.AccountingOnChargeLinesInIRCXML\nName\nInclude accounting info for charge lines in IR cXML\nDefault value\nNo\nThis parameter is applicable for sites that route invoice reconciliation (IR) documents to SAP Business', page_no=123, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('69ba4334-45d1-4d17-96ca-aa2a4c2f8d35'), chunk_index=684, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375173, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Network and is effective only when the Send invoice reconciliations to SAP Business Network\n(Application.Invoicing.SendIRToAN) parameter is enabled.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices\nPUBLIC\n123', page_no=123, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('39494318-0f7b-4e17-9374-0edb9380c231'), chunk_index=685, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375225, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nInvoice exception types for accrued tax payments\nLists unique names of the invoice exception types for which accrued tax payments are tracked in payment\nrequests. Applicable on sites that process payments for tax accrual, set by the parameter Process tax accrual', page_no=124, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6eb2e065-92ca-40a0-8cde-698ced05d74c'), chunk_index=686, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375230, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='payments, Application.Invoicing.ProcessPaymentsForTaxAccrual.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.TaxAccrualExceptions\nName\nInvoice exception types for accrued tax payments\nDefault value\nUnderTaxVariance,AccrualTaxVariance\nThe parameter value is a comma-separated list of strings, each of which represents the unique internal identifier of\nan invoice exception type in the site. Enter the unique name of the invoice exception types that trigger tracking of\naccrual taxes.', page_no=124, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('dd30e24c-ef8b-4229-90a8-2454396ed8be'), chunk_index=687, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375233, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='To get the unique internal identifiers of the preloaded invoice exception types, either export the invoice exception\ntypes from your site or see the Invoicing Default Data worksheet in the Reference Data Workbooks.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nProcess tax accrual payments [page 140]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\n124\nPUBLIC', page_no=124, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fddc45ee-b7c1-4ac2-9717-a181b021d282'), chunk_index=688, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375237, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices', page_no=124, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('03dd779e-919e-4124-b48b-a7ed676ff0c1'), chunk_index=689, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375308, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Generate default withholding tax at the header level\nBy default, computed withholding taxes are added at the header level of invoice reconciliation documents. If this\nparameter is set to No, withholding taxes are added at the line level instead. This parameter is applicable if the\nparameter Application.Invoicing.UseTLCTaxEngine is set to Yes.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.DefaultWithholdingTaxOnIRHeader\nName\nGenerate default withholding tax at the header level\nDefault value\nNo', page_no=125, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('b9fc8a6e-f367-42a7-9d70-f1572e62629f'), chunk_index=690, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375312, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The parameter Application.Invoicing.UseTLCTaxEngine, which SAP Ariba sets for you, specifies whether\nto use the enhanced tax computation engine or a third-party tax calculation engine for taxes applied on invoices. To\nchange the setting, have your Designated Support Contact (DSC) submit a Service Request (SR).\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration', page_no=125, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ce3bba72-ceb5-4101-9117-8f2549581e36'), chunk_index=691, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375316, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Parameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nAlways display Reject button for IRs in Approving\nSpecifies whether the Reject button on invoice reconciliation documents is available to all users or only to invoice\nexception handlers and members of the Invoice Manager group. This parameter affects the Exceptions tab of\ninvoice reconciliation documents in Approving status.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.AlwaysDisplayRejectButtonForIRsInApproving\nName\nAlways display Reject button for IRs in Approving\nDefault value\nNo', page_no=125, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6fd5aaa2-64d5-42ee-b888-50119a480edb'), chunk_index=692, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375319, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Possible values for this parameter are Yes and No.\n•\nWhen set to Yes, the Reject button on invoice reconciliation documents is available to all users.\n•\nWhen set to No, the Reject button is only available for exception handlers and members of the Invoice\nManager group.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide', page_no=125, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3a308e93-0713-497e-aab9-5fa472fa74b2'), chunk_index=693, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375323, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Self-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices\nPUBLIC\n125', page_no=125, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('be2645ee-fd63-4b0a-8d2e-ec7fd2a3fbbd'), chunk_index=694, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375374, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Related Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nRequire reason codes for invoice rejection\nSpecifies whether users must select one or more reason codes from a list of custom-defined options when\nrejecting an invoice during invoice reconciliation. The rejection reason is visible to suppliers.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.UseInvoiceRejectionReasonCodes\nName\nRequire reason codes for invoice rejection\nDefault value\nNo', page_no=126, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d4029ace-4932-4d2f-a216-31d6f6c0d9d5'), chunk_index=695, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375379, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='For information about configuring rejection reason codes for invoices, see Rejection Reason Codes for Invoices.\nIf you configure rejection reason codes for invoices, you might want to make comments to suppliers\noptional. To do so, set the following parameter to No: Require comments to supplier for invoice rejection,\nApplication.Invoicing.SupplierRejectionCommentsRequired.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information', page_no=126, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e603cb9c-7f1e-4ef7-8d6e-32ebc25d1a33'), chunk_index=696, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375382, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Require comments to supplier for invoice rejection [page 128]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nPrevent dispute of invoices\nDetermines whether to hide the Accept Expected option on the Action menu of invoice reconciliation documents.\nIf the option is hidden, invoice exception handlers can't dispute invoices. They must either accept the information\non the invoice or reject the entire invoice.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.DisallowDispute\nName", page_no=126, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ac9a810c-c6ba-4dd1-8cd6-4f111b43f5c7'), chunk_index=697, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375386, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Prevent dispute of invoices\nDefault value\nNo\n126\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices', page_no=126, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3c6c37c7-e5f8-48cb-8a21-4da32d2cdd9f'), chunk_index=698, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375494, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The Accept Expected action indicates that the approver does not agree to pay the amount specified on the invoice.\nInstead, the approver agrees to pay ("accepts") the amount specified on the associated reference document, such\nas the purchase order, contract, or receipt, or the amount calculated by the tax calculation engine.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nThis parameter is provided for European sites. European regulations require that invoices be rejected entirely or', page_no=127, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('35814a27-f5df-4c4b-9839-cabb8cdf40a7'), chunk_index=699, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375499, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='paid in full. The Accept Expected action allows "short pay" on invoices, which violates this regulation.\nPossible values for this parameter are Yes and No.\n•\nWhen this parameter is set to No, invoice exception handlers can dispute the information on invoices by\nchoosing the Accept Expected action when resolving an exception.\n•', page_no=127, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4dc434c7-fead-4c41-a013-0b987fbe43c5'), chunk_index=700, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375503, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="When this parameter is set to Yes, the Action menu for invoice exceptions doesn't include an Accept Expected\noption.\n•\nTo prevent dispute for an individual exception type, set this parameter to No, and set the Prevent Invoice\nDispute option for the exception type in Ariba Administrator.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information", page_no=127, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bc230d92-ba04-407f-8c39-4fc89479b46e'), chunk_index=701, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375506, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Prevent acceptance of specific invoice exceptions [page 127]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nPrevent acceptance of specific invoice exceptions\nPrevents users from accepting specific types of invoice exceptions by hiding the Accept Invoice actions for those\nexceptions. Enter the unique names of exception types.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.DisallowAcceptOnExceptionTypes\nName\nPrevent acceptance of specific invoice exceptions\nDefault value\nEmpty list', page_no=127, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bfa06aa4-34bf-4db6-a7c1-8b96328285ab'), chunk_index=702, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375510, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter removes the Accept Invoice option from the Action menu in the invoice reconciliation user\ninterface for the invoice exception types you specify. By removing the option to accept the information provided by\nsuppliers on their invoices for specific invoice exceptions, you can enforce that you only pay for what was ordered.', page_no=127, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('32a71995-d19b-45e4-9330-84b011a1d19a'), chunk_index=703, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375514, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The parameter value is a comma-separated list of strings, each of which represents the unique internal identifier of\nan invoice exception type in the site. Enter the unique name of the invoice exception types for which to remove the\nAccept Invoice option. For example: POPriceVariance.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nCertain countries/regions require that invoices are paid in full or rejected if there are possible invoice errors.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide', page_no=127, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('456bea95-9f57-41fd-aa25-3f04f922d74b'), chunk_index=704, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375518, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Self-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices\nPUBLIC\n127', page_no=127, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('07822536-246f-4338-8fdf-c5c0b68b49d1'), chunk_index=705, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375606, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='To get the unique internal identifiers of the preloaded invoice exception types, either export the invoice exception\ntypes from your site or see the Invoicing Default Data worksheet in the Reference Data Workbooks.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nPrevent dispute of invoices [page 126]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager', page_no=128, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('530f3459-6b4c-491a-8510-2b9be17f880e'), chunk_index=706, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375610, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Require comments to supplier for invoice rejection\nSpecifies whether an approver must add comments to the supplier when rejecting an invoice reconciliation\ndocument.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.SupplierRejectionCommentsRequired\nName\nRequire comments to supplier for invoice rejection\nDefault value\nNo\nWhen set to Yes, the approver must enter comments that are visible to the supplier. Comments can be entered', page_no=128, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6011e1d3-4852-4509-b10d-c5f31d6a0543'), chunk_index=707, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375614, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='in the Comments field in the user interface or, in sites enabled for email approvals, in the space provided in the\nmessage body of an email notification.\nIf you configure rejection reason codes for invoices, you might want to make comments to suppliers optional.\nThe following points pertain to comments submitted through email approval:\n•', page_no=128, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('586c6561-ce40-4243-9462-328c3a551f77'), chunk_index=708, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375618, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If the parameter is set to Yes, and a user has opted to receive email notifications in compact text format, when\nthe user enters a comment while rejecting the IR in email, those comments are treated as comments to the\nsupplier and meet the requirement.\n•\nIf the parameter is set to No, and a user has opted to receive email notifications in compact text format, when', page_no=128, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ce30a88c-f697-4a11-ad47-a1bd491ead02'), chunk_index=709, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375622, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='the user enters a comment while rejecting the IR in email, those comments are treated as internal.\n•\nIf the parameter is set to Yes and a user has not opted to receive email notifications in compact text format, the\nuser must enter a comment in the Comments to Supplier field to meet the requirement.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager', page_no=128, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d6e96442-c9c5-4e53-b668-3b984fa938c7'), chunk_index=710, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375626, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='workspace.\nRelated Information\nRequire reason codes for invoice rejection [page 126]\n128\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices', page_no=128, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('eaa621a3-e2a3-4e5b-ae05-260414c93267'), chunk_index=711, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375693, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Intelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nRequire invoice reconciliation in the ERP system\nSpecifies whether invoices require a final reconciliation step in your ERP system before they can progress to Paying\nstatus. This parameter applies to SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.ExternalReconciliationEnabled\nName\nRequire invoice reconciliation in the ERP system\nDefault value\nYes', page_no=129, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1cf58228-842f-43c9-b189-71febd216d5a'), chunk_index=712, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375697, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='When set to Yes, and an invoice reconciliation document is finally approved, the status changes to Awaiting\nExternal Reconciliation instead of Paying.\nWhen set to No, and an invoice reconciliation document is finally approved, the status changes to Paying.\nIf your invoices require reconciliation in the ERP system, you must enable Send invoice reconciliations to SAP\nBusiness Network (Application.Invoicing.SendIRtoAN) parameter.', page_no=129, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('298e2808-eda6-4996-b2b5-af2c950eb9c0'), chunk_index=713, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375701, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nRemit To on invoice reconciliations is from invoice\nDetermines whether the default Remit To address on invoice reconciliation (IR) documents is the\nRemit To address on the invoice or the first Remit To address found for the supplier. This', page_no=129, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('205126b4-83dc-4787-9375-facadcb8ae59'), chunk_index=714, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375705, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='parameter applies to sites that process supplier bank details in invoices during invoice reconciliation\n(Application.Invoicing.SupportSupplierBankInfoOnInvoices is set to Yes).\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.RemittanceLocationUsingRemitToId\nName\nRemit To on invoice reconciliations is from invoice\nDefault value\nNo\nThis parameter applies to cXML invoices transmitted between SAP Business Network and the SAP Ariba invoicing\nsolution, as with SAP Ariba Invoice Management sites and merged sites that include both SAP Ariba Buying and', page_no=129, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c22e25e7-0646-42e7-a13a-5de47c2373c4'), chunk_index=715, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375709, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices\nPUBLIC\n129', page_no=129, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('230020d6-b406-4631-b8f1-2252532f622c'), chunk_index=716, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375802, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="In sites that process bank details in invoices, if the invoice doesn't have a payment method specified, and\nthere are multiple Remit To addresses configured for the supplier location, the parameter Remit To on invoice\nreconciliations is from invoice works as follows:\n•\nIf set to Yes, IR documents use the Remit To address on the invoice.\n•", page_no=130, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4706f4b1-cd4c-46f9-9060-a32f396acb83'), chunk_index=717, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375806, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='If set to No, IR documents use the first remittance address of the supplier location.\nYour site uses the following bank information to find the right Remit To address, adding only the IDs or numbers\nand omitting fields such as account type and branch name: ABA routing number, Swift ID, iBan ID, account ID.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.', page_no=130, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('925b80a2-ddaf-455d-889e-3cb4a9b8e24c'), chunk_index=718, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375810, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Related Parameter\nApplication.Invoicing.SupportSupplierBankInfoOnInvoices (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nDetermines whether the SAP Ariba solution processes the supplier bank details in cXML\ninvoices (in the payment method extrinsic) and whether the supplier bank details in cXML\ninvoices from SAP Business Network are used on invoice reconciliation (IR) documents.\nSetting this parameter to Yes helps the SAP Ariba solution find the correct remittance\nlocation.', page_no=130, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fb2b73ac-f348-45b4-8a56-ed5850c47950'), chunk_index=719, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375814, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Suppliers might send updated bank details in cXML invoices over SAP Business Network.\nThis parameter applies to cXML invoices transmitted between SAP Business Network\nand the SAP Ariba invoicing solution. It's most likely to pertain to SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement sites and merged sites that include both SAP Ariba Invoice Management and\nSAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing.", page_no=130, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7a3c936c-7581-437b-a65a-d0a68dabb5dd'), chunk_index=720, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375818, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="If this parameter is set to No, the SAP Ariba solution doesn't process updated bank\ndetails in invoices sent by suppliers. Supplier-specified bank details are not included in\nthe reconciled invoices sent to SAP Business Network for payment processing.\nIf this parameter is set to Yes, the following bank details can be received and processed\nduring the invoice reconciliation process and are included in the reconciled invoices sent to", page_no=130, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9b517297-7dee-4265-85e2-f387f901b0c1'), chunk_index=721, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375822, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Business Network:\n•\nBank ID Type\n•\nBank ID\n•\nBank Account ID\n•\nBank Account Type\n•\nIBAN\n•\nBranch Name\n•\nAccount Name\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\n130\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices', page_no=130, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6dbb2af5-2c5e-446b-ad67-b9a540602450'), chunk_index=722, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375901, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Parameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nEnable goods receipt-based invoice verification\nSpecifies whether goods receipt-based invoice verification is enabled. If set to Yes, for order lines that require\nreceipt-based invoice verification, invoice quantities and prices are reconciled against receipts.\nID\nApplication.Procure.EnableGRBasedInvoice\nName\nEnable goods receipt-based invoice verification\nDefault value\nNo\nWhen this parameter is enabled, the parameter Application.Procure.EnablePriceDateControl (Use', page_no=131, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('c2e0b359-6a7e-4112-aaa3-3ba26971aa0a'), chunk_index=723, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375905, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='receipt unit price to validate invoice unit price) must also be set to Yes to ensure that the invoicing solution\nverifies the prices for line items on invoices based on the prices specified for the items on the associated receipts.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nGoods Receipt-Based Invoice Verification [page 74]', page_no=131, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('61c7d725-686f-4653-a0d1-452626a01368'), chunk_index=724, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375909, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Match receipts to invoices without ship notices [page 131]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nAllow edits to matched quantity in receipt matching [page 132]\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nMatch receipts to invoices without ship notices\nOn sites enabled for goods receipt-based invoice verification, determines whether invoices must include ship notice\nIDs in order to be matched to receipts automatically.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.MatchReceiptToInvoiceWithoutShipNotice\nName\nMatch receipts to invoices without ship notices', page_no=131, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5baaa370-4e3a-43f3-90b2-2229de980ace'), chunk_index=725, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375913, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Default value\nNo\nPossible values for this parameter are Yes and No.\n•\nWhen set to Yes:\n•\nInvoices without ship notice IDs are matched to goods receipts based on purchase order.\n•\nInvoices with ship notice IDs are matched to goods receipts that have the same ship notice ID as the\ninvoice.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices\nPUBLIC\n131', page_no=131, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9dfaa46b-1e72-49f8-8797-964b1f766b7b'), chunk_index=726, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375981, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\nWhen set to No, automatic matching of invoices to receipts is based solely on ship notice ID. Invoices without a\nship notice ID are not matched to receipts.\nThis parameter is applicable if the following parameter is set to Yes: Enable goods receipt-based invoice\nverification, Application.Procure.EnableGRBasedInvoice.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information', page_no=132, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('64bd0be2-f5ce-46f4-984b-4b71153e6265'), chunk_index=727, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375985, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Enable goods receipt-based invoice verification [page 131]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nAllow edits to matched quantity in receipt matching\nDetermines if users can edit the matched quantity when manually matching receipts to invoice lines.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.AllowMatchedReceiptQuantityEdit\nName\nAllow edits to matched quantity in receipt matching\nDefault value\nNo\nSome accounts payable departments need the ability to choose specific quantities from multiple receipts when', page_no=132, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d30b4867-5835-4085-a5bf-94a8e42efd42'), chunk_index=728, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375989, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='matching receipts to invoice lines. When this parameter is set to Yes, the system determines the default matched\nquantity, but users can change the value.\nThe values entered for matched quantity are validated as follows. If the user tries to submit invalid changes, an\nerror message appears.\n•\nThe total matched quantity for all matched receipts must be less than or equal to the invoice quantity.', page_no=132, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('908d0cf8-b15e-4cbb-81fe-ba13cf2b5616'), chunk_index=729, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375993, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="If the total matched quantity is less than the invoice quantity, there's an informational warning, but the user\ncan still proceed.\n•\nThe matched quantity for a receipt must be 0 or more.\n•\nThe matched quantity for a receipt must not exceed the receipt's available quantity.\nWhen this parameter is set to No, the system determines the matched quantity, and users can't change the value.\n132\nPUBLIC", page_no=132, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bb8f0728-206a-41ed-803b-04b2c1237e2f'), chunk_index=730, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 375997, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Invoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices', page_no=132, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fa7f64c6-0db2-4dcd-9ab7-c8d0b7b2c76d'), chunk_index=731, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376053, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nMatch receipts to invoices without ship notices [page 131]\nEnable goods receipt-based invoice verification [page 131]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nDays to delay creating an IR document\nIn sites enabled for goods receipt-based invoice verification, specifies the number of days to delay the creation of', page_no=133, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('40a33c1d-116f-4a01-a5c5-f35b81cf4dbe'), chunk_index=732, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376057, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="the invoice reconciliation (IR) document after an invoice has been approved if the supporting documents haven't\narrived yet. Set this parameter to prevent premature invoice exceptions due to missing receipts.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.DaysToDelayIRCreatio\nn\nName\nDays to delay creating an IR document\nDefault value\n0\nWhen a goods receipt-based invoice is approved in the SAP Ariba solution, and receipts are still outstanding,", page_no=133, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('32885cc7-6571-4f1f-bbec-eb9a98fb160b'), chunk_index=733, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376061, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='the invoice remains in Awaiting Receipts status during the delay period. The invoice reconciliation document is\ncreated within 6 hours after the specified number of days has elapsed.\nMembers of the Invoice Administrator group can manually start the reconciliation process during the delay period.\nThis parameter is applicable if the following parameter is set to Yes: Enable goods receipt-based invoice\nverification, Application.Procure.EnableGRBasedInvoice.', page_no=133, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('eeae7159-fde0-4dac-a1b2-ed8e7477debf'), chunk_index=734, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376064, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nEnable goods receipt-based invoice verification [page 131]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices\nPUBLIC\n133', page_no=133, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6b4c8716-a8c8-4fc0-b3ed-48eecf332f95'), chunk_index=735, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376124, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Third-party tax calculation for buying and invoicing\nSpecifies if your site is integrated with a third-party tax calculation engine to calculate taxes for approvable\ndocuments such as requisitions and invoice reconciliations. If set to Yes, taxes are calculated when tax\nmanagers initiate tax calculation for the documents or when users submit the documents for approval. If', page_no=134, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fb8e6730-e102-4666-af0c-5064cc8b307e'), chunk_index=736, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376128, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='set to Yes, you can set another parameter to turn on enhanced third-party tax calculation for invoicing,\nApplication.Procure.EnhancedTaxCalculationInExternalSystems.\nID\nApplication.Procure.EnableTaxCalculationInExternalSystems\nName\nThird-party tax calculation for buying and invoicing\nDefault value\nNo\nIf you set this parameter to Yes, we recommend that the parameter\nApplication.Procure.EnableTaxesChargesAndDiscount be set to Yes to ensure that taxes\nfor requisitions are calculated in the third-party tax calculation engine. SAP Ariba sets\nApplication.Procure.EnableTaxesChargesAndDiscount for you.', page_no=134, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bc6ba3f4-cc9b-4566-8da0-14f784c57e36'), chunk_index=737, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376131, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nEnhanced third-party tax calculation for invoicing [page 134]\nThird-Party Tax Calculation Overview\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nEnhanced third-party tax calculation for invoicing\nOn sites integrated with a third-party tax calculation engine, specifies if tax calculation includes enhanced tax', page_no=134, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('36466654-bc09-425a-975c-a584b157f693'), chunk_index=738, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376135, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='information for reconciliation and payment processes. Enhancements include improved handling of summary and\ngranular tax details, buyer-payable taxes, and accrual taxes. Applicable if Third-party tax calculation for buying\nand invoicing (Application.Procure.EnableTaxCalculationInExternalSystems) is set to Yes.\nID\nApplication.Procure.EnhancedTaxCalculationInExternalSystems\nName\nEnhanced third-party tax calculation for invoicing\nDefault value\nNo\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\n134\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide', page_no=134, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5d52d754-86fc-430b-8d19-f6c4df229a76'), chunk_index=739, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376139, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Self-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices', page_no=134, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('bf2d6402-a111-4053-ba93-76f6c964ad99'), chunk_index=740, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376191, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Related Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nThird-party tax calculation for buying and invoicing [page 134]\nThird-Party Tax Calculation Overview\nEnhanced Third-Party Tax Calculation for Invoices\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nEnhanced warnings for force actions on invoices and\npayments\nDetermines whether to show enhanced warnings when users force an invoice or payment document to the next', page_no=135, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('445204e9-b03f-43c9-8185-8cf30b13bddb'), chunk_index=741, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376194, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="status. Enhanced warnings explain that the force action doesn't send the document to any other system, such as\nSAP Business Network or the ERP system. It only changes the document status.\nID\nApplication.Approvable.EnableEnhancedWarningsForForceInvoiceAndPaymentAc\ntions\nName\nEnhanced warnings for force actions on invoices and payments\nDefault value\nYes\nThis parameter applies to the following actions: Force Reconcile on invoices, Force Pay and Force Reject", page_no=135, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('18e5da1b-c741-4160-a7b6-d82eb8330e5f'), chunk_index=742, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376198, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='on invoice reconciliations, Force Send on payment requests, and Force Pay and Force Cancel on payment\ntransactions and advance payments.\nIf this parameter is set to Yes, the enhanced warnings are displayed.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nUse receipt unit price to validate invoice unit price', page_no=135, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('515e8f36-67b8-40e8-99e3-7d86f8b71133'), chunk_index=743, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376202, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Determines whether the SAP Ariba solution uses the unit price on the receipt for price verification on invoices.\nID\nApplication.Procure.EnablePriceDateControl\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices\nPUBLIC\n135', page_no=135, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9610f64b-4041-448b-9c00-66fc13f9464f'), chunk_index=744, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376239, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Name\nUse receipt unit price to validate invoice unit price\nDefault value\nNo\nWhen this parameter is set to Yes, for invoice items that reference an order item marked as Ship Notice Required,\nthe SAP Ariba solution compares the price on the invoice with the price on the receipt, not the order. For sites that\nuse goods receipt-based invoice verification, the recommended setting is Yes.', page_no=136, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('ef88402a-c80c-4700-ad58-0e3f06899896'), chunk_index=745, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376243, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='To enable goods receipt-based invoice verification, you must also set the parameter Enable goods receipt-based\ninvoice verification (Application.Procure.EnableGRBasedInvoice) to Yes.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nEnable goods receipt-based invoice verification [page 131]\nIntelligent Configuration Manager Administration\nReceipt Dispute for Variance Exceptions\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\n136\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide', page_no=136, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('6311bcc3-2f56-40ba-b02b-ac4b0dc1be73'), chunk_index=746, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376247, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Self-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Reconciling Invoices', page_no=136, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('feabceca-9cac-4258-ac79-942ff2550739'), chunk_index=747, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376341, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Managing\nPayment Documents\nSome of the functionality for managing payment documents is controlled by configuration options that SAP\nAriba Support sets for you. These parameters apply to SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and SAP Ariba Invoice\nManagement.\nApplication.Invoicing.ShowInvoiceAndPaymentsToRequisitionCreator (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether or not requisition requesters and preparers can view', page_no=137, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('3662eb1b-4cb4-4647-a3e9-27c4426b2a86'), chunk_index=748, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376345, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="related invoices and payments on the requisition's Summary tab. When this parameter is\nset to Yes, requisition requesters and preparers can click the order number link for each\nrequisition line item, and then click the Invoice and Payment tabs on the order to view\nrelated invoices and payments. The default setting is No.\nApplication.Invoicing.ShowPaymentsToInvoiceCreator (set by SAP Ariba Support)", page_no=137, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f390e332-3b36-4981-a022-f154d57fea1e'), chunk_index=749, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376348, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter specifies whether or not invoice requesters and preparers can view related\npayments. When this parameter is set to Yes, invoice requesters and preparers can view\nrelated payments on the Payment tabs of the Order and Invoice pages. The default setting\nis No.\nApplication.Settlement.DynamicDiscountsEnabled (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether or not the discounting capability is enabled in a site.', page_no=137, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('16753f44-0edf-4c6f-aa4d-cb42b5c9b8b1'), chunk_index=750, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376352, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Discounting capabilities enable buyers to pay suppliers early in exchange for discounts. The\ndefault value is No.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nThis parameter only affects suppliers that send payment requests through SAP\nBusiness Network. Suppliers that use the External System payment model can use\ndynamic discounting if discount management is enabled for them in the buyer's SAP\nBusiness Network account, regardless of the setting for this parameter.\nApplication.Settlement.LocalPaymentModelSupported", page_no=137, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0e23cfa0-47f4-4893-ad2d-df9af1c46c1a'), chunk_index=751, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376356, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="This parameter determines whether the local payment model is supported. A local payment\nmodel sends the reconciled invoice to SAP Business Network to be processed, not to the\nbuyer's external ERP system.\nWhen this parameter is set to Yes, the Pay Via dropdown in searches for invoice\nreconciliation documents includes the value Local. (Pay Via means payment model.) Also,", page_no=137, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('f28070a6-5651-4545-938e-bff15120a1d0'), chunk_index=752, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376360, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="if a payment doesn't include a supplier or supplier location, then Pay Via is set to Local in\nthat payment.\nIf a supplier location for the payment is configured with a local payment model, this\nparameter has no effect. The reconciled invoice is sent to SAP Business Network for\nprocessing.\nThe default value of this parameter No.\nApplication.Settlement.PaymentDiscountSelectionPolicy (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide", page_no=137, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('74073a51-6b4f-4a9c-b399-6d3422ead576'), chunk_index=753, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376364, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='SAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Managing Payment Documents\nPUBLIC\n137', page_no=137, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7a43e6bf-78f7-4828-8e3e-8752df3fff9a'), chunk_index=754, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376469, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter specifies one of a set of predefined discount policies for payments. The\nvalue must be one of the following keys:\n•\nTakeDiscountNone, which selects the payment schedule corresponding to the net\nterm, with no discounts applied.\n•\nTakeDiscountMaximum, which selects the payment schedule that offers the largest\ndiscount.\n•\nTakeDiscountApplicable, which selects a payment schedule based on the', page_no=138, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a13a8ff2-3ab0-4842-9a2d-47ba0a6f31c1'), chunk_index=755, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376473, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='transaction date, using the best discount that is available for the given transaction\ndate.\nThe default value is TakeDiscountMaximum.\nApplication.Settlement.PaymentTermsLineTypeCategories (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter defines which line types are to be considered when evaluating payment\ndiscounts. For example, you might choose to exclude tax items or shipping charges when\ncalculating payment discounts. The value is a comma-separated list of integers, where each', page_no=138, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('211c89ce-c79a-4f61-b7c2-b0f1416ff4eb'), chunk_index=756, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376477, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='integer represents a standard line category. The default value is 1. Valid integer values are:\n•\n1 - Procurement line items\n•\n2 - Tax charges\n•\n4 - Freight charges\n•\n8 - Handling charges\n•\n16 - Special charges\n•\n32 - Discounts\nApplication.Settlement.PaymentModel (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies the preferred payment model for the site. For new sites, the', page_no=138, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('4e9d4d41-6f5e-49dc-97e2-3fa3d7b45b40'), chunk_index=757, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376481, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='External Pay payment model is the only supported option. In the default configuration,\nthis parameter is set to ExternalPay. There is no default value.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nThe payment model specified with the AribaPay setting is deprecated and will be\nde-supported in a future release; it is only available in older implementations of SAP\nAriba Invoice Management and SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing.', page_no=138, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('e67a2923-04da-456f-845f-68f1141c713c'), chunk_index=758, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376485, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Payment models can also be associated with specific suppliers (in\nthe SupplierSupplement.csv file) and supplier locations (in the\nSupplierLocationSupplement.csv file).\nApplication.Settlement.PaymentRequestSendMethodOption (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies a method for sending payment requests, which in turn defines\nwhether or not the status of invoice reconciliation and payment request documents in your\ninvoicing solution depends on the success or failure of invoices in integrated ERP systems.', page_no=138, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9ec04f01-af83-420c-9343-2647016510d9'), chunk_index=759, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376488, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='The following values are valid settings for this parameter:\n•\nDefault: the default value for the parameter. In this case, the status of the invoice\nreconciliation and payment request in your invoicing solution does not change based on\nthe success or failure of the invoice in the ERP system. You must use this setting if you\nexport payment requests using SAP Integration Suite, managed gateway (formerly SAP', page_no=138, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('1d1eef56-9fb7-4158-bb5d-4eb4150db45a'), chunk_index=760, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376492, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Ariba Cloud Integration Gateway).\n138\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Managing Payment Documents', page_no=138, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0aff34f5-a55e-4763-9d16-2a3e0a93daef'), chunk_index=761, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376598, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='•\nAsynchronous Push: the recommended setting for sites that use file-based\nintegration between SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and the ERP system. In this case,\nthe status of the invoice reconciliation and payment request in SAP Ariba Buying and\nInvoicing changes based on the success or failure of the invoice in the ERP system. This\nvalue is not applicable to SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\n•', page_no=139, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('d1cb3321-2c31-413e-9e97-57be9e7791d1'), chunk_index=762, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376603, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='DirectPush: the recommended setting for sites that use web services-based\nintegration between SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing and the ERP system. In this case,\nthe status of the invoice reconciliation and payment request in SAP Ariba Buying and\nInvoicing changes based on the success or failure of the invoice in the ERP system. This\nvalue is not applicable to SAP Ariba Invoice Management.\nApplication.Settlement.EnableAdvancePayment (set by SAP Ariba Support)', page_no=139, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a57c9f29-3598-4d70-844a-d02d70b1f769'), chunk_index=763, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376606, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter enables or disables the functionality to create advance payments. By\ndefault, this parameter is disabled. For SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing, also enable the\nenhanced invoicing user interface to adjust advance payments against invoices.\nApplication.Settlement.EnableAdvancePaymentForCopyOrders (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nThis parameter specifies whether users can create advance payments for copy orders.\nThe default value of this parameter is No.\nApplication.Settlement.TransactionPush.AdvancePayment.Enabled (set by SAP Ariba Support)', page_no=139, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9769b963-e40c-4b7f-aeab-f220a294e40e'), chunk_index=764, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376610, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter specifies whether the site should push advance payment documents to a\npending queue for export. Advance payments documents are exported to a CSV file only\nif this parameter is enabled. This parameter does not affect the web services export of\nadvance payments.\nBy default, this parameter is enabled.\nApplication.Settlement.TransactionPush.AdvancePayment.Statuses (set by SAP Ariba Support)', page_no=139, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('fcce8f0c-4156-4cba-9598-05d9795fcb8d'), chunk_index=765, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376614, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='This parameter enables you to specify a list of status strings that, upon status change,\nwill cause an advance payment to be queued for export. For example, if the value of this\nparameter is set to Submitted, Approved, Canceling, an advance payment document will get\nqueued for export when its status changes to Submitted, Approved, or Canceling.\nThe default value of this parameter is Approved and Canceling.', page_no=139, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('da073b61-4312-4498-8258-4ac52cbfa9ed'), chunk_index=766, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376618, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Application.Invoicing.AllowExportingTaxSplitAccountings (set by SAP Ariba Support)\nIn SAP variants, specifies whether tax line split accounting is included in exported\npayment requests. When set to Yes, split accounting information for all tax lines in the\ninvoice reconciliation document is included. This parameter applies to the following export\ntasks: Export Payment Requests, Export Payment Requests with Advance Payments,\nExport Payment Requests Asynchronously, Export Payment Requests with Receipts', page_no=139, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('7a529a76-9833-4b1e-8143-11ac8429d99a'), chunk_index=767, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376621, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Asynchronously. It’s also applicable to sites using SAP Integration Suite, managed gateway\nfor spend management and SAP Business Network.\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSAP Ariba-Controlled Parameters for Managing Payment Documents\nPUBLIC\n139', page_no=139, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0408cf7a-472c-4617-b3ca-a005d075991d'), chunk_index=768, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376675, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Self-Service Site Configuration Parameters for\nManaging Payment Documents\nProcess tax accrual payments [page 140]\nERP errors that trigger auto-resend of documents [page 140]\nProcess tax accrual payments\nWhen set to Yes, tax difference is accrued for invoice exceptions listed in the parameter Invoice exception types\nfor accrued tax payments (Application.Invoicing.TaxAccrualExceptions) if the computed tax amount', page_no=140, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('8b86512f-9e99-4be2-a251-a35056d20511'), chunk_index=769, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376679, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='is more than invoice tax, and the invoice exception handler disputes the invoice tax amount by accepting the\nexpected tax amount. Payment request documents contain accrual tax amounts.\nID\nApplication.Invoicing.ProcessPaymentsForTaxAccrual\nName\nProcess tax accrual payments\nDefault value\nYes\nWhen set to No, tax difference is not accrued.\nA member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration', page_no=140, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('0e163493-d78e-4c31-9aa7-0938c1b4b41a'), chunk_index=770, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376683, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Parameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nERP errors that trigger auto-resend of documents\nLists the ERP errors for which you want the SAP Ariba solution to try resending documents automatically. For\nexample, if sending a payment to the ERP system causes ERP error 123, and error 123 is in this list, the payment is\nautomatically resent. Add the errors using IDs from the ErrorNumber or ErrorCode element of the WSDL.', page_no=140, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('a2db6e04-75d0-4e45-80a7-caa6e8ebad6d'), chunk_index=771, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376687, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='ID\nApplication.Invoicing.ERPErrorsThatTriggerAutoResend\nName\nERP errors that trigger auto-resend of documents\n140\nPUBLIC\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Managing Payment Documents', page_no=140, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('9ed8f74c-da67-4e46-b30a-8aa73c942ab5'), chunk_index=772, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376732, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Default value\nEmpty list\nTypically, this parameter is used for errors that are quickly resolved in the ERP system, such as temporary push\nerrors. When the ERP system sends an error that's in this list, SAP Ariba Buying and Invoicing tries resending the\npayment request for up to 5 tries.\nPayment requests that currently have an error are listed on a Failed Payments tab of the Payments page (under\nManage", page_no=141, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5bd9d730-dc9f-418e-a92f-c69a54cdf809'), chunk_index=773, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376736, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text="Payments\n). To see the error code, open the payment request and check the ERP Error Code field.\nFor SAP variants, the errors are identified in the WSDL by ErrorNumber. For other ERP systems, the errors are\nidentified by ErrorCode.\n\ue05c\xa0Note\nThis feature uses web services to transfer information to and from the ERP system. This feature doesn't\nsupport the OK-to-pay file.", page_no=141, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('abfa3005-0246-4188-899e-f9961733db0a'), chunk_index=774, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376740, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='A member of the Customer Administrator group sets this parameter in the Intelligent Configuration Manager\nworkspace.\nRelated Information\nIntelligent Configuration Manager administration\nParameter Management in Intelligent Configuration Manager\nInvoicing and Payment Process Guide\nSelf-Service Site Configuration Parameters for Managing Payment Documents\nPUBLIC\n141', page_no=141, section=None, title=None), DocumentChunk(chunk_id=UUID('5f72bc4b-2061-49ab-b645-b2c265b0ab46'), chunk_index=775, chunking_version=1, document_id=UUID('d1090e27-f0b5-4d35-981b-60e944035eab'), document_group_id=UUID('8312be5e-84ce-46d3-ac0e-83f061f850bc'), is_active=True, created_at=datetime.datetime(2026, 8, 27, 18, 34, 24, 376860, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc), text='Important Disclaimers and Legal Information\nHyperlinks\nSome links are classified by an icon and/or a mouseover text. These links provide additional information.\nAbout the icons:\n•\nLinks with the icon\n: You are